// 写作 · 真题版（往年四级写作真题原题）
// 题数：89 道（2013年6月–2026年6月全部已核实者），按主题分：教育 16、科技 11、环境 1、健康 3、社会现象 13、文化 9、校园生活 23、职业规划 6、其他 7。
// 数据来源：英语四级学习页 artifact（ying-yu-si-ji-xue-xi）的 exportWritingReal 动作一次返回全部 89 道，原样返回。
// 内容未改写：每道带主题、年份、月份、套数、题面（Directions 原文，含中文提示和图片说明的文字描述）、参考范文（120–180 词，明确标注非官方范文）、逐句解析（好词/好句/好结构标注）。
// 注意：各出版社对第1/2/3套的编号不完全一致，同一场次的三道题以题面为准；2025年6月第1套题面里的“seeking”是按原文（Guojiya 写作“seeing”疑为笔误，调研报告已注明）；2021年6月三道标题作文的参考说法放在题面第二行“题目给出的参考说法：……”。
// 格式：window.ENG_WRITING_REAL = [{ id, kind, themeId, themeName, type, title, prompt, essay: [段落], analysis: [{en, note, tag}], wordRequirement, suggestedMinutes, source, year, month, set }]
window.ENG_WRITING_REAL = [{"analysis":[{"en":"The picture shows a teacher talking with a student about a literature book.","note":"图画作文第一句先客观描述画面：谁、在做什么，一句说清。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The teacher suggests that the student think of the book as a long text-message, so that reading it will not feel so hard.","note":"think of…as…（把……看作……）正是图中老师的说法；so that 引出目的。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The picture is humorous, but it points to a real problem: many young people today find literature too long and too difficult to read.","note":"描述完画面立刻转到现实问题，冒号展开——图画作文的标准过渡。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"However, reading literature is of great importance.","note":"短句亮明观点，of great importance 替换 very important。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, literature is a window on other lives and other times.","note":"window 比喻：文学是看别人生活和别的时代的窗口。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Through novels and poems, we can experience joys and sorrows that our own life may never offer.","note":"joys and sorrows（悲欢）对举；that 从句点出文学能给我们自己经历不到的人生。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Second, literature improves our language.","note":"First / Second 分层，结构清楚。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The beautiful sentences we meet in books slowly shape the way we write and speak.","note":"shape（塑造）用得准：好句子潜移默化地塑造我们的表达。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Most importantly, literature teaches us to think and to feel deeply, which short messages can never do.","note":"which 从句把文学和短信对比，呼应图中的 text-message。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, a literature book is far more than a long message.","note":"结尾回扣图片：far more than（远不止）一句点题。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"If we are willing to slow down and read it patiently, it will reward us with wisdom and beauty that last a lifetime.","note":"reward us with…（以……回报我们）+ last a lifetime（一生受用），收尾有余味。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["The picture shows a teacher talking with a student about a literature book. The teacher suggests that the student think of the book as a long text-message, so that reading it will not feel so hard. The picture is humorous, but it points to a real problem: many young people today find literature too long and too difficult to read.","However, reading literature is of great importance. First, literature is a window on other lives and other times. Through novels and poems, we can experience joys and sorrows that our own life may never offer. Second, literature improves our language. The beautiful sentences we meet in books slowly shape the way we write and speak. Most importantly, literature teaches us to think and to feel deeply, which short messages can never do.","In short, a literature book is far more than a long message. If we are willing to slow down and read it patiently, it will reward us with wisdom and beauty that last a lifetime."],"id":"edu-r1","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay. You should start your essay with a brief description of the picture and then express your views on the importance of reading literature. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.\n图中一位老师对学生说，可以把一本文学书想象成一条很长的短信来读。","set":"写作题2","source":"真题 · 2013年6月 · 写作题2","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"阅读文学的重要性","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2013},{"analysis":[{"en":"The picture shows a father and his son talking.","note":"图画作文先描述人物关系，一句入题。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The son says with worry, “Dad, I'm a bit worried about disposing of nuclear waste.”","note":"直接引用图中儿子的原话：disposing of nuclear waste（处理核废料）——志向大得离谱，正是笑点。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The father answers, “If you can empty the dustbin here, you can do anything.”","note":"父亲的原话就是全图的题眼：empty the dustbin（倒垃圾箱）这件最小的事。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The conversation is funny, but it carries a serious message.","note":"funny / serious 对照，从描述过渡到议论的标准转折。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The picture tells us the importance of doing small things before undertaking something big.","note":"点题句用题目原词组 doing small things before undertaking something big，一字不漏地接住。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Every great achievement is built on small steps.","note":"金句：is built on（建立在……之上）——伟大成就建立在小步之上。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A student who cannot finish today's homework well cannot expect to pass an important exam; a worker who ignores small tasks will never be trusted with a big project.","note":"分号并列学生与工人两个例子，结构对称：小事做不好的人，大事轮不到。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Small things also train our patience and responsibility.","note":"also 再挖一层：小事练的是 patience 和 responsibility（耐心与责任心）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Emptying a dustbin takes only a minute, but the habit of finishing what is in front of us is the base of all success.","note":"回扣图中垃圾箱收束本段：the habit of finishing what is in front of us（把眼前事做完的习惯）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, do not look down on small things.","note":"look down on（看不起）祈使句收尾，先给态度。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"If we do every small thing well, big things will no longer seem so far away.","note":"no longer seem so far away（不再显得那么遥远）展望收尾。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["The picture shows a father and his son talking. The son says with worry, “Dad, I'm a bit worried about disposing of nuclear waste.” The father answers, “If you can empty the dustbin here, you can do anything.” The conversation is funny, but it carries a serious message.","The picture tells us the importance of doing small things before undertaking something big. Every great achievement is built on small steps. A student who cannot finish today's homework well cannot expect to pass an important exam; a worker who ignores small tasks will never be trusted with a big project. Small things also train our patience and responsibility. Emptying a dustbin takes only a minute, but the habit of finishing what is in front of us is the base of all success.","In short, do not look down on small things. If we do every small thing well, big things will no longer seem so far away."],"id":"oth-r1","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay. You should start your essay with a brief description of the picture and then express your views on the importance of doing small things before undertaking something big. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.\n【图片说明】图中父子对话——儿子说：「爸，我有点担心怎么处理核废料。」父亲说：「你要是能先把这儿的垃圾箱倒了，你就什么都能做。」","set":"写作题1","source":"真题 · 2013年6月 · 写作题1","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"other","themeName":"其他","title":"先做小事，再做大事","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2013},{"analysis":[{"en":"The Internet has greatly changed the way students learn.","note":"真题题面就是「影响」，第一句直接点题，不绕弯。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Today, with a computer or a phone in hand, a student can reach almost any knowledge in the world within seconds.","note":"with 短语作伴随状语 + within seconds，把变化写得有画面。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"On the positive side, the Internet makes learning far more convenient and efficient.","note":"On the positive side 开启正面段，和后面的 negative side 成对。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Online courses, digital libraries and search engines allow students to study anytime and anywhere, and to find answers the moment a question appears.","note":"三个名词并列举例；the moment（就在……的那一刻）引导时间从句，地道。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"It also makes learning more interesting, as videos and interactive exercises explain difficult points in a vivid way.","note":"as 引导原因；in a vivid way（生动地）替换 in an interesting way。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, the negative side cannot be ignored.","note":"短句转折开启负面段，cannot be ignored 语气到位。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Too much information makes it hard to judge what is true and useful, and endless entertainment online easily distracts students from their books.","note":"make it hard to do 句型 + distract sb from（让某人从……分心），两个缺点一句说完。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Some even copy homework directly from the Internet instead of thinking on their own.","note":"instead of thinking on their own 用具体行为点出最严重的危害。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In my opinion, the Internet is a powerful tool for learning.","note":"结尾先给定位：工具——好坏取决于人，自然引出最后一句。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Whether it helps or harms depends on how students use it.","note":"whether…or… + depends on how…，辩证收尾，适合一切科技类话题。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["The Internet has greatly changed the way students learn. Today, with a computer or a phone in hand, a student can reach almost any knowledge in the world within seconds.","On the positive side, the Internet makes learning far more convenient and efficient. Online courses, digital libraries and search engines allow students to study anytime and anywhere, and to find answers the moment a question appears. It also makes learning more interesting, as videos and interactive exercises explain difficult points in a vivid way. However, the negative side cannot be ignored. Too much information makes it hard to judge what is true and useful, and endless entertainment online easily distracts students from their books. Some even copy homework directly from the Internet instead of thinking on their own.","In my opinion, the Internet is a powerful tool for learning. Whether it helps or harms depends on how students use it."],"id":"edu-r2","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay based on the picture below. You should start your essay with a brief account of the impact of the Internet on learning and then explain why education doesn't simply mean learning to obtain information. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.\n图中一句话：「等我学会用谷歌了，那不就是我真正需要的全部教育了吗？」","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2013年12月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"网络对学习的影响","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2013},{"analysis":[{"en":"The picture shows a busy street where many people are crossing the road with their eyes fixed on their mobile phones.","note":"eyes fixed on（眼睛盯着）把「低头族」的样子写活；where 从句交代地点。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Strangely, some of them are even using walking sticks to feel the way, as if they could not see the road at all.","note":"as if（仿佛）点出图画的夸张手法：看手机看到像盲人一样探路。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The picture is an exaggeration, but it truly reflects the increasing use of the mobile phone in people's life.","note":"先点明夸张，再落回现实，increasing use 直接用上题目的原词组。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Mobile phones have become a part of our daily life.","note":"主体段先肯定手机的地位，再讲过度使用，评论不偏激。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"We use them to talk, to study, to shop and to find our way.","note":"四个 to do 并列列用途，简洁地交代「使用越来越多」的原因。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, overusing them brings serious consequences.","note":"转折句正面点题：consequences（后果）就是题目要解释的词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"People who stare at their phones while walking or driving put themselves and others in danger.","note":"stare at（盯着看）+ put…in danger（使……处于危险中），第一个后果写得具体。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Besides, spending too much time on phones harms our eyes and sleep, and makes us ignore the family and friends right beside us.","note":"Besides 补两个后果：伤眼伤睡眠 + 忽略身边人（right beside us 点出讽刺)。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, the mobile phone is a useful tool, but we should use it at the right time and in the right place.","note":"结尾给建议：right time、right place，对仗好记。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Only when we control the phone, instead of being controlled by it, can we enjoy its benefits safely.","note":"Only 倒装 + control / be controlled 主被动对比，手机题的经典收尾。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["The picture shows a busy street where many people are crossing the road with their eyes fixed on their mobile phones. Strangely, some of them are even using walking sticks to feel the way, as if they could not see the road at all. The picture is an exaggeration, but it truly reflects the increasing use of the mobile phone in people's life.","Mobile phones have become a part of our daily life. We use them to talk, to study, to shop and to find our way. However, overusing them brings serious consequences. People who stare at their phones while walking or driving put themselves and others in danger. Besides, spending too much time on phones harms our eyes and sleep, and makes us ignore the family and friends right beside us.","In short, the mobile phone is a useful tool, but we should use it at the right time and in the right place. Only when we control the phone, instead of being controlled by it, can we enjoy its benefits safely."],"id":"tech-r1","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay based on the picture below. You should start your essay with a brief account of the increasing use of the mobile phone in people's life and then explain the consequences of overusing it. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.\n【图片说明】图中许多人过马路时低头看着手机，还拄着拐杖探路，仿佛看不见路一样。","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2013年12月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"过度使用手机的后果","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2013},{"analysis":[{"en":"The Internet has brought great changes to the way people communicate with each other.","note":"bring changes to 点题，真题作文第一句就扣住「影响」。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Messages that once took days to deliver now reach friends on the other side of the world in a second.","note":"days → a second 时间对比，把变化写得直观。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"There is no doubt that online communication is convenient and efficient.","note":"There is no doubt that… 开启正面段，语气肯定。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Through social apps, people can keep in touch with old friends, share their daily life and get help quickly whenever they need it.","note":"keep in touch with 是沟通话题的核心词组；三个动词并列列好处。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Distances seem to disappear on the Internet.","note":"短句拟人，正面段的小结，有画面。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"However, problems have appeared at the same time.","note":"转折短句开启负面段，和同年另一套同一主题的写法呼应。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Many young people chat actively online but become silent and awkward when facing real people.","note":"actively online ↔ silent and awkward 对比，「线上社牛、线下社恐」一句写透。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Family members sitting at the same table may each stare at their own phones instead of talking to one another.","note":"一个家庭餐桌的具体场景，正是图中那封信在讽刺的画面，比讲道理更有说服力。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Communication seems easier, yet hearts sometimes grow farther apart.","note":"yet 转折 + 对仗，全篇的点睛句：沟通更易，心却更远。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my opinion, the Internet should serve as a bridge between people, not a wall.","note":"bridge / wall 一对反义比喻表态，正面回答题目「能否取代面对面」：不能。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"We should make good use of it while never forgetting the warmth of face-to-face communication.","note":"make good use of、face-to-face 收尾，落点回到真人交流。","tag":"好词"}],"essay":["The Internet has brought great changes to the way people communicate with each other. Messages that once took days to deliver now reach friends on the other side of the world in a second.","There is no doubt that online communication is convenient and efficient. Through social apps, people can keep in touch with old friends, share their daily life and get help quickly whenever they need it. Distances seem to disappear on the Internet. However, problems have appeared at the same time. Many young people chat actively online but become silent and awkward when facing real people. Family members sitting at the same table may each stare at their own phones instead of talking to one another. Communication seems easier, yet hearts sometimes grow farther apart.","In my opinion, the Internet should serve as a bridge between people, not a wall. We should make good use of it while never forgetting the warmth of face-to-face communication."],"id":"tech-r2","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay based on the picture below. You should start your essay with a brief account of the impact of the Internet on the way people communicate and then explain whether electronic communication can replace face-to-face contact. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.\n【图片说明】图中是一封信：「亲爱的安迪：你好吗？我和你妈妈都很好。我们很想你，希望你一切都好。盼着下次你的电脑坏了、你下楼来吃点东西时，能再见到你。爱你的爸爸妈妈。」","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2013年12月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"网络对人际沟通的影响","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2013},{"analysis":[{"en":"Suppose a foreign friend of mine is coming to visit my campus.","note":"第一句直接套用题目给的 Suppose 假设场景入题，不用另想开头。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Of all the places here, the one I would most like to take him to see is our university library.","note":"Of all…（在所有地方中）+ the one…is… 一句给出选择，正面回答 what。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It is not only the tallest building on campus, but also the heart of our school life.","note":"not only…but also…；heart（心脏、中心）比喻给图书馆定位。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The library is worth visiting for several reasons.","note":"总起句预告下文讲 why，be worth visiting（值得参观）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, its design is special: the building looks like an open book, which stands for knowledge and openness.","note":"stand for（象征）写建筑寓意；open book 的形象具体可感。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Inside, there are millions of books, quiet reading rooms and modern computer areas, where students study from morning till night.","note":"millions of（数百万）写规模；from morning till night 写学习氛围。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"From the top floor, my friend can see the whole campus — the lake, the teaching buildings and the sports field.","note":"破折号列出从楼顶看到的三处景物，画面感强。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"More importantly, in the library he can feel the real atmosphere of our university: everyone is working hard for his or her dream.","note":"More importantly 升到最重要的一点：atmosphere（氛围）——不只是看建筑，是感受学校。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I believe my friend will love this place, because to understand a university, there is no better window than its library.","note":"window 比喻收尾：图书馆是了解一所大学的窗口。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Suppose a foreign friend of mine is coming to visit my campus. Of all the places here, the one I would most like to take him to see is our university library. It is not only the tallest building on campus, but also the heart of our school life.","The library is worth visiting for several reasons. First, its design is special: the building looks like an open book, which stands for knowledge and openness. Inside, there are millions of books, quiet reading rooms and modern computer areas, where students study from morning till night. From the top floor, my friend can see the whole campus — the lake, the teaching buildings and the sports field. More importantly, in the library he can feel the real atmosphere of our university: everyone is working hard for his or her dream.","I believe my friend will love this place, because to understand a university, there is no better window than its library."],"id":"cul-r1","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay on the following topic. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words. Suppose a foreign friend of yours is coming to visit your campus, what is the most interesting place you would like to take him/her to see and why?\n（中文提示：假设你的一位外国朋友来参观你的校园，你最感兴趣的地方想带他/她去看？为什么？）","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2014年6月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"带外国朋友参观校园：图书馆","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2014},{"analysis":[{"en":"If a foreign friend of mine comes to visit my hometown, the first place I would like to take him to is the old town by the river.","note":"If 从句套用题目场景，第一句就给出选择：河边老城。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It is the most interesting place here, because it keeps the history and the true life of our town.","note":"直接用题目原词 the most interesting place；keep（保存）写老城的价值。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In the old town, narrow stone streets are lined with small shops and tea houses that have stood there for hundreds of years.","note":"be lined with（两旁排列着）+ for hundreds of years，历史感一句到位。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"My friend can taste our local food, watch old craftsmen making traditional snacks and tools by hand, and hear stories about the town from friendly shop owners.","note":"taste / watch / hear 三个感官动词并列：吃、看、听——写参观体验的高分写法；craftsmen（手艺人）、by hand（手工）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In the evening, red lanterns light up along the river, and people dance, sing and take walks there.","note":"时间转到傍晚，red lanterns（红灯笼）是家乡夜景的标志画面。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"It is beautiful and peaceful.","note":"短句小结氛围，节奏放缓。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Modern buildings can be seen in any city, but the old town is ours alone.","note":"结尾对比：现代建筑哪儿都有，老城只属于我们——选它的深层理由。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I am sure my friend will understand my hometown much better after this visit.","note":"I am sure… 展望收尾，回扣「带朋友了解家乡」的目的。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["If a foreign friend of mine comes to visit my hometown, the first place I would like to take him to is the old town by the river. It is the most interesting place here, because it keeps the history and the true life of our town.","In the old town, narrow stone streets are lined with small shops and tea houses that have stood there for hundreds of years. My friend can taste our local food, watch old craftsmen making traditional snacks and tools by hand, and hear stories about the town from friendly shop owners. In the evening, red lanterns light up along the river, and people dance, sing and take walks there. It is beautiful and peaceful.","Modern buildings can be seen in any city, but the old town is ours alone. I am sure my friend will understand my hometown much better after this visit."],"id":"cul-r2","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay on the following topic. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words. Suppose a foreign friend of yours is coming to visit your hometown, what is the most interesting place you would like to take him/her to see and why?\n（中文提示：假设你的一位外国朋友来参观你的家乡，你最感兴趣的地方想带他/她去看？为什么？）","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2014年6月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"带外国朋友参观家乡：河边老城","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2014},{"analysis":[{"en":"Suppose a foreign friend of mine is coming to visit China for the first time.","note":"套用题目的 Suppose 场景入题，for the first time 点明「第一次来」。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The first place I would like to take him to see is Beijing, the capital of China.","note":"直接回答 the first place，同位语 the capital of China 补身份。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"No other city can show him so much of our country in so short a time.","note":"No other city… 否定比较句，比 the best 更有力地给出总理由。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Beijing is a city where the old and the new stand side by side.","note":"stand side by side（并肩而立）一句立住全篇框架：古老与现代。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"On one day, my friend can walk on the Great Wall and through the Forbidden City, feeling the long history of China.","note":"On one day / On another day 按天分写行程；Great Wall、Forbidden City 是必写的专名。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"On another day, he can visit modern areas with tall buildings, busy subways and young people working in technology companies.","note":"第二天换到现代面，和第一天对称；technology companies 点出新北京。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"He can also taste Beijing duck, listen to Peking opera and talk with local people in the hutongs.","note":"also 补文化体验三件套：Beijing duck、Peking opera、hutongs——具体名词是文化题的加分项。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Through these experiences, he will see both the past and the future of China.","note":"past / future 对照小结，回扣 old and new 的框架。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"That is why Beijing is my first choice.","note":"That is why… 短句收束论证。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"One city, two faces — ancient and modern — will give my friend a true first picture of China.","note":"One city, two faces 对仗收尾，ancient and modern 呼应全篇。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Suppose a foreign friend of mine is coming to visit China for the first time. The first place I would like to take him to see is Beijing, the capital of China. No other city can show him so much of our country in so short a time.","Beijing is a city where the old and the new stand side by side. On one day, my friend can walk on the Great Wall and through the Forbidden City, feeling the long history of China. On another day, he can visit modern areas with tall buildings, busy subways and young people working in technology companies. He can also taste Beijing duck, listen to Peking opera and talk with local people in the hutongs. Through these experiences, he will see both the past and the future of China.","That is why Beijing is my first choice. One city, two faces — ancient and modern — will give my friend a true first picture of China."],"id":"cul-r3","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay on the following question. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words. Suppose a foreign friend of yours is coming to visit China, what is the first place you would like to take him/her to see and why?\n（中文提示：假设你的一位外国朋友来参观中国，你最感兴趣的地方想带他/她去看？为什么？）","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2014年6月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"带外国朋友游中国：先去北京","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2014},{"analysis":[{"en":"Among all my classmates at college, the one who has influenced me most is my roommate Li Hua.","note":"Among all… + the one who… 第一句直接答出题目问的人，influenced 用题目原词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"She is not the top student in our class, but she has changed the way I study and live more than anyone else.","note":"先抑后扬：不是成绩最好的，却改变我最多——影响不靠名次，立意有新意。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Li Hua is the most hardworking person I know.","note":"主体段总评一句：hardworking（勤奋）是她影响我的核心。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Every morning she gets up at six to read English, and every evening she reviews what she has learned before going to bed.","note":"Every morning / every evening 对照 + 具体时间六点：用日常细节写勤奋，不喊口号。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"At first I laughed at her strict schedule, but when I saw her English improve quickly while mine stayed the same, I began to follow her example.","note":"写自己从嘲笑到效仿的转变：follow her example（以她为榜样）——影响的过程写出来了。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"She also influenced me in life.","note":"also 把影响从学习扩到生活，层次推进。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Whenever I feel lazy or want to give up, her quiet effort reminds me that success is built by daily habits, not by luck.","note":"Whenever…（每当……时）；quiet effort（默默的努力）+ daily habits / luck 对比点题。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I am grateful to have such a classmate.","note":"结尾先表情感：be grateful to（感激）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"She taught me a simple truth: the people around us can be our best teachers.","note":"冒号引出感悟收尾：身边的人就是最好的老师。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Among all my classmates at college, the one who has influenced me most is my roommate Li Hua. She is not the top student in our class, but she has changed the way I study and live more than anyone else.","Li Hua is the most hardworking person I know. Every morning she gets up at six to read English, and every evening she reviews what she has learned before going to bed. At first I laughed at her strict schedule, but when I saw her English improve quickly while mine stayed the same, I began to follow her example. She also influenced me in life. Whenever I feel lazy or want to give up, her quiet effort reminds me that success is built by daily habits, not by luck.","I am grateful to have such a classmate. She taught me a simple truth: the people around us can be our best teachers."],"id":"cam-r1","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay about a classmate of yours who has influenced you most in college. You should state the reasons and write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.\n（中文提示：大学中对你影响最深的一位同学）","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2014年12月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"对我影响最深的同学","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2014},{"analysis":[{"en":"Among all the campus activities I have taken part in, the one that has benefited me most is the volunteer teaching activity organized by our university last summer.","note":"和「影响最深的同学」同一开场句型：一套卷里两道同类题共用骨架，省时又稳。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In that activity, I spent two weeks teaching English to children in a mountain village.","note":"spend time doing（花时间做）交代活动内容：两周、山区、教英语——信息具体。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The activity benefited me in many ways.","note":"总起句用题目原词 benefited，预告下文分点讲受益。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, it improved my ability to communicate and teach.","note":"First / Second 两个受益分层：能力、观念。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"To make children understand, I had to speak simply, use games and be patient — skills no textbook had taught me.","note":"破折号补一句点睛：skills no textbook had taught me（课本没教过的技能）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Second, it changed my view of life.","note":"第二个受益升到人生观，比技能更深一层。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The children studied in simple classrooms with few books, yet they were eager to learn and grateful for every lesson.","note":"simple classrooms / few books 与 eager / grateful 对比：条件差却珍惜——感动的来源写具体了。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Compared with them, I had complained too much and treasured too little.","note":"complained too much / treasured too little 对仗自省：抱怨太多、珍惜太少。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I returned to campus with a clear goal and a thankful heart.","note":"a clear goal and a thankful heart（明确的目标、感恩的心）小结收获。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"That is why this activity has benefited me most: it gave me skills, but more importantly, it gave me a new attitude toward study and life.","note":"That is why… 回扣开头；skills → attitude 两层收获收齐。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Among all the campus activities I have taken part in, the one that has benefited me most is the volunteer teaching activity organized by our university last summer. In that activity, I spent two weeks teaching English to children in a mountain village.","The activity benefited me in many ways. First, it improved my ability to communicate and teach. To make children understand, I had to speak simply, use games and be patient — skills no textbook had taught me. Second, it changed my view of life. The children studied in simple classrooms with few books, yet they were eager to learn and grateful for every lesson. Compared with them, I had complained too much and treasured too little. I returned to campus with a clear goal and a thankful heart.","That is why this activity has benefited me most: it gave me skills, but more importantly, it gave me a new attitude toward study and life."],"id":"cam-r2","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay about a campus activity that has benefited you most. You should state the reasons and write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.\n（中文提示：使你受益最深的一项校园活动）","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2014年12月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"使我受益最深的校园活动","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2014},{"analysis":[{"en":"Among all the courses I have taken at college, the one that has impressed me most is College English.","note":"Among all… 开头 + 定语从句，直接答出题目问的「哪门课」。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It may sound like a common course, but for me it opened a completely new door.","note":"先抑后扬：听起来普通，却为我打开一扇新门——open a door 比喻好用。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I still remember my first English class.","note":"用一次具体的课展开，比空讲「这门课很好」有说服力。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Our teacher did not ask us to memorize words from a list.","note":"memorize words（背单词）+ 否定句式，先写老师「不做什么」制造对比。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Instead, she played short English videos, divided us into groups and encouraged us to discuss and act out the stories.","note":"Instead 转折后三个动词并列，课堂画面一下子具体了；act out（表演出来）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"For the first time, I found that English was not just a subject for exams, but a living tool for communication.","note":"not just…but… + living tool（活的工具），点出认识上的转变。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The course also trained my ability to learn on my own.","note":"also 引出第二个理由：从课堂形式转到自学能力，层次分明。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"We had to search for materials, prepare presentations and answer questions in English, which built up my confidence step by step.","note":"三个任务并列；build up confidence（建立信心）+ step by step 收尾。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Thanks to this course, English has become my favourite subject, and I am no longer afraid of speaking it.","note":"Thanks to（多亏）+ no longer（不再），写出课程带来的改变。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"A good course can change a student's attitude toward learning, and College English has done exactly that for me.","note":"结尾从一门课升到普遍道理，再落回自己，首尾呼应。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Among all the courses I have taken at college, the one that has impressed me most is College English. It may sound like a common course, but for me it opened a completely new door.","I still remember my first English class. Our teacher did not ask us to memorize words from a list. Instead, she played short English videos, divided us into groups and encouraged us to discuss and act out the stories. For the first time, I found that English was not just a subject for exams, but a living tool for communication. The course also trained my ability to learn on my own. We had to search for materials, prepare presentations and answer questions in English, which built up my confidence step by step.","Thanks to this course, English has become my favourite subject, and I am no longer afraid of speaking it. A good course can change a student's attitude toward learning, and College English has done exactly that for me."],"id":"edu-r3","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay about a course that has impressed you most in college. You should state the reasons and write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.\n（中文提示：大学中给你印象最深的一门课）","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2014年12月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"印象最深的一门课","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2014},{"analysis":[{"en":"The picture shows a little boy talking to his parent.","note":"图画作文开头先描述：人物 + 动作，一句到位。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"He asks proudly, “Why am I going to school if my phone already knows everything?”","note":"直接引用图中的原话，proudly（得意地）一个词写出孩子的神气。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"His words sound funny, but they reveal how the kid understands going to school: in his eyes, school is only a place to get knowledge, and since the phone knows everything, school seems useless.","note":"reveal 引出题目要评论的「孩子的理解」，冒号后把他的逻辑复述清楚，再开始评论。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"This understanding is natural for a child, but it is far from the truth.","note":"先肯定（对孩子来说很自然）再否定（far from the truth），评论有分寸。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A phone can give answers, yet it cannot teach a child how to ask good questions, how to judge whether an answer is right, or how to get along with classmates and teachers.","note":"can / cannot 对比 + 三个 how to 并列：提问、判断、相处，都是手机教不了的。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"School is not only about knowledge.","note":"短句单独成句，强调转折，全段的中心句。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It is where children learn rules, friendship, patience and responsibility — lessons no screen can provide.","note":"四个名词并列列出学校真正教的东西；no screen can provide 收得有力。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In my view, parents and teachers should guide children to use phones wisely, as a helper in study rather than a replacement for school.","note":"guide sb to do（引导某人做）；helper / replacement 一对词把态度说清。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Only at school can a child grow in every way.","note":"Only 倒装结尾，grow in every way（全面成长）点题。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["The picture shows a little boy talking to his parent. He asks proudly, “Why am I going to school if my phone already knows everything?” His words sound funny, but they reveal how the kid understands going to school: in his eyes, school is only a place to get knowledge, and since the phone knows everything, school seems useless.","This understanding is natural for a child, but it is far from the truth. A phone can give answers, yet it cannot teach a child how to ask good questions, how to judge whether an answer is right, or how to get along with classmates and teachers. School is not only about knowledge. It is where children learn rules, friendship, patience and responsibility — lessons no screen can provide.","In my view, parents and teachers should guide children to use phones wisely, as a helper in study rather than a replacement for school. Only at school can a child grow in every way."],"id":"edu-r4","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay based on the picture below. You should start your essay with a brief description of the picture and then comment on the kid's understanding of going to school. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.\n图中孩子说：「我的手机什么都知道了，我为什么还要上学？」","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2015年6月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"孩子眼中的上学","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2015},{"analysis":[{"en":"The picture shows a happy girl telling her mother the good news: she was accepted to the college of her mother's choice.","note":"描述画面时把关键信息带出来：of her mother's choice（她妈妈选的）——图画的讽刺点就在这几个词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The mother smiles proudly, while the girl's words quietly reveal something worth thinking about — the college was chosen not by the girl, but by her mother.","note":"while 对照母女神情；not by…but by… 把「谁在做主」点破，过渡到评论。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Parents play a very important role in their children's growth.","note":"评论第一句正面点题：play a role 用上题目原词 role。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"They are our first teachers: they feed us, protect us and teach us right from wrong.","note":"first teachers 比喻；right from wrong（是非对错）固定搭配。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Good parents also guide us at key moments, such as choosing a school, with their experience and love.","note":"guide（引导）先肯定父母的正面角色；such as choosing a school 回扣图中的选大学。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, guidance should not become control.","note":"guidance / control 一词之差点出分寸：引导不能变成控制——全篇的题眼句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"If parents decide everything, children may lose the chance to think and choose for themselves, and may never learn to take responsibility for their own life.","note":"If 从句推演后果链：包办 → 不会选择 → 不会负责；take responsibility for（对……负责）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"What children need most is support that respects their own wishes.","note":"What 主语从句给出正面主张：尊重孩子意愿的支持。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my view, the best parents are like gardeners: they give water and sunshine, but let the flowers grow in their own way.","note":"园丁与花朵的比喻收尾：给水给阳光，但让花按自己的方式长——背下来，亲子题万能结尾。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["The picture shows a happy girl telling her mother the good news: she was accepted to the college of her mother's choice. The mother smiles proudly, while the girl's words quietly reveal something worth thinking about — the college was chosen not by the girl, but by her mother.","Parents play a very important role in their children's growth. They are our first teachers: they feed us, protect us and teach us right from wrong. Good parents also guide us at key moments, such as choosing a school, with their experience and love. However, guidance should not become control. If parents decide everything, children may lose the chance to think and choose for themselves, and may never learn to take responsibility for their own life. What children need most is support that respects their own wishes.","In my view, the best parents are like gardeners: they give water and sunshine, but let the flowers grow in their own way."],"id":"soc-r1","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay based on the picture below. You should start your essay with a brief description of the picture and then comment on parents' role in their children's growth. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.\n【图片说明】图中女孩高兴地告诉妈妈：「好消息，妈妈！我被你选的那所大学录取了。」","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2015年6月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"父母在孩子成长中的角色","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2015},{"analysis":[{"en":"The picture shows a person who spends the whole day in front of a computer.","note":"描述画面先抓总特征：whole day + in front of a computer。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"He works before the screen, studies before the screen, plays games before the screen, and even in his dreams he is still sitting there.","note":"before the screen 重复三次的排比 + even in his dreams，把图中的夸张细节写足。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"This is the modern life of many people today.","note":"短句把画面落到题目原词 modern life 上，过渡到评论。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"There is no doubt that computers have brought us great convenience.","note":"评论先扬：convenience（便利）开启正面部分。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"We can finish work faster, learn almost anything online and talk with friends far away.","note":"三个动词并列列便利，具体不空洞。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Life without computers is hard to imagine now.","note":"hard to imagine（难以想象）侧面写电脑的普及程度。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"However, this kind of life also has a worrying side.","note":"However 转入担忧，this kind of life 回扣题目措辞。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Sitting before a screen all day harms our eyes and bodies, and many people slowly lose the habit of exercising and meeting friends face to face.","note":"动名词作主语；lose the habit of（失去……的习惯）点出生活方式的退化。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"What is worse, some become so dependent on computers that they feel lost without them.","note":"What is worse 递进；be dependent on（依赖）+ feel lost（无所适从）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, computers should serve our life, not rule it.","note":"serve / rule 对比收尾表态：电脑该服务生活，而不是主宰生活。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"We should enjoy their convenience while remembering to stand up, go out and live a real life beyond the screen.","note":"三个动作（站起来、走出去、过真实生活）+ beyond the screen，结尾有行动感。","tag":"好词"}],"essay":["The picture shows a person who spends the whole day in front of a computer. He works before the screen, studies before the screen, plays games before the screen, and even in his dreams he is still sitting there. This is the modern life of many people today.","There is no doubt that computers have brought us great convenience. We can finish work faster, learn almost anything online and talk with friends far away. Life without computers is hard to imagine now. However, this kind of life also has a worrying side. Sitting before a screen all day harms our eyes and bodies, and many people slowly lose the habit of exercising and meeting friends face to face. What is worse, some become so dependent on computers that they feel lost without them.","In my view, computers should serve our life, not rule it. We should enjoy their convenience while remembering to stand up, go out and live a real life beyond the screen."],"id":"tech-r3","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay based on the picture below. You should start your essay with a brief description of the picture and then comment on this kind of modern life. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.\n【图片说明】图中一个人整天守在电脑前：工作、学习、玩乐，连做梦时都在电脑前。","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2015年6月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"评论图中「电脑前的人生」","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2015},{"analysis":[{"en":"There is a famous saying: “Learning is a daily experience and a lifetime mission.”","note":"评论名言类作文，第一句先把名言原样引出来。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It tells us that learning should not stop when we leave school; instead, it should go on every day and throughout our whole life.","note":"用自己的话解释名言：daily 对应 every day，lifetime 对应 whole life——解释名言就是换词复述。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I fully agree with this view.","note":"短句表态，fully（完全）语气明确。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The importance of lifelong learning is easy to see.","note":"主体段首句点出本段任务：讲重要性（题目原词 lifelong learning)。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Knowledge and technology are changing faster than ever before.","note":"faster than ever before（比以往任何时候都快），讲变化的万能句。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"A skill that is useful today may become out of date in a few years.","note":"out of date（过时）是准词；today / in a few years 时间对比。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"My father, an engineer, still spends an hour reading technical books every evening, because he knows that once he stops learning, he will fall behind.","note":"题目说 cite examples——身边的例子最可信；spend time doing + fall behind（落伍）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Lifelong learning also keeps our minds young.","note":"also 引出第二个好处，keep our minds young 说法形象。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Grandparents who learn to use smartphones and computers can enjoy modern life instead of feeling left out.","note":"再举一例（老人学手机）；feel left out（觉得被落下）地道。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In short, learning is not a task for students only.","note":"结尾先破除误解：学习不只是学生的事。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It is a habit for life, and those who keep learning will always keep growing.","note":"habit for life 呼应 lifetime，keep learning / keep growing 排比收尾。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["There is a famous saying: “Learning is a daily experience and a lifetime mission.” It tells us that learning should not stop when we leave school; instead, it should go on every day and throughout our whole life. I fully agree with this view.","The importance of lifelong learning is easy to see. Knowledge and technology are changing faster than ever before. A skill that is useful today may become out of date in a few years. My father, an engineer, still spends an hour reading technical books every evening, because he knows that once he stops learning, he will fall behind. Lifelong learning also keeps our minds young. Grandparents who learn to use smartphones and computers can enjoy modern life instead of feeling left out.","In short, learning is not a task for students only. It is a habit for life, and those who keep learning will always keep growing."],"id":"edu-r5","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay commenting on the saying “Learning is a daily experience and a lifetime mission.” You can cite examples to illustrate the importance of lifelong learning. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2015年12月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"评论名言：终身学习","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2015},{"analysis":[{"en":"There is a saying: “Never go out there to see what happens, go out there to make something happen.”","note":"名言题第一句引原话；这句名言本身就是 see / make 的对照，先抄准。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It calls on us not to be mere onlookers in life, but to be creative and take action.","note":"用自己的话解释名言：mere onlookers（ mere 仅仅是）用题目原词，call on（号召）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"I cannot agree more.","note":"I cannot agree more（我完全同意）短句表态，比 I agree 更有力。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The world is changed by people who make things happen, not by those who only watch.","note":"被动语态 + make things happen / only watch 对照，把名言变成论点。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In our daily life, onlookers are easy to find: students who wait for others to answer every question, or group members who never offer an idea but only comment on others' work.","note":"题目说 cite examples——举身边两类旁观者：等别人答题的、只评论不出主意的。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Such people may feel safe, but they learn little and achieve little.","note":"learn little and achieve little 对仗：看着安全，其实学得少成得也少。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In contrast, those who dare to try — starting a small project, joining a competition, or simply raising a hand in class — grow quickly even when they fail, because action turns ideas into experience.","note":"In contrast 转到行动者；破折号里三个动作从大到小（项目、比赛、举手）；turn…into… 点出失败也值。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, life rewards the doers, not the watchers.","note":"the doers / the watchers（行动者 / 旁观者）名词化对照收尾。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Let us stop waiting to see what happens, and start making something happen today.","note":"最后一句把名言的两半各用一次作号召，首尾呼应。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["There is a saying: “Never go out there to see what happens, go out there to make something happen.” It calls on us not to be mere onlookers in life, but to be creative and take action. I cannot agree more.","The world is changed by people who make things happen, not by those who only watch. In our daily life, onlookers are easy to find: students who wait for others to answer every question, or group members who never offer an idea but only comment on others' work. Such people may feel safe, but they learn little and achieve little. In contrast, those who dare to try — starting a small project, joining a competition, or simply raising a hand in class — grow quickly even when they fail, because action turns ideas into experience.","In short, life rewards the doers, not the watchers. Let us stop waiting to see what happens, and start making something happen today."],"id":"oth-r2","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay commenting on the saying “Never go out there to see what happens, go out there to make something happen.” You can cite examples to illustrate the importance of being creative rather than mere onlookers in life. You should write at least 120 words, no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2015年12月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"other","themeName":"其他","title":"评论名言：去创造，别旁观","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2015},{"analysis":[{"en":"There is a saying: “Listening is more important than talking.”","note":"名言评论题第一句先引名言，和终身学习那道题同一开场。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"At first this may sound strange, because we usually praise people who speak well.","note":"先写读者的第一反应（有点奇怪），制造悬念再翻转——评论名言的好起手。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"But if we think carefully, we will find deep truth in it.","note":"But 转折亮明态度：细想有道理。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Listening is important for at least three reasons.","note":"at least three reasons 预告三层论证，结构感强。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, we learn by listening.","note":"三个理由：学知识、表尊重、防冲突。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In class, in meetings and in daily conversation, the person who listens carefully gains the most knowledge.","note":"三个 in 场景并列；gain knowledge（获得知识）搭配准。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, listening shows respect.","note":"第二个理由换到人际层面。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"When we listen to others without interrupting, they feel understood and are willing to share their real thoughts.","note":"without interrupting（不打断）是倾听最具体的动作；feel understood（觉得被理解）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Third, listening prevents mistakes and conflicts.","note":"第三个理由讲预防：prevent（预防）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Many arguments begin simply because neither side truly heard the other.","note":"neither side（一边都不）点出争吵的根源：谁也没听谁。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A good listener often solves problems that a good talker cannot.","note":"listener / talker 对照收束三段论证。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, talking expresses what we already know, but listening opens the door to what we do not know.","note":"already know / do not know 对比：说的是已知的，听的是未知的——金句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"That is why the wise listen more and talk less.","note":"listen more and talk less 对仗收尾，和名言首尾呼应。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["There is a saying: “Listening is more important than talking.” At first this may sound strange, because we usually praise people who speak well. But if we think carefully, we will find deep truth in it.","Listening is important for at least three reasons. First, we learn by listening. In class, in meetings and in daily conversation, the person who listens carefully gains the most knowledge. Second, listening shows respect. When we listen to others without interrupting, they feel understood and are willing to share their real thoughts. Third, listening prevents mistakes and conflicts. Many arguments begin simply because neither side truly heard the other. A good listener often solves problems that a good talker cannot.","In short, talking expresses what we already know, but listening opens the door to what we do not know. That is why the wise listen more and talk less."],"id":"soc-r2","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay commenting on the saying “Listening is more important than talking.” You can cite examples to illustrate the importance of listening. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2015年12月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"评论名言：倾听比谈话更重要","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2015},{"analysis":[{"en":"Dear Mom and Dad,","note":"感谢信称呼，对象就是题目给定的父母。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I am writing this letter to express my sincere gratitude to you both.","note":"第一句点明写信目的：express gratitude（表达感谢）是感谢信的标志说法。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Now that I have been away at university for a term, I understand more deeply how much you have done for me over the years.","note":"Now that（既然、如今）引出离家后的新体会，感谢有了由头，不空。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Thank you for raising me with endless patience and love.","note":"主体段用 Thank you for… 分层展开感谢，raise（养育）用词准。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"You worked hard to give me a comfortable life and a good education, yet you seldom spoke of your own tiredness.","note":"yet 转折写出父母的默默付出，具体才动人。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Thank you also for teaching me to be honest, kind and independent.","note":"第二层感谢从养育升到品格：honest、kind、independent 三个词并列。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The words you repeated a thousand times, which I once found annoying, have become my guide whenever I face difficulties away from home.","note":"which 从句插入「曾经嫌烦」的真心话，感情真实，是全信最动人的一句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I know I cannot repay all that you have given me, but I will study hard and take good care of myself, so that one day I can support you as you have supported me.","note":"repay（报答）+ so that 目的从句许下回报的承诺，感谢信不能只谢不表态。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Thank you again for everything.","note":"结尾再次致谢，书信收束的礼节。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I miss you very much and will come home as soon as the term ends.","note":"补一句思念和归期，落款 Yours lovingly + Li Ming——给父母的信落款用 lovingly 更贴切，且按惯例不用真名。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Dear Mom and Dad,","I am writing this letter to express my sincere gratitude to you both. Now that I have been away at university for a term, I understand more deeply how much you have done for me over the years.","Thank you for raising me with endless patience and love. You worked hard to give me a comfortable life and a good education, yet you seldom spoke of your own tiredness. Thank you also for teaching me to be honest, kind and independent. The words you repeated a thousand times, which I once found annoying, have become my guide whenever I face difficulties away from home. I know I cannot repay all that you have given me, but I will study hard and take good care of myself, so that one day I can support you as you have supported me.","Thank you again for everything. I miss you very much and will come home as soon as the term ends.","Yours lovingly,","Li Ming"],"id":"oth-r3","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a letter to express your thanks to your parents or any other family member upon making a memorable achievement. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2016年6月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"other","themeName":"其他","title":"感谢信：写给父母","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2016},{"analysis":[{"en":"Dear Mr. Li,","note":"写给老师的称呼用 Mr./Ms. + 姓，和写给父母、朋友的信区分开——同年三封感谢信称呼各不同。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I am writing to express my sincere thanks to you.","note":"第一句点明目的，和父母那封同一骨架，只换致谢对象。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Now that I have entered college, I often think of the days in your class, and I realize more and more how much you have helped me.","note":"Now that… 点出题目给的时机 upon entering college（考上大学之际）——谢信要有由头。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"You were the teacher who changed my attitude toward English.","note":"主体段总起：先给老师一个定位（改变我对英语态度的人），再展开细节。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In high school, I was afraid of this subject and my grades were poor.","note":"先写自己的起点（怕英语、成绩差），老师的帮助才有对照。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Instead of blaming me, you encouraged me after every small progress, stayed after class to answer my questions, and taught me how to learn step by step.","note":"Instead of blaming（不责备）+ 三个具体动作并列：鼓励、留堂答疑、手把手教方法——感谢要谢到具体事上。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Because of you, English became my favourite subject, and I finally entered the university I had dreamed of.","note":"Because of you（因为您）点出结果；the university I had dreamed of 回扣 upon entering college。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"More importantly, you taught me to be patient with myself and never give up — a lesson I will use for my whole life.","note":"感谢从成绩升到品格：be patient with oneself（对自己有耐心）；a lesson… 同位语收束。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Thank you again for everything you have done for me.","note":"结尾再次致谢，书信礼节。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I will study hard at college and come back to visit you one day as a student you can be proud of.","note":"许诺 + be proud of（为……自豪）：让老师自豪的学生——最打动老师的一句收尾。落款 Yours sincerely 给老师用最得体。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Dear Mr. Li,","I am writing to express my sincere thanks to you. Now that I have entered college, I often think of the days in your class, and I realize more and more how much you have helped me.","You were the teacher who changed my attitude toward English. In high school, I was afraid of this subject and my grades were poor. Instead of blaming me, you encouraged me after every small progress, stayed after class to answer my questions, and taught me how to learn step by step. Because of you, English became my favourite subject, and I finally entered the university I had dreamed of. More importantly, you taught me to be patient with myself and never give up — a lesson I will use for my whole life.","Thank you again for everything you have done for me. I will study hard at college and come back to visit you one day as a student you can be proud of.","Yours sincerely,","Li Ming"],"id":"oth-r4","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a letter to express your thanks to one of your school teachers upon entering college. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2016年6月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"other","themeName":"其他","title":"感谢信：写给老师","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2016},{"analysis":[{"en":"Dear Xiao Ming,","note":"写给朋友称呼用名字即可，语气可以比给老师的信亲近。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I am writing to say thank you to my best friend.","note":"第一句点明目的，say thank you 口语化，正合朋友身份。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Last winter, when I was in the greatest difficulty of my life, it was you who helped me most, and I have never found the right chance to thank you properly.","note":"强调句 it was you who… 把题目原词 helped me most、in difficulty 都接住；补一句「一直没机会好好谢你」交代写信由头。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"That winter, I broke my leg in an accident and had to stay in hospital for a month.","note":"主体段先把「困难」讲具体：骨折住院一个月——感谢信要先有故事。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I was worried about my studies and felt lonely and helpless.","note":"lonely and helpless（孤独无助）写困境中的心情，为朋友的帮助做铺垫。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"You came to see me almost every day after class, bringing me notes, homework and news from school.","note":"帮助写成具体动作：almost every day + bringing 三样东西（笔记、作业、消息）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"You helped me review lessons beside my bed and encouraged me whenever I wanted to give up.","note":"再补一层帮助：补课 + 鼓励；whenever I wanted to give up 写出低谷时刻。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Thanks to you, I did not fall behind, and I recovered with a peaceful heart.","note":"Thanks to you（多亏你）点出结果：没落下功课、安心养伤。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A friend in need is a friend indeed, and you are the truest proof of this saying.","note":"谚语 A friend in need is a friend indeed（患难见真情）用在朋友感谢信里正对题；proof（证明）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Thank you again, my dear friend.","note":"结尾再次致谢。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Whenever you need me in the future, I will be there for you, just as you were there for me.","note":"be there for you（在你身边支持你）许下对等承诺 + 落款 Yours + Li Ming，朋友信的落款最简短亲切。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Dear Xiao Ming,","I am writing to say thank you to my best friend. Last winter, when I was in the greatest difficulty of my life, it was you who helped me most, and I have never found the right chance to thank you properly.","That winter, I broke my leg in an accident and had to stay in hospital for a month. I was worried about my studies and felt lonely and helpless. You came to see me almost every day after class, bringing me notes, homework and news from school. You helped me review lessons beside my bed and encouraged me whenever I wanted to give up. Thanks to you, I did not fall behind, and I recovered with a peaceful heart. A friend in need is a friend indeed, and you are the truest proof of this saying.","Thank you again, my dear friend. Whenever you need me in the future, I will be there for you, just as you were there for me.","Yours,","Li Ming"],"id":"oth-r5","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a letter to express your thanks to one of your friends who helped you most when you were in difficulty. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2016年6月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"other","themeName":"其他","title":"感谢信：写给朋友","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2016},{"analysis":[{"en":"Upon graduation, I have two options: one is to take a job in a company and the other to go to a graduate school.","note":"第一句把题目的两个选项原样摆出来，one is…the other…——二选一作文的标准开场，同年三道题共用。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"After careful thinking, I choose the first one — to start working right after graduation.","note":"第二句就亮明选择，不拖泥带水；After careful thinking（经过认真考虑）显出不是随口选的。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I make this choice for three reasons.","note":"总起预告三条理由，结构先行。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, I want to become financially independent as early as possible.","note":"financially independent（经济独立）是就业话题的题眼词组。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"My parents have supported me for many years, and it is time for me to earn my own living and lighten their burden.","note":"earn my own living（自己谋生）+ lighten their burden（减轻他们的负担），理由落到家庭真实。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, real work experience is valuable.","note":"第二条转到经验价值。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In a company, I can learn how society and my industry truly work, which no classroom can teach completely.","note":"两个 how 从句并列；which…no classroom can teach（课堂教不了的）点出工作的不可替代。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Third, going to graduate school is not the only way to keep learning.","note":"第三条先破除对方的最强理由：读研不是唯一的学习路。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I can study while working, and if I find a clear research interest later, I can still apply for further study with richer experience.","note":"留一条后路：以后有兴趣还能读研——选择显得不极端，论证更稳。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Everyone's situation is different, and graduate school is a good choice for many.","note":"结尾先让步：承认另一选择对很多人是对的。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"But for me, entering society first is the better road, and I will walk it with full effort.","note":"for me 限定回自己；the better road + walk it with full effort（全力走下去）收尾有决心。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Upon graduation, I have two options: one is to take a job in a company and the other to go to a graduate school. After careful thinking, I choose the first one — to start working right after graduation.","I make this choice for three reasons. First, I want to become financially independent as early as possible. My parents have supported me for many years, and it is time for me to earn my own living and lighten their burden. Second, real work experience is valuable. In a company, I can learn how society and my industry truly work, which no classroom can teach completely. Third, going to graduate school is not the only way to keep learning. I can study while working, and if I find a clear research interest later, I can still apply for further study with richer experience.","Everyone's situation is different, and graduate school is a good choice for many. But for me, entering society first is the better road, and I will walk it with full effort."],"id":"car-r1","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay. Suppose you have two options upon graduation: one is to take a job in a company and the other to go to a graduate school. You are to make a choice between the two. Write an essay to explain the reasons for your choice. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2016年12月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"career","themeName":"职业规划","title":"毕业二选一：就业还是读研","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2016},{"analysis":[{"en":"Upon graduation, I have two options: one is to work in a state-owned business and the other in a joint venture.","note":"开场句型与同年第 1 套完全一致，只换选项——二选一题的选项词要写准：state-owned business（国企）、joint venture（合资企业）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"After comparing the two, I choose to work in a joint venture.","note":"comparing（比较过后）比第 1 套的 careful thinking 更贴这道题：两种企业要比着选。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"My choice is based on three reasons.","note":"总起三条理由：环境、英语眼界、待遇。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, a joint venture offers a more open and competitive environment.","note":"offer（提供）+ competitive environment（竞争环境），先讲成长环境。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Young people there are usually given chances according to their ability, not their age, so I can grow faster.","note":"according to ability, not age（凭能力不凭资历）一句写出合资企业的吸引力。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Second, working in a joint venture can improve my English and international view.","note":"international view（国际视野）是合资企业独有的好处，别的选项给不了。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"I will have chances to work with foreign colleagues and customers, which is valuable experience in today's world.","note":"foreign colleagues and customers 具体化「国际」二字。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Third, the pay in joint ventures is often higher, and the training systems are usually complete.","note":"第三条讲待遇与培训：pay、training systems 都是求职话题准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Admittedly, the pressure is also greater and the job is less stable than in a state-owned business, but I am young and willing to accept challenges.","note":"Admittedly（不可否认）主动承认对方的长处（stable 稳定），再用年轻愿意拼反打——二选一作文的高分让步。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In conclusion, both choices have their own advantages.","note":"结尾先公平评价两边。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"For a young graduate who wants to grow quickly, a joint venture is the better choice, and I am ready for it.","note":"把选择限定到「想快速成长的年轻人」，I am ready for it 收尾有劲。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Upon graduation, I have two options: one is to work in a state-owned business and the other in a joint venture. After comparing the two, I choose to work in a joint venture.","My choice is based on three reasons. First, a joint venture offers a more open and competitive environment. Young people there are usually given chances according to their ability, not their age, so I can grow faster. Second, working in a joint venture can improve my English and international view. I will have chances to work with foreign colleagues and customers, which is valuable experience in today's world. Third, the pay in joint ventures is often higher, and the training systems are usually complete. Admittedly, the pressure is also greater and the job is less stable than in a state-owned business, but I am young and willing to accept challenges.","In conclusion, both choices have their own advantages. For a young graduate who wants to grow quickly, a joint venture is the better choice, and I am ready for it."],"id":"car-r2","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay. Suppose you have two options upon graduation: one is to work in a state-owned business and the other in a joint venture. You are to make a choice between the two. Write an essay to explain the reasons for your choice. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2016年12月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"career","themeName":"职业规划","title":"毕业二选一：国企还是合资企业","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2016},{"analysis":[{"en":"Upon graduation, I have two options: one is to find a job somewhere and the other to start a business of my own.","note":"开场三度复用同年句型：start a business of my own（创办自己的事业）用题目原词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"After serious consideration, I choose to find a job first instead of starting a business right away.","note":"选择的关键在 first 和 right away 两个词：不是不创业，是先就业——立场比前两道更曲折，开头就要点清。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"My reasons are practical.","note":"短句定调：practical（务实的）——这道题的理由要讲现实条件。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, starting a business needs money, experience and connections, and as a new graduate I have none of them.","note":"创业三要素并列：money、experience、connections（人脉）；have none of them 一句说清新毕业生的处境。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Most businesses started without preparation fail within a few years.","note":"fail（失败）+ within a few years，用普遍事实支撑判断，不空谈。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, working in a company first is itself a preparation for business.","note":"翻转视角：先工作本身就是为创业做准备——本篇的核心论点。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In a job, I can learn how a company is run, how customers think and how a team works, while saving money for the future.","note":"三个 how 从句并列写工作中学什么；while saving money 补上攒钱。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Starting a business is my long-term dream, not a plan for today.","note":"long-term dream / a plan for today 对照：梦想保留，时机未到。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"When I have experience, savings and a clear idea, I will start my own business with a much greater chance of success.","note":"When 从句列出创业的三个前提，和第一段缺的三样正好呼应——首尾成环。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, I do not give up the dream of my own business; I only choose a safer order: work first, prepare well, and then start.","note":"结尾三段式口号收束：work first, prepare well, then start——顺序感就是全篇的答案。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Upon graduation, I have two options: one is to find a job somewhere and the other to start a business of my own. After serious consideration, I choose to find a job first instead of starting a business right away.","My reasons are practical. First, starting a business needs money, experience and connections, and as a new graduate I have none of them. Most businesses started without preparation fail within a few years. Second, working in a company first is itself a preparation for business. In a job, I can learn how a company is run, how customers think and how a team works, while saving money for the future. Starting a business is my long-term dream, not a plan for today. When I have experience, savings and a clear idea, I will start my own business with a much greater chance of success.","In short, I do not give up the dream of my own business; I only choose a safer order: work first, prepare well, and then start."],"id":"car-r3","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay. Suppose you have two options upon graduation: one is to find a job somewhere and the other to start a business of your own. You are to make a choice between the two. Write an essay to explain the reasons for your choice. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2016年12月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"career","themeName":"职业规划","title":"毕业二选一：找工作还是自己创业","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2016},{"analysis":[{"en":"Used Computer for Sale — Good Condition, Low Price!","note":"广告标题三要素：卖什么 + 品相 + 价格——和旧书广告同一格式，一套卷三种广告共用。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Are you looking for a cheap but reliable computer for study?","note":"问句开场锁定买家：学生党要的就是 cheap but reliable（便宜又可靠）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I am a senior student who is about to graduate, and I am selling the laptop I used at college.","note":"交代卖家身份和出售原因（毕业），广告可信度立刻上来。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It is a Lenovo laptop with a 14-inch screen, an Intel i5 processor, 8GB of memory and a 512GB hard drive.","note":"题目点名要写 brand 和 specifications：品牌 + 屏幕、处理器、内存、硬盘四项参数一项不少——广告题按题目清单逐项落实。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"It runs fast and is perfect for writing papers, watching online courses and doing daily work.","note":"参数之后讲用途：写论文、看网课——买家关心的是能干什么。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The computer is in good condition.","note":"第二段专讲 condition（品相），和题目清单一一对应。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I bought it two years ago, and it has never been repaired.","note":"has never been repaired（从没修过）是二手电子产品最有分量的一句品相证明。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The battery still lasts about five hours.","note":"lasts（续航）补电池状态，细节决定可信度。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The original price was 4,500 yuan, and now I am selling it for only 1,800 yuan.","note":"原价与现价数字对比，only 强调便宜——广告没有价格等于白写。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A mouse and a computer bag will be given free to the buyer.","note":"赠品促销，和旧书广告的赠品手法呼应。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Interested?","note":"短问句转入行动号召。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Please contact me at 138-XXXX-XXXX, or come to Room 405, Dormitory Building 3, to see it yourself.","note":"联系方式 + 看货地点齐全（题目点名要 contact information），电话用 XXXX 占位。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First come, first served!","note":"先到先得收尾，广告固定说法。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Used Computer for Sale — Good Condition, Low Price!","Are you looking for a cheap but reliable computer for study? I am a senior student who is about to graduate, and I am selling the laptop I used at college. It is a Lenovo laptop with a 14-inch screen, an Intel i5 processor, 8GB of memory and a 512GB hard drive. It runs fast and is perfect for writing papers, watching online courses and doing daily work.","The computer is in good condition. I bought it two years ago, and it has never been repaired. The battery still lasts about five hours. The original price was 4,500 yuan, and now I am selling it for only 1,800 yuan. A mouse and a computer bag will be given free to the buyer.","Interested? Please contact me at 138-XXXX-XXXX, or come to Room 405, Dormitory Building 3, to see it yourself. First come, first served!"],"id":"cam-r3","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an advertisement on your campus website to sell a computer you used at college. Your advertisement may include its brand, specifications/features, condition and price, and your contact information. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2017年6月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"广告：出售二手笔记本电脑","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2017},{"analysis":[{"en":"Bicycle for Sale — Almost New!","note":"标题：品名 + 最大卖点（Almost New 几乎全新）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Do you want an easy way to travel around our large campus?","note":"问句从买家的痛点切入：校园大、走路累——先讲需求再讲车。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I am selling the bicycle I used at college because I am graduating this summer.","note":"出售原因（毕业）一句交代，和电脑广告同一手法。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It is a Giant mountain bike, black and silver, with 21 speeds.","note":"题目要的 brand 和 features：品牌、车型、颜色、变速档位，一句写全。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"It is light, strong and comfortable to ride, and it is suitable for both boys and girls.","note":"三个形容词写骑行感受；suitable for both boys and girls 扩大买家范围。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The bicycle is in very good condition.","note":"第二段讲 condition，和题目清单对应。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I bought it one year ago for 900 yuan, and I have kept it carefully.","note":"购买时间 + kept it carefully（保养得好）证明品相。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The brakes and tyres are almost new, and the lock and basket are included.","note":"brakes（刹车）、tyres（轮胎）点名易损件的状态；included（附带）锁和车筐。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Now the price is only 350 yuan, much cheaper than a new one with the same quality.","note":"价格 + 和新车比价：much cheaper than… 广告的价格要有参照物。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"If you are interested, please call me at 139-XXXX-XXXX or visit Room 210, Dormitory Building 6, any evening this week.","note":"联系方式、地点、时间三齐全。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Hurry up — such a good bicycle will not wait long!","note":"will not wait long（不会等太久）拟人化催单收尾。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Bicycle for Sale — Almost New!","Do you want an easy way to travel around our large campus? I am selling the bicycle I used at college because I am graduating this summer. It is a Giant mountain bike, black and silver, with 21 speeds. It is light, strong and comfortable to ride, and it is suitable for both boys and girls.","The bicycle is in very good condition. I bought it one year ago for 900 yuan, and I have kept it carefully. The brakes and tyres are almost new, and the lock and basket are included. Now the price is only 350 yuan, much cheaper than a new one with the same quality.","If you are interested, please call me at 139-XXXX-XXXX or visit Room 210, Dormitory Building 6, any evening this week. Hurry up — such a good bicycle will not wait long!"],"id":"cam-r4","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an advertisement on your campus website to sell a bicycle you used at college. Your advertisement may include its brand, features, condition and price, and your contact information. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2017年6月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"广告：出售二手自行车","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2017},{"analysis":[{"en":"Used Books for Sale — A Chance You Cannot Miss!","note":"广告第一要素是标题：品名 + 一句吆喝，广告体和议论文完全不同，开头就要抓人。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Are you tired of paying high prices for new textbooks?","note":"问句开场直击痛点，Are you tired of… 是广告文案的经典句式。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"As a graduating senior, I am selling my used books at prices you will love.","note":"交代卖家身份（毕业生清仓），可信度立刻上来。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"All the books are in good condition, with careful notes written in class that may save you hours of review time.","note":"in good condition（品相好）是二手广告的准说法；把「有笔记」写成卖点而不是缺点，角度聪明。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The collection covers the main courses of the first two years, including English, advanced mathematics, computer science and economics.","note":"including 列出具体科目，买家一眼判断有没有自己要的——题目要的 content 描述就是这一句。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Most books are priced at only one third of the original price, and if you buy three or more, you will get an extra 10 percent off.","note":"价格和优惠必须写具体数字：one third、10 percent off——广告没有数字就没有说服力。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A set of CET-4 exercise books will be given free to the first five buyers.","note":"赠品 + 限量（first five）制造紧迫感，广告的促销手法。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Interested?","note":"短问句转入结尾的行动号召，广告节奏感。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Come to Room 302, Dormitory Building 5, any evening this week between 7 and 10, or contact me at 138-XXXX-XXXX.","note":"结尾必须留联系方式和时间地点，缺了这条广告就白写；电话用 XXXX 占位即可。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Books are limited, so hurry up — first come, first served!","note":"first come, first served（先到先得）是广告收尾的固定说法，背下来。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Used Books for Sale — A Chance You Cannot Miss!","Are you tired of paying high prices for new textbooks? As a graduating senior, I am selling my used books at prices you will love. All the books are in good condition, with careful notes written in class that may save you hours of review time.","The collection covers the main courses of the first two years, including English, advanced mathematics, computer science and economics. Most books are priced at only one third of the original price, and if you buy three or more, you will get an extra 10 percent off. A set of CET-4 exercise books will be given free to the first five buyers.","Interested? Come to Room 302, Dormitory Building 5, any evening this week between 7 and 10, or contact me at 138-XXXX-XXXX. Books are limited, so hurry up — first come, first served!"],"id":"cam-r5","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an advertisement on your campus website to sell some of the course books you used at college. Your advertisement may include a brief description of their content, their condition and price, and your contact information. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2017年6月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"广告：出售旧教材","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2017},{"analysis":[{"en":"How to best handle the relationship between doctors and patients is a question that concerns everyone.","note":"How to… 名词短语作主语，把题目原样变成第一句，concerns everyone 点出普遍性。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A good relationship brings trust and better treatment, while a bad one can lead to arguments and even harm.","note":"good / bad 对比 + while 连接：关系好坏的两种结果一句说清。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, both sides have a part to play.","note":"表态：both sides（双方都有责任）——关系类题目的基本立场，也预告了下文结构。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"For doctors, the key is respect and patience.","note":"For doctors / For patients 对称分段，先医生后患者，一边一句总起。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"They should explain illnesses in words that patients can understand, listen to their worries and never treat them as mere numbers.","note":"三个动作写医生该怎么做；treat them as mere numbers（把病人当数字）批评得具体。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"For patients, the key is trust and understanding.","note":"换到患者一边，key 换成 trust and understanding，和医生一边不重复。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Doctors work long hours under great pressure, and no doctor can cure every disease.","note":"先体谅医生（under great pressure 在高压下），再点明医学的限度——理解的前提。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"If patients respect medical knowledge and follow advice, treatment will go much more smoothly.","note":"follow advice（遵医嘱）准词；go smoothly（顺利进行）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Communication is the bridge between the two sides: honest talks can prevent most misunderstandings before they grow into conflicts.","note":"bridge 比喻收束两段；prevent…before…（在……之前预防）写出沟通的作用时机。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, a healthy doctor-patient relationship is built on trust, respect and communication.","note":"结尾把全文三个关键词收齐：信任、尊重、沟通。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"When both sides try to understand each other, hospitals will become warmer places for everyone.","note":"warmer places（更温暖的地方）收尾，从关系升到愿景。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["How to best handle the relationship between doctors and patients is a question that concerns everyone. A good relationship brings trust and better treatment, while a bad one can lead to arguments and even harm. In my view, both sides have a part to play.","For doctors, the key is respect and patience. They should explain illnesses in words that patients can understand, listen to their worries and never treat them as mere numbers. For patients, the key is trust and understanding. Doctors work long hours under great pressure, and no doctor can cure every disease. If patients respect medical knowledge and follow advice, treatment will go much more smoothly. Communication is the bridge between the two sides: honest talks can prevent most misunderstandings before they grow into conflicts.","In short, a healthy doctor-patient relationship is built on trust, respect and communication. When both sides try to understand each other, hospitals will become warmer places for everyone."],"id":"hea-r1","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay on how to best handle the relationship between doctors and patients. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2017年12月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"health","themeName":"健康","title":"如何处理医患关系","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2017},{"analysis":[{"en":"How to best handle the relationship between parents and children is a question for every family.","note":"和医患关系题同一开场：How to… 作主语把题目变成第一句。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"As children grow up, especially at college, the old way of getting along may no longer work, and both sides need to learn new ways.","note":"get along（相处）+ no longer work（不再管用），点出关系需要随成长更新。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Communication is the first key.","note":"三个 key 分层：沟通、尊重、空间与信任——关系类题目的通用骨架。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Parents and children should talk honestly and listen to each other, instead of giving orders or keeping silent.","note":"instead of 后面两个反面动作（下命令、冷战）把「不沟通」写具体。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Many conflicts come not from bad intentions, but from a lack of understanding.","note":"not from…but from…（不是源于……而是源于……）：不是坏心，是缺理解。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Respect is the second key.","note":"第二个 key 转到尊重。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Parents should respect their children as independent adults with their own choices, and children should respect the experience and love behind their parents' advice, even when they disagree.","note":"respect 两边对称写：父母尊重独立，子女尊重经验与爱；even when they disagree 留有分寸。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Finally, both sides should give each other space and trust.","note":"Finally 收第三个 key：空间和信任。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A phone call, a family trip or simply eating together can keep hearts close.","note":"三个最小的日常动作举例：电话、旅行、一起吃饭——建议要具体才可信。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, there is no perfect formula, but with communication, respect and trust, the relationship between parents and children can grow warmer as children grow up.","note":"结尾收齐三个 key；grow warmer / grow up 两个 grow 呼应收尾。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["How to best handle the relationship between parents and children is a question for every family. As children grow up, especially at college, the old way of getting along may no longer work, and both sides need to learn new ways.","Communication is the first key. Parents and children should talk honestly and listen to each other, instead of giving orders or keeping silent. Many conflicts come not from bad intentions, but from a lack of understanding. Respect is the second key. Parents should respect their children as independent adults with their own choices, and children should respect the experience and love behind their parents' advice, even when they disagree. Finally, both sides should give each other space and trust. A phone call, a family trip or simply eating together can keep hearts close.","In conclusion, there is no perfect formula, but with communication, respect and trust, the relationship between parents and children can grow warmer as children grow up."],"id":"soc-r3","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay on how to best handle the relationship between parents and children. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2017年12月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"如何处理亲子关系","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2017},{"analysis":[{"en":"How to best handle the relationship between teachers and students matters a lot in education.","note":"How to… 作主语点题，matter（重要）收句。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A good relationship makes learning pleasant and effective, while a poor one can turn the classroom into a cold and silent place.","note":"good / poor 对比：pleasant and effective ↔ cold and silent，两对词写出两种课堂。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, respect is the base of this relationship, and it works in both directions.","note":"总观点：尊重是 base（基础），且 in both directions（双向的）——预告下文两边都写。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Teachers should respect students as independent persons: listen to their questions, encourage different opinions and never laugh at their mistakes.","note":"冒号后三个动作写老师的尊重；laugh at（嘲笑）是老师最不该做的事。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Students, in return, should respect teachers' work: attend classes on time, listen carefully and finish homework honestly.","note":"in return（作为回报）对称写学生的尊重；on time、honestly 都是具体要求。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Beyond respect, communication is equally important.","note":"Beyond respect（除了尊重）引出第二点，equally（同样地）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"When teachers know what students truly think and students understand why teachers teach in a certain way, misunderstandings disappear and trust grows.","note":"When 从句里 what / why 两个从句对称：老师懂学生想什么，学生懂老师为什么这样教。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, the best teacher-student relationship is like that between guides and travellers: the guide leads the way, and both enjoy the journey of learning together.","note":"导游与旅人比喻收尾：leads the way（领路）+ journey of learning（学习之旅）。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["How to best handle the relationship between teachers and students matters a lot in education. A good relationship makes learning pleasant and effective, while a poor one can turn the classroom into a cold and silent place.","In my view, respect is the base of this relationship, and it works in both directions. Teachers should respect students as independent persons: listen to their questions, encourage different opinions and never laugh at their mistakes. Students, in return, should respect teachers' work: attend classes on time, listen carefully and finish homework honestly. Beyond respect, communication is equally important. When teachers know what students truly think and students understand why teachers teach in a certain way, misunderstandings disappear and trust grows.","In short, the best teacher-student relationship is like that between guides and travellers: the guide leads the way, and both enjoy the journey of learning together."],"id":"soc-r4","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay on how to best handle the relationship between teachers and students. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2017年12月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"如何处理师生关系","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2017},{"analysis":[{"en":"Reading ability plays an important role in our study and life.","note":"play an important role in（起重要作用）是「重要性」题的第一句万能句。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Good readers can understand books quickly, remember more, and learn new subjects with less effort.","note":"三个动词并列写阅读能力带来的具体好处，不空喊重要。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"That is why every student should pay attention to developing this ability.","note":"That is why… 承接上文，引出「所以要培养」的下文。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Then how can we develop our reading ability?","note":"自问自答开启方法段，和题目 how to develop 直接对应。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, we should read widely.","note":"First / Second / Finally 三个方法分层，阅卷一眼看清结构。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Newspapers, novels and science books train our minds in different ways.","note":"举例支撑「广泛」：三类读物并列，train our minds（锻炼思维）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, we should read actively instead of just moving our eyes over the words.","note":"move our eyes over the words（眼睛扫过文字）把「假阅读」写活了。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Asking questions, taking notes and thinking about the writer's purpose all help us understand more deeply.","note":"三个动名词并列作主语，写出「主动阅读」的具体动作。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Finally, practice matters most.","note":"短句强调最后一个方法最重要。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"If we keep reading for half an hour every day, our speed and understanding will improve step by step.","note":"给具体量（每天半小时）比空说「多练习」可信；step by step。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, reading ability is not a gift but a skill built by daily practice.","note":"not a gift but a skill（不是天赋而是技能），点出全文落点。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The sooner we start, the more we will gain from books throughout our life.","note":"the sooner…, the more… 句型收尾，越早开始收获越多。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Reading ability plays an important role in our study and life. Good readers can understand books quickly, remember more, and learn new subjects with less effort. That is why every student should pay attention to developing this ability.","Then how can we develop our reading ability? First, we should read widely. Newspapers, novels and science books train our minds in different ways. Second, we should read actively instead of just moving our eyes over the words. Asking questions, taking notes and thinking about the writer's purpose all help us understand more deeply. Finally, practice matters most. If we keep reading for half an hour every day, our speed and understanding will improve step by step.","In conclusion, reading ability is not a gift but a skill built by daily practice. The sooner we start, the more we will gain from books throughout our life."],"id":"edu-r6","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay on the importance of reading ability and how to develop it. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2018年6月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"阅读能力的重要性与培养","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2018},{"analysis":[{"en":"Writing ability is one of the most useful skills a student can have.","note":"one of the most useful skills… 定语从句，第一句先给写作能力定位。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It helps us express ideas clearly in exams, in reports and later in our jobs.","note":"express ideas clearly（清楚表达想法）；三个 in 短语从考试写到工作。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"A person who writes well is often a person who thinks clearly.","note":"两个 who 从句对仗：写得好的人，往往想得清楚——点出写作和思维的关系。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"To develop writing ability, the first step is reading.","note":"方法段用 the first/second/third step 分层，和阅读、说话两道同年真题是同一套骨架。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Good writing grows out of good reading: when we read fine articles, we naturally learn how sentences and paragraphs are built.","note":"grow out of（源于）比喻；how 从句写出从阅读里学到的具体东西。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The second step is practice.","note":"短句领起第二个方法，节奏干脆。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Keeping a diary, writing short essays and rewriting them after receiving advice can all improve our writing little by little.","note":"三个动名词并列写练习方式；little by little（一点点地）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The third step is thinking before writing.","note":"第三个方法先想后写，出乎意料但合理。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A clear outline makes an essay organized, and organized essays are always easier to read.","note":"outline（提纲）是写作话题的准词；organized 前后呼应。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In short, writing ability cannot be gained in a day, but with wide reading and regular practice, everyone can learn to write clearly and effectively.","note":"结尾收束两个核心方法（读 + 练），clearly and effectively 回扣开头。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Writing ability is one of the most useful skills a student can have. It helps us express ideas clearly in exams, in reports and later in our jobs. A person who writes well is often a person who thinks clearly.","To develop writing ability, the first step is reading. Good writing grows out of good reading: when we read fine articles, we naturally learn how sentences and paragraphs are built. The second step is practice. Keeping a diary, writing short essays and rewriting them after receiving advice can all improve our writing little by little. The third step is thinking before writing. A clear outline makes an essay organized, and organized essays are always easier to read.","In short, writing ability cannot be gained in a day, but with wide reading and regular practice, everyone can learn to write clearly and effectively."],"id":"edu-r7","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay on the importance of writing ability and how to develop it. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2018年6月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"写作能力的重要性与培养","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2018},{"analysis":[{"en":"Speaking ability matters more and more in modern society.","note":"matter（重要）比 is important 更简洁；more and more 点出趋势。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Whether we are giving a presentation, taking part in an interview or simply talking with foreign friends, the ability to speak clearly and confidently can help us greatly.","note":"Whether… 三个场景并列：做报告、面试、交朋友，重要性落到实处。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"How, then, can we develop this ability?","note":"then 插入问句，自然从「重要性」转到「怎么培养」。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First of all, we must open our mouths and not be afraid of making mistakes.","note":"open our mouths（开口）口语化又准确，是口语题最该写的一句。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Every fluent speaker was once a shy beginner.","note":"金句：每个流利的人都曾经是害羞的新手——鼓励句，背下来多题可用。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Second, we should create chances to speak: join an English corner, discuss in groups, or practise with classmates after class.","note":"冒号后三个具体做法；English corner（英语角）是校园准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Third, listening is the partner of speaking.","note":"partner 比喻：听是说的伙伴，一个方法带出另一个方法。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"By listening to news and speeches, we learn natural expressions and correct pronunciation, which make our own speaking better.","note":"natural expressions、pronunciation（发音）都是口语题的准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, speaking ability grows out of courage and practice.","note":"结尾把方法收成两个词：勇气 + 练习。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"If we speak a little every day, we will one day speak with ease and confidence.","note":"with ease and confidence（轻松自信地）收尾，呼应开头的 confidently。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Speaking ability matters more and more in modern society. Whether we are giving a presentation, taking part in an interview or simply talking with foreign friends, the ability to speak clearly and confidently can help us greatly.","How, then, can we develop this ability? First of all, we must open our mouths and not be afraid of making mistakes. Every fluent speaker was once a shy beginner. Second, we should create chances to speak: join an English corner, discuss in groups, or practise with classmates after class. Third, listening is the partner of speaking. By listening to news and speeches, we learn natural expressions and correct pronunciation, which make our own speaking better.","In conclusion, speaking ability grows out of courage and practice. If we speak a little every day, we will one day speak with ease and confidence."],"id":"edu-r8","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay on the importance of speaking ability and how to develop it. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2018年6月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"口语能力的重要性与培养","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2018},{"analysis":[{"en":"Starting a career after graduation is an exciting step, but it is also full of challenges.","note":"先扬后抑开场，和大城市、留学两道同年挑战题同一手法：一套卷三道挑战题共用骨架。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The world of work is very different from the campus, and every new graduate needs time to adapt to it.","note":"点出挑战的根源：职场 ≠ 校园；adapt to（适应）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The first challenge is the gap between theory and practice.","note":"the gap between theory and practice（理论与实践的差距）是职业题的核心表达，背下来。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"What we learned from books is often not enough for real tasks, and we must learn again from the very beginning.","note":"What 主语从句展开 gap；from the very beginning（从头学起）写新人的真实处境。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The second challenge is pressure and competition.","note":"第二个挑战换到强度层面。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"New workers have to prove themselves while facing heavy workloads and experienced colleagues, and mistakes at the start are hard to avoid.","note":"prove themselves（证明自己）、heavy workloads（繁重的工作量）都是职场准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The third challenge is finding one's direction.","note":"第三个挑战最深：direction（方向）——不知道自己适合什么。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Many graduates are not sure what job truly suits them, and changing jobs too often may waste their best years.","note":"suit（适合）+ waste their best years（浪费最好的年华），点出频繁跳槽的代价。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In my view, these challenges are normal and even necessary.","note":"结尾翻转：normal and even necessary（正常，甚至必要）——挑战题的经典收尾。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A career is a long road, and those who face the first difficulties patiently will grow into real professionals.","note":"a long road 比喻 + grow into（成长为）收尾：耐心熬过开头，就能成为真正的职业人。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Starting a career after graduation is an exciting step, but it is also full of challenges. The world of work is very different from the campus, and every new graduate needs time to adapt to it.","The first challenge is the gap between theory and practice. What we learned from books is often not enough for real tasks, and we must learn again from the very beginning. The second challenge is pressure and competition. New workers have to prove themselves while facing heavy workloads and experienced colleagues, and mistakes at the start are hard to avoid. The third challenge is finding one's direction. Many graduates are not sure what job truly suits them, and changing jobs too often may waste their best years.","In my view, these challenges are normal and even necessary. A career is a long road, and those who face the first difficulties patiently will grow into real professionals."],"id":"car-r4","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay on the challenges of starting a career after graduation. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2018年12月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"career","themeName":"职业规划","title":"毕业后开启职业生涯的挑战","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2018},{"analysis":[{"en":"Studying abroad is a dream for many students, but it is not an easy road.","note":"先扬后抑开场：是梦想，但路不好走——挑战类题目的标准起手。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Besides the excitement of a new country, students have to face many challenges that they may not expect.","note":"Besides… 引出兴奋之外的另一面；face challenges（面对挑战）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The first challenge is language.","note":"The first/second/third challenge 分层，挑战类题目最好用的骨架。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Even students who passed English exams may find it hard to follow lectures or express their ideas in daily life.","note":"Even…may… 写出反差：过了考试也未必听得懂课；follow lectures（跟上讲课）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The second challenge is loneliness.","note":"第二个挑战换到情感层面，和语言层面不重复。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Far from family and friends, they must cook, clean and solve every problem on their own, and homesickness often makes study harder.","note":"Far from… 开头；cook、clean 三个动词写独立生活；homesickness（思乡）准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The third challenge is cultural difference.","note":"第三个挑战升到文化层面，三个挑战层层递进。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Different food, customs and ways of thinking take time to get used to, and misunderstandings may happen at first.","note":"get used to（习惯于）；at first 点出只是初期困难。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In my view, these challenges are also chances to grow.","note":"结尾翻转：challenges 也是 chances，一词之差点题。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Students who overcome them return home more independent, more confident and with a wider view of the world.","note":"overcome（克服）；independent、confident、wider view 三个收获收尾。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Studying abroad is a dream for many students, but it is not an easy road. Besides the excitement of a new country, students have to face many challenges that they may not expect.","The first challenge is language. Even students who passed English exams may find it hard to follow lectures or express their ideas in daily life. The second challenge is loneliness. Far from family and friends, they must cook, clean and solve every problem on their own, and homesickness often makes study harder. The third challenge is cultural difference. Different food, customs and ways of thinking take time to get used to, and misunderstandings may happen at first.","In my view, these challenges are also chances to grow. Students who overcome them return home more independent, more confident and with a wider view of the world."],"id":"edu-r9","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay on the challenges of studying abroad. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2018年12月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"出国留学的挑战","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2018},{"analysis":[{"en":"Living in a big city is attractive to many young people, but it is full of challenges.","note":"先扬后抑：attractive（有吸引力）↔ full of challenges——挑战题的经典开场。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Behind the bright lights and busy streets, city life tests everyone who comes to build a future there.","note":"Behind…（在……背后）揭开繁华的另一面；tests（考验）用词有力。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The first challenge is the high cost of living.","note":"三个 challenge 分层：花钱、压力、孤独——大城市题的标配三点。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Rents, food and transport take most of a young person's salary, and buying a home seems almost impossible.","note":"cost of living 展开成三笔账；take most of（占去大半）写出钱紧。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The second challenge is pressure.","note":"第二个挑战转到节奏与竞争。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Work in big cities is fast and competitive; people work long hours, travel long distances every day and still worry about falling behind.","note":"competitive（竞争激烈的）；long hours / long distances 两个 long 对举 + falling behind（落后）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The third challenge is loneliness.","note":"第三个挑战落到情感：孤独。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Surrounded by millions of people, a newcomer may still know nobody, and homesickness can make the nights feel very long.","note":"Surrounded by millions（被数百万人包围）却 know nobody——反差写孤独，全篇最动人的一句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Still, challenges are the price of chances.","note":"结尾翻转：challenges 是 chances 的 price（代价）——和留学题的收尾同一手法。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Big cities offer better jobs, wider views and more choices.","note":"offer 三个好处并列，和挑战段对称。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Those who face the challenges bravely may find that the city slowly becomes their second home.","note":"second home（第二故乡）收尾：挑战熬过去，城市就成了家。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Living in a big city is attractive to many young people, but it is full of challenges. Behind the bright lights and busy streets, city life tests everyone who comes to build a future there.","The first challenge is the high cost of living. Rents, food and transport take most of a young person's salary, and buying a home seems almost impossible. The second challenge is pressure. Work in big cities is fast and competitive; people work long hours, travel long distances every day and still worry about falling behind. The third challenge is loneliness. Surrounded by millions of people, a newcomer may still know nobody, and homesickness can make the nights feel very long.","Still, challenges are the price of chances. Big cities offer better jobs, wider views and more choices. Those who face the challenges bravely may find that the city slowly becomes their second home."],"id":"soc-r5","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a short essay on the challenges of living in a big city. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2018年12月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"在大城市生活的挑战","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2018},{"analysis":[{"en":"Last Saturday, the Student Union organized a visit to a local farm for about eighty students, offering them a chance to get close to nature and learn about modern agriculture.","note":"导语段五要素齐全；offering 分词补目的，modern agriculture 点出参观的主题不只是玩。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The students arrived at the farm at nine in the morning and were warmly welcomed by the farmers.","note":"按时间线叙事，were welcomed 被动句是报道常用语态。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Guided by the farm manager, they visited greenhouses full of vegetables, watched machines working in the fields and learned how modern technology has changed traditional farming.","note":"Guided by… 分词开头；三个动词并列推进参观流程；how 从句点出学习点。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The most exciting part was hands-on experience: students picked strawberries, fed animals and even tried driving a small tractor under the farmers' guidance.","note":"hands-on experience（亲手体验）是活动报道的高频词；冒号后三个动作把高潮写具体。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Many said it was their first time to see where their food actually comes from.","note":"间接引语代替直接引语，换一种引述方式；where 从句收得自然。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The visit ended at four in the afternoon, with students returning tired but happy.","note":"with 短语收束行程，tired but happy 是活动报道的经典收尾状态。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It was widely agreed that the activity had broadened their horizons and deepened their respect for farmers and the land.","note":"It was widely agreed that… 报道式总结句；broaden horizons + respect 收尾点意义。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Last Saturday, the Student Union organized a visit to a local farm for about eighty students, offering them a chance to get close to nature and learn about modern agriculture.","The students arrived at the farm at nine in the morning and were warmly welcomed by the farmers. Guided by the farm manager, they visited greenhouses full of vegetables, watched machines working in the fields and learned how modern technology has changed traditional farming. The most exciting part was hands-on experience: students picked strawberries, fed animals and even tried driving a small tractor under the farmers' guidance. Many said it was their first time to see where their food actually comes from.","The visit ended at four in the afternoon, with students returning tired but happy. It was widely agreed that the activity had broadened their horizons and deepened their respect for farmers and the land."],"id":"cam-r6","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a news report to your campus newspaper on a visit to a local farm organized by your Student Union. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2019年6月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"新闻报道：学生会组织参观农场","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2019},{"analysis":[{"en":"Last Friday, the Student Union of our university organized a visit to a Hope elementary school in the countryside, and about fifty student volunteers took part in the activity.","note":"导语五要素齐全，和同年助老、农场两篇报道同一骨架——一套卷三篇报道共用格式。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The volunteers arrived at the school at nine in the morning and were warmly welcomed by the teachers and children.","note":"时间线推进 + 被动语态 welcomed，报道的常规写法。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"They brought books, schoolbags and sports goods as gifts, and then gave short lessons in English, music and painting.","note":"带的东西和教的课都列具体名词；sports goods（体育用品）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In the playground, volunteers played games with the children and taught them new songs.","note":"换场景（操场）再写一项活动，报道内容不单调。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"“I hope I can go to a university like yours one day,” said a ten-year-old girl, holding a new picture book in her arms.","note":"直接引语选孩子的一句梦想话，比大人的感想更动人；holding… 分词补画面。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"According to the Student Union, more visits will be organized in the future.","note":"According to… 交代后续安排的来源，新闻体的严谨。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The visit not only brought joy and help to the children, but also encouraged the volunteers to treasure their own study opportunities.","note":"not only…but also… 双向点意义：孩子得了快乐，志愿者学会珍惜——和助老篇同一收尾法。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Last Friday, the Student Union of our university organized a visit to a Hope elementary school in the countryside, and about fifty student volunteers took part in the activity.","The volunteers arrived at the school at nine in the morning and were warmly welcomed by the teachers and children. They brought books, schoolbags and sports goods as gifts, and then gave short lessons in English, music and painting. In the playground, volunteers played games with the children and taught them new songs. “I hope I can go to a university like yours one day,” said a ten-year-old girl, holding a new picture book in her arms.","According to the Student Union, more visits will be organized in the future. The visit not only brought joy and help to the children, but also encouraged the volunteers to treasure their own study opportunities."],"id":"cam-r7","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a news report to your campus newspaper on a visit to a Hope elementary school organized by your Student Union. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2019年6月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"新闻报道：参观希望小学","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2019},{"analysis":[{"en":"Last Sunday, the Student Union of our university organized a volunteer activity to assist elderly people in the neighboring community, and more than sixty student volunteers took part in it.","note":"新闻报道第一段是导语：时间、组织者、事件、规模五要素一句说全——这是真题应用文的核心格式。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Early in the morning, the volunteers arrived at the community in groups.","note":"第二段按时间推进，in groups 交代组织有序。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Some helped elderly people clean their homes and repair small electrical appliances, while others offered free health checks, measuring blood pressure and giving advice on daily health care.","note":"some…while others… 分工写活动内容；health checks、blood pressure 都是助老场景的准词。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In the community hall, several students performed songs and dances, bringing laughter to the old people who live alone.","note":"bringing laughter 分词补结果；who live alone 点出空巢老人的背景。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"“These young students are like our own grandchildren,” said Mrs. Zhang, an eighty-year-old resident, with a warm smile.","note":"直接引语 + 人物身份是新闻报道的标志写法，引语让报道有现场感；注意引语的标点格式。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"According to the Student Union, such activities will be held regularly in the future.","note":"According to… 交代消息来源，新闻体的严谨之处。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The event not only brought real help and happiness to the elderly, but also taught students the value of serving society.","note":"not only…but also… 收尾点意义：帮了老人，也教育了学生——报道结尾要点题升华。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Last Sunday, the Student Union of our university organized a volunteer activity to assist elderly people in the neighboring community, and more than sixty student volunteers took part in it.","Early in the morning, the volunteers arrived at the community in groups. Some helped elderly people clean their homes and repair small electrical appliances, while others offered free health checks, measuring blood pressure and giving advice on daily health care. In the community hall, several students performed songs and dances, bringing laughter to the old people who live alone. “These young students are like our own grandchildren,” said Mrs. Zhang, an eighty-year-old resident, with a warm smile.","According to the Student Union, such activities will be held regularly in the future. The event not only brought real help and happiness to the elderly, but also taught students the value of serving society."],"id":"soc-r6","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a news report to your campus newspaper on a volunteer activity organized by your Student Union to assist elderly people in the neighborhood. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2019年6月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"新闻报道：学生会助老志愿活动","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2019},{"analysis":[{"en":"Dear John,","note":"写给外国朋友的信，称呼用名字即可（题目没给名字时用常见名）——书信格式第一分。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I am glad to hear that you want to teach English in China.","note":"第一句回应对方的来意，是推荐信的标准开场。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Among all the cities I know, I recommend Chengdu most strongly, and I am sure you will love living and working there.","note":"recommend（推荐）是本题的题眼词；most strongly 语气明确，不含糊。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Chengdu is a great place for an English teacher.","note":"主体段总起：先从「对教英语的人好不好」切入，正对朋友的需求。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"There are many schools and language centres looking for foreign teachers, and the pay is good while the cost of living is much lower than in Beijing or Shanghai.","note":"先讲工作机会，再用 cost of living（生活成本）+ 比较级讲性价比——推荐城市要讲对方最关心的。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Life in Chengdu is famous for being slow and comfortable: people enjoy tea houses, delicious hot pot and pandas — the city is the home of giant pandas.","note":"be famous for（以……闻名）；hot pot、giant pandas 具体名词写出城市特色。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The local people are friendly and warm, and many young people are eager to practise English with you, so you will make friends quickly.","note":"最后讲人：eager to practise English（乐意练英语）对一位英语老师是额外的吸引力。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I hope this helps.","note":"结尾短句收束推荐内容。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"If you decide to come, write to me and I will help you get settled.","note":"get settled（安顿下来）地道；主动提出帮忙，信的温度出来了。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Looking forward to seeing you in China!","note":"Looking forward to… + 落款 Best wishes + Li Ming（不用真名），格式完整。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Dear John,","I am glad to hear that you want to teach English in China. Among all the cities I know, I recommend Chengdu most strongly, and I am sure you will love living and working there.","Chengdu is a great place for an English teacher. There are many schools and language centres looking for foreign teachers, and the pay is good while the cost of living is much lower than in Beijing or Shanghai. Life in Chengdu is famous for being slow and comfortable: people enjoy tea houses, delicious hot pot and pandas — the city is the home of giant pandas. The local people are friendly and warm, and many young people are eager to practise English with you, so you will make friends quickly.","I hope this helps. If you decide to come, write to me and I will help you get settled. Looking forward to seeing you in China!","Best wishes,","Li Ming"],"id":"cul-r4","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a letter to a foreign friend who wants to teach English in China. Please recommend a city to him. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2019年12月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"推荐信：请朋友来成都教英语","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2019},{"analysis":[{"en":"Dear Tom,","note":"称呼格式同推荐城市那封信——同年三封推荐信共用一套格式。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I am happy to hear that you want to learn Chinese.","note":"回应来意开场。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"If you ask me where to go, my answer is Beijing.","note":"If you ask me… 口语化的设问，推荐干脆利落。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"It is, in my opinion, the best place in China to learn our language.","note":"in my opinion 插入语 + the best place 总评，先给结论再讲理由。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"There are good reasons for this choice.","note":"总起句引出 First / Second / Third 三个理由。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, people in Beijing speak standard Mandarin, the same Chinese you hear on television and in textbooks, so what you learn in class can be used everywhere in daily life.","note":"standard Mandarin（标准普通话）是学中文话题的题眼词；so 引出「学了就能用」的实际好处。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, Beijing has many excellent language schools and universities with courses for foreigners at every level.","note":"at every level（各个级别都有）点出课程资源丰富。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Third, the city is full of chances to practise: you can chat with local people in parks, visit museums and watch Chinese plays.","note":"冒号后三个练习场景并列；be full of chances（充满机会）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Living in Beijing, you will be surrounded by the language and the culture behind it.","note":"be surrounded by（被……包围）写语言环境；the culture behind it 升一层：学的是语言背后的文化。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I hope you will come soon.","note":"结尾邀约收束。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Learning Chinese in Beijing will be an experience you never forget.","note":"an experience you never forget（难忘的经历）+ 落款 Best wishes + Li Ming，收尾完整。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Dear Tom,","I am happy to hear that you want to learn Chinese. If you ask me where to go, my answer is Beijing. It is, in my opinion, the best place in China to learn our language.","There are good reasons for this choice. First, people in Beijing speak standard Mandarin, the same Chinese you hear on television and in textbooks, so what you learn in class can be used everywhere in daily life. Second, Beijing has many excellent language schools and universities with courses for foreigners at every level. Third, the city is full of chances to practise: you can chat with local people in parks, visit museums and watch Chinese plays. Living in Beijing, you will be surrounded by the language and the culture behind it.","I hope you will come soon. Learning Chinese in Beijing will be an experience you never forget.","Best wishes,","Li Ming"],"id":"cul-r5","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a letter to a foreign friend who wants to learn Chinese. Please recommend a place to him. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2019年12月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"推荐信：去北京学中文","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2019},{"analysis":[{"en":"Dear Jack,","note":"称呼格式与同年另两封推荐信一致。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Since you want to study in China, I would like to recommend my own university to you.","note":"Since（既然）引出推荐对象：my own university——推荐自己的学校最有素材可写。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It may not be the most famous university in China, but I believe it is a place where you can truly learn and enjoy your life.","note":"先让步（不算最有名）再转折，推荐显得诚恳可信，不吹牛。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Our university has a long history and strong programmes in computer science and business, with many courses taught in English for international students.","note":"先讲学术：programmes（专业项目）、courses taught in English（英文授课）正对留学生的需求。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The teachers are kind and patient, and the library and laboratories are modern and open long hours.","note":"再讲人和设施：laboratories（实验室）、open long hours（开放时间长）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Life here is also convenient and friendly.","note":"also 转到生活层面，总起下句。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The campus is green and quiet, the food in the canteens is cheap and delicious, and there are many clubs where you can make Chinese friends and practise your Chinese.","note":"三个并列分句写生活：环境、食堂、社团——留学生最关心的三件事。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The university also offers scholarships to excellent international students.","note":"scholarships（奖学金）是推荐大学时很有分量的一条，别漏。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"I warmly welcome you to study here.","note":"结尾发出邀请，warmly（热忱地）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"If you come, I will be your first friend and guide on campus.","note":"your first friend and guide（第一个朋友和向导）+ 落款，信收得有人情味。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Dear Jack,","Since you want to study in China, I would like to recommend my own university to you. It may not be the most famous university in China, but I believe it is a place where you can truly learn and enjoy your life.","Our university has a long history and strong programmes in computer science and business, with many courses taught in English for international students. The teachers are kind and patient, and the library and laboratories are modern and open long hours. Life here is also convenient and friendly. The campus is green and quiet, the food in the canteens is cheap and delicious, and there are many clubs where you can make Chinese friends and practise your Chinese. The university also offers scholarships to excellent international students.","I warmly welcome you to study here. If you come, I will be your first friend and guide on campus.","Best wishes,","Li Ming"],"id":"cul-r6","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write a letter to a foreign friend who wants to study in China. Please recommend a university to him. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2019年12月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"推荐信：来我的大学留学","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2019},{"analysis":[{"en":"Making plans is of great importance in our study and life.","note":"第一句把题目原词 importance 换成 of great importance 直接点题。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A plan is like a map: it tells us where we are, where we want to go and how to get there.","note":"map 比喻 + 三个 where/how 并列：计划的作用一句说清——本主题优美句式原句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Without a plan, we may work hard but still go in circles.","note":"go in circles（原地打转）反面点题：没计划，努力也白费。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Plans help us in at least two ways.","note":"at least two ways 预告两层好处，结构先行。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, a good plan makes our goals clear and our time useful.","note":"第一层：目标清、时间值。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A student who plans his week knows what to do each day and seldom wastes time deciding where to start.","note":"举一类人的日常状态作证；waste time deciding（把时间浪费在纠结上）写得很真实。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, a plan helps us face difficulties calmly.","note":"第二层转到心态：calmly（镇定地）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"When we prepare for an exam step by step according to a plan, we feel less nervous, because we know we are ready.","note":"according to a plan（按计划）+ step by step；less nervous 是计划带来的底气。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Let me take myself as an example.","note":"题目说 give examples——take myself as an example（拿我自己举例）过渡自然。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Last term, I made a plan for English: twenty words a day and one listening practice each evening.","note":"例子必须带数字：twenty words a day——计划写得越具体越可信。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Three months later, my English had improved more than in the whole year before.","note":"Three months / the whole year before 时间对比收束例子：三个月胜过一年。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, success seldom comes by luck.","note":"结尾先破：seldom（很少）+ luck。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It comes to those who plan their steps and follow their plans with action.","note":"plan + follow with action（用行动执行）收尾：计划要配执行，正是本篇题眼。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Making plans is of great importance in our study and life. A plan is like a map: it tells us where we are, where we want to go and how to get there. Without a plan, we may work hard but still go in circles.","Plans help us in at least two ways. First, a good plan makes our goals clear and our time useful. A student who plans his week knows what to do each day and seldom wastes time deciding where to start. Second, a plan helps us face difficulties calmly. When we prepare for an exam step by step according to a plan, we feel less nervous, because we know we are ready. Let me take myself as an example. Last term, I made a plan for English: twenty words a day and one listening practice each evening. Three months later, my English had improved more than in the whole year before.","In short, success seldom comes by luck. It comes to those who plan their steps and follow their plans with action."],"id":"oth-r6","kind":"real","month":7,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay commenting on the importance of making plans. You can give one or two examples to illustrate your point. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2020年7月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"other","themeName":"其他","title":"做计划的重要性","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2020},{"analysis":[{"en":"There is a saying: “The best preparation for future is doing your best today.”","note":"名言题先引原话；注意原题就是 for future（不带 the），照抄原题不要自己加词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It tells us a simple truth: the future is not built in the future, but today.","note":"用一句话解释名言：not built in the future, but today——绕口令式的对照，正是这句名言的精髓。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I fully agree with it.","note":"短句表态，和终身学习那道名言题同一收尾法。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Everything we will have tomorrow grows out of what we do today.","note":"grow out of（从……中长出）比喻：明天的一切从今天长出来。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A student who dreams of a good university but plays games every day is only dreaming; a student who reads, practises and corrects mistakes today is truly preparing.","note":"分号对照两个学生：only dreaming（只是做梦）↔ truly preparing（真在准备）——全篇最有力的一句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The same is true in work and health.","note":"短句把话题从学习扩到工作和健康，例子面打开。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Small efforts today — saving a little money, exercising for half an hour, learning one new skill — seem unimportant, but over months and years they add up to a strong future.","note":"破折号里三个最小的今日努力并列；add up to（累积成）点出时间的力量。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"On the contrary, if we always wait for tomorrow, tomorrow will never be ready.","note":"On the contrary 反面收束：老等明天，明天永远不会准备好。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, the future belongs to those who prepare for it today.","note":"the future belongs to those who…（未来属于……的人）经典收尾句型。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Let us stop waiting and do our best right now, one day at a time.","note":"do our best 回扣名言原词；one day at a time（一次过好一天）作最后落点。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["There is a saying: “The best preparation for future is doing your best today.” It tells us a simple truth: the future is not built in the future, but today. I fully agree with it.","Everything we will have tomorrow grows out of what we do today. A student who dreams of a good university but plays games every day is only dreaming; a student who reads, practises and corrects mistakes today is truly preparing. The same is true in work and health. Small efforts today — saving a little money, exercising for half an hour, learning one new skill — seem unimportant, but over months and years they add up to a strong future. On the contrary, if we always wait for tomorrow, tomorrow will never be ready.","In short, the future belongs to those who prepare for it today. Let us stop waiting and do our best right now, one day at a time."],"id":"oth-r7","kind":"real","month":7,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay on the saying “The best preparation for future is doing your best today.” You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2020年7月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"other","themeName":"其他","title":"评论名言：做好今天就是为未来准备","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2020},{"analysis":[{"en":"The use of translation apps is becoming increasingly popular.","note":"题目给定的首句原样使用，不要改写、不要漏掉。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"With a phone in hand, people can translate words and sentences in seconds, and even talk with foreigners through these apps.","note":"in seconds（几秒内）写速度；even 递进到「和外国人对话」。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"It is no surprise that more and more people rely on them.","note":"It is no surprise that…（不足为奇）+ rely on（依赖），承接首句的 popular。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Translation apps bring us much convenience.","note":"主体段先讲好处，总起句简洁。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"When we travel abroad, they help us read menus, ask for directions and book rooms without knowing the local language.","note":"三个旅行场景并列：menus、directions、book rooms，全是实用准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"When we study, they give us meanings and pronunciations at once, which saves a lot of time.","note":"at once（立刻）+ which 从句点出省时间。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, these apps are not perfect.","note":"短句转入缺点，利弊对称。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Their translations are sometimes wrong, especially for long or difficult sentences, and blindly trusting them may cause misunderstandings.","note":"blindly（盲目地）+ cause misunderstandings（造成误解），缺点写得准。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Besides, if students use apps for all their homework, they may never learn the language themselves.","note":"Besides 补一个更深的缺点：代做作业会废掉自己的语言能力。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my opinion, translation apps are helpful tools, but they should be our assistants, not our masters.","note":"assistants / masters 对比：工具定位是科技作文的万能落点。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"We can use them to learn faster, yet we should still build our own language ability.","note":"build our own ability（建立自己的能力）收尾，落点回到人。","tag":"好词"}],"essay":["The use of translation apps is becoming increasingly popular. With a phone in hand, people can translate words and sentences in seconds, and even talk with foreigners through these apps. It is no surprise that more and more people rely on them.","Translation apps bring us much convenience. When we travel abroad, they help us read menus, ask for directions and book rooms without knowing the local language. When we study, they give us meanings and pronunciations at once, which saves a lot of time. However, these apps are not perfect. Their translations are sometimes wrong, especially for long or difficult sentences, and blindly trusting them may cause misunderstandings. Besides, if students use apps for all their homework, they may never learn the language themselves.","In my opinion, translation apps are helpful tools, but they should be our assistants, not our masters. We can use them to learn faster, yet we should still build our own language ability."],"id":"tech-r4","kind":"real","month":7,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay on the use of translation apps. You can start your essay with the sentence “The use of translation apps is becoming increasingly popular.” You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2020年7月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"翻译软件的使用","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2020},{"analysis":[{"en":"The use of PowerPoint is becoming increasingly popular in class.","note":"题目给定的首句，原样用作第一句——给定首句的题千万不要改写它。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In most classrooms today, teachers show slides instead of writing everything on the blackboard, and students seem to welcome this change.","note":"slides（幻灯片）是本题准词；instead of 和 blackboard 对比出新旧变化。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"PowerPoint brings clear benefits to teaching.","note":"主体段先讲好处，bring benefits to（给……带来好处）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"With pictures, videos and charts, difficult points become easier to understand and remember.","note":"With 三个名词并列写出 PPT 的具体优势：图、视频、图表。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"A lesson with slides is also more lively, which helps students stay focused.","note":"lively（生动的）+ stay focused（保持专注），课堂话题准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Besides, teachers can save the slides and share them after class, so students can review what they have learned.","note":"Besides 补一个好处：课后可复习；so 引出结果。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"However, PowerPoint has its problems too.","note":"However 转入坏处，利弊题的对称结构。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Some teachers put too many words on the slides and simply read them aloud, which makes the class boring.","note":"read them aloud（照着念）把「念 PPT」的毛病写具体了。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Students, busy copying the slides, may stop listening and thinking.","note":"插入语 busy copying… 写学生只顾抄不顾听，一句点出另一方的问题。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my opinion, PowerPoint is only a tool.","note":"结尾定位：只是工具——科技类作文的万能落点。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Used well, it makes learning easier; used badly, it turns a class into a reading show.","note":"Used well / used badly 对仗；reading show（朗读表演）讽刺到位。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"What matters most is still the teacher and the students.","note":"What 主语从句收尾：最重要的还是人和人。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["The use of PowerPoint is becoming increasingly popular in class. In most classrooms today, teachers show slides instead of writing everything on the blackboard, and students seem to welcome this change.","PowerPoint brings clear benefits to teaching. With pictures, videos and charts, difficult points become easier to understand and remember. A lesson with slides is also more lively, which helps students stay focused. Besides, teachers can save the slides and share them after class, so students can review what they have learned. However, PowerPoint has its problems too. Some teachers put too many words on the slides and simply read them aloud, which makes the class boring. Students, busy copying the slides, may stop listening and thinking.","In my opinion, PowerPoint is only a tool. Used well, it makes learning easier; used badly, it turns a class into a reading show. What matters most is still the teacher and the students."],"id":"edu-r10","kind":"real","month":9,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay on the use of PowerPoint (PPT) in class. You can start your essay with the sentence “The use of PowerPoint is becoming increasingly popular in class.” You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2020年9月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"课堂上使用 PPT","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2020},{"analysis":[{"en":"Online libraries are becoming increasingly popular.","note":"给定首句原样使用。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Instead of going to a building and searching through shelves, readers can now open a website and find the book they need within minutes.","note":"Instead of… 把新旧方式对照：跑楼翻架 vs 打开网站，within minutes 写速度。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"There are good reasons for this change.","note":"主体段总起：下面讲流行的原因。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, online libraries are convenient.","note":"First / Second / Third 三个优点分层，和 PPT、词典两道同年题同一骨架。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"They are open twenty-four hours a day, and readers can read at home, on a bus or anywhere with a phone.","note":"twenty-four hours a day 写「全天开放」；三个地点并列写「随时随地」。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, they offer far more books than a traditional library, including old and rare ones that are hard to find.","note":"far more（多得多）比较；rare（珍稀的）点出藏书优势。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Third, searching is easy: type a key word, and all related books appear at once.","note":"key word（关键词）+ at once（立刻），把搜索的易写具体。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Of course, online libraries cannot fully replace real ones.","note":"Of course 让步转折：不能完全取代——评论有分寸。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Reading on a screen for long is tiring, and a quiet reading room offers an atmosphere that a website cannot give.","note":"atmosphere（氛围）是实体图书馆不可替代的东西，用词准。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, online libraries are a great gift of the Internet age.","note":"gift（礼物）比喻定性，结尾先给总评价。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The wise choice is to use both kinds of libraries, each for its own strengths.","note":"落点是「两种都用、各取所长」，比二选一更成熟。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Online libraries are becoming increasingly popular. Instead of going to a building and searching through shelves, readers can now open a website and find the book they need within minutes.","There are good reasons for this change. First, online libraries are convenient. They are open twenty-four hours a day, and readers can read at home, on a bus or anywhere with a phone. Second, they offer far more books than a traditional library, including old and rare ones that are hard to find. Third, searching is easy: type a key word, and all related books appear at once. Of course, online libraries cannot fully replace real ones. Reading on a screen for long is tiring, and a quiet reading room offers an atmosphere that a website cannot give.","In conclusion, online libraries are a great gift of the Internet age. The wise choice is to use both kinds of libraries, each for its own strengths."],"id":"tech-r5","kind":"real","month":9,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay on online libraries. You can start your essay with the sentence “Online libraries are becoming increasingly popular.” You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2020年9月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"在线图书馆","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2020},{"analysis":[{"en":"Online dictionaries are becoming increasingly popular.","note":"给定首句原样使用。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In the past, students carried thick paper dictionaries everywhere; today, a dictionary app on the phone can do the same job, and often more.","note":"In the past / today 今昔对比；thick（厚厚的）一个词写出纸词典的笨重。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The popularity of online dictionaries is easy to explain.","note":"主体段总起：下面解释为什么流行。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"They are fast: type a word, and its meaning, pronunciation and example sentences appear in a second.","note":"冒号后一个动作写清「快」；meaning、pronunciation、example sentences 三样齐全。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"They are also rich, offering far more words and more detailed explanations than a paper dictionary of the same price.","note":"fast / rich 两个短形容词领起优点；offering 分词展开比较。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Besides, they can read the word aloud, which paper dictionaries can never do.","note":"read aloud（朗读）是电子词典独有的功能，which 从句点出对比。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, online dictionaries have a weakness.","note":"However 转入缺点，weakness（弱点）和前面的优点对称。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Because looking up words is so easy, some students check every new word and remember none of them.","note":"check every word / remember none 对比，把「查得勤、记得空」的毛病写透。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A dictionary should help us learn words, not replace our memory.","note":"help / replace 对比：词典是帮手不是记忆的替代品。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, online dictionaries are excellent tools for language learning.","note":"结尾定性：excellent tools，回扣工具定位。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Used wisely, they make every word we meet a chance to learn.","note":"Used wisely 分词开头；every word…a chance 把每个生词都说成学习机会，收尾积极。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Online dictionaries are becoming increasingly popular. In the past, students carried thick paper dictionaries everywhere; today, a dictionary app on the phone can do the same job, and often more.","The popularity of online dictionaries is easy to explain. They are fast: type a word, and its meaning, pronunciation and example sentences appear in a second. They are also rich, offering far more words and more detailed explanations than a paper dictionary of the same price. Besides, they can read the word aloud, which paper dictionaries can never do. However, online dictionaries have a weakness. Because looking up words is so easy, some students check every new word and remember none of them. A dictionary should help us learn words, not replace our memory.","In short, online dictionaries are excellent tools for language learning. Used wisely, they make every word we meet a chance to learn."],"id":"tech-r6","kind":"real","month":9,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay on online dictionaries. You can start your essay with the sentence “Online dictionaries are becoming increasingly popular.” You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2020年9月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"在线词典","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2020},{"analysis":[{"en":"Great changes have taken place in the way of education in recent years.","note":"take place（发生）+ in recent years，「变化」类题目的标准第一句。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In the past, students could only learn from teachers in classrooms and from printed books.","note":"先写过去的样子，和后面的 Today 对照——变化题必须有今昔对比。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Today, education has broken the limits of time and place.","note":"break the limits（打破限制）一句概括变化的本质。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The biggest change comes from the Internet.","note":"主体段先抓最大的变化来源：互联网。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Online courses allow students to learn from famous teachers in other cities and even other countries, and to study whenever they are free.","note":"allow sb to do；even（甚至）递进，从外市写到外国。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Learning has also become more active.","note":"also 引出第二个变化，短句领起。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Instead of only listening, students now discuss in groups, search for information and finish projects together.","note":"Instead of only listening 对比旧方式；三个动词并列写新方式。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Besides, education is no longer just for the young.","note":"no longer（不再）+ 第三个变化：教育不再只是年轻人的事。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Many adults return to online classes to improve their skills, which makes learning a lifelong habit.","note":"举例支撑；lifelong habit（终身习惯）点出深层变化。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, education is becoming more open, more flexible and more personal.","note":"三个 more… 并列总结变化方向，整齐好记。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"These changes give everyone more chances to learn, and they will surely shape the future of our society.","note":"shape the future（塑造未来）收尾，把话题升到社会层面。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Great changes have taken place in the way of education in recent years. In the past, students could only learn from teachers in classrooms and from printed books. Today, education has broken the limits of time and place.","The biggest change comes from the Internet. Online courses allow students to learn from famous teachers in other cities and even other countries, and to study whenever they are free. Learning has also become more active. Instead of only listening, students now discuss in groups, search for information and finish projects together. Besides, education is no longer just for the young. Many adults return to online classes to improve their skills, which makes learning a lifelong habit.","In conclusion, education is becoming more open, more flexible and more personal. These changes give everyone more chances to learn, and they will surely shape the future of our society."],"id":"edu-r11","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write on the topic Changes in the Way of Education. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2020年12月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"教育方式的变化","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2020},{"analysis":[{"en":"Great changes have taken place in the way of transportation.","note":"和教育、沟通两道同年题同一开场：take place + 题目原词——一套卷三道题可以共用骨架。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In the past, people travelled by slow trains and crowded buses, and a trip to another city could take a whole day.","note":"slow / crowded 两个形容词写旧交通的样子；a whole day 和下文 a few hours 对照。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Today, travel is faster and more comfortable than ever before.","note":"Today 转到现在，总评一句：更快更舒适。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"High-speed trains are the symbol of this change.","note":"high-speed trains（高铁）是中国语境最该写的变化；symbol（象征）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"They connect cities hundreds of kilometres apart within a few hours, making it possible to work in one city and live in another.","note":"hundreds of kilometres apart（相距几百公里）+ making it possible 分词补出「双城生活」的影响。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In cities, subways, shared bikes and ride-hailing apps give people many choices for every trip, short or long.","note":"subways、shared bikes、ride-hailing apps（网约车）三个城市出行准词并列。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Air travel, once a luxury, is now common for ordinary families.","note":"once a luxury（曾经是奢侈品）插入语，今昔对比一句完成。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"These changes have shortened distances and brought people closer.","note":"shorten distances（缩短距离）小结影响。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, they also bring problems, such as traffic jams in big cities and pressure on the environment.","note":"However 补问题面：traffic jams（堵车）+ 环境压力，评论才完整。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In conclusion, transportation is becoming faster, greener and smarter.","note":"三个比较级展望，和沟通题的收尾同一句型。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"These changes are quietly reshaping how we live, work and see the world.","note":"reshape（重塑）+ how 从句收尾，把变化升到生活方式层面。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Great changes have taken place in the way of transportation. In the past, people travelled by slow trains and crowded buses, and a trip to another city could take a whole day. Today, travel is faster and more comfortable than ever before.","High-speed trains are the symbol of this change. They connect cities hundreds of kilometres apart within a few hours, making it possible to work in one city and live in another. In cities, subways, shared bikes and ride-hailing apps give people many choices for every trip, short or long. Air travel, once a luxury, is now common for ordinary families. These changes have shortened distances and brought people closer. However, they also bring problems, such as traffic jams in big cities and pressure on the environment.","In conclusion, transportation is becoming faster, greener and smarter. These changes are quietly reshaping how we live, work and see the world."],"id":"soc-r7","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write on the topic Changes in the Way of Transportation. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2020年12月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"交通方式的变化","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2020},{"analysis":[{"en":"The way people communicate has changed greatly in recent years.","note":"第一句把题目原词 the way of communication 换成定语从句点题。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In the past, people wrote letters and waited weeks for a reply.","note":"先写过去：写信、等几周——和下一句形成速度对比。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Today, a message can reach anyone in the world in a second.","note":"weeks → a second，今昔对比一句完成，变化题的核心手法。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The Internet and smartphones are behind this change.","note":"be behind（是……背后的原因）引出变化的推手。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"With social apps, we can send texts, pictures and videos, make free video calls and talk in groups with friends in different cities at the same time.","note":"三个动词短语并列列新方式；at the same time 点出群聊的同时性。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Communication has become faster, cheaper and richer than ever before.","note":"三个比较级并列总结变化，整齐有力。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"However, the change also has a side we should notice.","note":"However 转入变化的另一面，评论不停留在夸新方式。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Because messages are so easy to send, people may talk more but think less, and face-to-face communication is slowly being replaced by screens.","note":"talk more but think less（说得多想得少）对仗；be replaced by screens 点出代价。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Family members at the same table sometimes chat online instead of talking to each other.","note":"餐桌场景举例，和 2013 年沟通题的信里写的是同一幅画面。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In conclusion, communication is becoming faster and easier, but its purpose never changes: to connect hearts.","note":"冒号点出沟通的本质：connect hearts（连接人心）——结尾升华。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"We should enjoy the new ways while keeping real conversation in our life.","note":"enjoy…while keeping… 收尾建议：享受新方式，也留住真对话。","tag":"好词"}],"essay":["The way people communicate has changed greatly in recent years. In the past, people wrote letters and waited weeks for a reply. Today, a message can reach anyone in the world in a second.","The Internet and smartphones are behind this change. With social apps, we can send texts, pictures and videos, make free video calls and talk in groups with friends in different cities at the same time. Communication has become faster, cheaper and richer than ever before. However, the change also has a side we should notice. Because messages are so easy to send, people may talk more but think less, and face-to-face communication is slowly being replaced by screens. Family members at the same table sometimes chat online instead of talking to each other.","In conclusion, communication is becoming faster and easier, but its purpose never changes: to connect hearts. We should enjoy the new ways while keeping real conversation in our life."],"id":"tech-r7","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write on the topic Changes in the Way of Communication. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2020年12月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"沟通方式的变化","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2020},{"analysis":[{"en":"Do violent video games lead to violence?","note":"题目原问作第一句，和同年另外两道科技题同一开场法。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"This question worries many parents and teachers.","note":"短句点出谁在担心，引出下文的讨论。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A growing body of research finds that violent games can make kids act aggressively in real life.","note":"a growing body of research（越来越多研究）转述题目给的参考说法；act aggressively（行为有攻击性）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In my view, the worry is reasonable, but games are not the only cause.","note":"表态有分寸：担心合理，但游戏不是唯一原因——辩证立场先立住。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"There is no doubt that violent games have a bad influence on some children.","note":"主体段先承认影响，on some children 限定范围，不把话说满。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Kids learn by copying, and a child who spends hours shooting in games may slowly see fighting as a normal way to solve problems.","note":"learn by copying（靠模仿学习）点出机制；see…as（把……看作）写出观念的改变。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Games also fill children's hearts with excitement instead of calm, which may make them lose their temper more easily.","note":"also 补第二个影响；lose their temper（发脾气）准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, millions of children play such games and never hurt anyone.","note":"However 用一个事实反驳绝对化结论：millions…never（几百万孩子从没伤过人）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Whether a game leads to violence depends on the child, the family and the guidance he receives.","note":"depends on 三个因素：孩子、家庭、引导——把结论落到条件上。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Children whose parents play and talk with them usually know clearly that games are not real life.","note":"whose 从句举例：有父母陪伴交流的孩子分得清游戏和现实。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, violent games can push some children toward violence, but they are not the whole story.","note":"结尾重申分寸：can push（可能推动）≠ 全部原因，not the whole story 地道。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Wise limits and warm guidance are the real answer.","note":"limits + guidance 两个对策词收尾：明智的限制、温暖的引导。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Do violent video games lead to violence? This question worries many parents and teachers. A growing body of research finds that violent games can make kids act aggressively in real life. In my view, the worry is reasonable, but games are not the only cause.","There is no doubt that violent games have a bad influence on some children. Kids learn by copying, and a child who spends hours shooting in games may slowly see fighting as a normal way to solve problems. Games also fill children's hearts with excitement instead of calm, which may make them lose their temper more easily. However, millions of children play such games and never hurt anyone. Whether a game leads to violence depends on the child, the family and the guidance he receives. Children whose parents play and talk with them usually know clearly that games are not real life.","In conclusion, violent games can push some children toward violence, but they are not the whole story. Wise limits and warm guidance are the real answer."],"id":"soc-r8","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay titled “Do violent video games lead to violence?” The statement given below is for your reference. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.\n题目给出的参考说法：A growing body of research finds that violent video games can make kids act aggressively in their real world relationships, causing an increase in violence.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2021年6月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"暴力电子游戏会导致暴力吗","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2021},{"analysis":[{"en":"Are people becoming addicted to technology?","note":"第一句直接用题目原问开场——命题作文把标题写成第一句，天然点题。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Many would say yes.","note":"短句先给一个倾向性回答，再展开论证。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Look around: on buses, in restaurants and even at family dinners, people are staring at their phones, unable to put them down.","note":"Look around 祈使句拉读者入场；三个地点并列 + unable to put them down（放不下）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"There are reasons to worry.","note":"主体段先讲「值得担心」的一面。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Studies claim that addiction to technology has the same effect on the brain as drug addiction.","note":"把题目给的参考说法用 claim 转述进来——参考说法就是让你用的素材。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Addicted people check their phones hundreds of times a day, feel anxious without them, and slowly lose interest in real life.","note":"hundreds of times（几百次）、feel anxious（焦虑）写出上瘾者的三个典型状态。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Short videos and games are designed to keep us watching, and many students waste hours that should be spent on study and sleep.","note":"be designed to（被设计成）点出产品在「钩」人；should be spent 本应用在学习睡眠上的时间。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"However, we should not blame technology itself.","note":"However 转入另一面：不怪科技本身——辩证是这类题的高分关键。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"For most people, phones are tools for work, study and connection, not drugs.","note":"tools / drugs 对比，回应参考说法里的 drug addiction。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The problem lies in how we use them and whether we can control ourselves.","note":"The problem lies in…（问题在于）点出真正的病根：自制力。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, technology addiction is real for some people, but it can be beaten.","note":"结尾表态有分寸：对一部分人是真的，但可以战胜。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Setting limits, turning off unnecessary messages and spending more time with real people will bring our life back under our own control.","note":"三个动名词并列给具体办法；under our own control 收尾呼应 control ourselves。","tag":"好词"}],"essay":["Are people becoming addicted to technology? Many would say yes. Look around: on buses, in restaurants and even at family dinners, people are staring at their phones, unable to put them down.","There are reasons to worry. Studies claim that addiction to technology has the same effect on the brain as drug addiction. Addicted people check their phones hundreds of times a day, feel anxious without them, and slowly lose interest in real life. Short videos and games are designed to keep us watching, and many students waste hours that should be spent on study and sleep. However, we should not blame technology itself. For most people, phones are tools for work, study and connection, not drugs. The problem lies in how we use them and whether we can control ourselves.","In my view, technology addiction is real for some people, but it can be beaten. Setting limits, turning off unnecessary messages and spending more time with real people will bring our life back under our own control."],"id":"tech-r8","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay titled “Are people becoming addicted to technology?” The statement given below is for your reference. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.\n题目给出的参考说法：Numerous studies claim that addiction to technology is real and it has the same effect on the brain as drug addiction.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2021年6月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"人们对科技上瘾了吗","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2021},{"analysis":[{"en":"Is technology making people lazy?","note":"用题目原问作第一句，和同年「上瘾」题同一开场法。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"With washing machines, delivery apps and smart tools doing more and more work for us, this question is worth thinking about.","note":"With 独立结构列出三样替我们干活的科技；worth thinking about（值得思考）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In my view, technology does make life easier, but whether it makes us lazy depends on ourselves.","note":"先表态：does 强调「确实让生活变易」，但懒不懒 depends on ourselves——辩证立场。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It is true that technology can encourage laziness.","note":"It is true that… 先让步承认一方，论证更可信。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Many studies claim that computers distract people, make them lazy thinkers and even lower their work efficiency.","note":"转述题目给的参考说法：distract、lazy thinkers、work efficiency 三个点全用上。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"When a search engine gives answers in seconds, some students stop thinking for themselves.","note":"When 从句给具体场景：秒出答案 → 不再自己想。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"When cars and elevators are everywhere, people walk less and less.","note":"第二个 When 场景换到身体层面；less and less 对举。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Yet technology can also make us more active and efficient.","note":"Yet 转入另一面，和前面的让步形成完整辩证。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Online courses push us to learn new skills, fitness apps remind us to exercise, and smart tools save time that we can spend on more meaningful work.","note":"三个例子并列反驳：网课、健身 App、智能工具；meaningful work 收得有高度。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, technology itself is neither good nor bad for our habits.","note":"neither…nor… 定性：科技对习惯无所谓好坏。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"It only offers choices; active people use it to grow, while lazy people use it to escape effort.","note":"active / lazy 两类人对比收尾：它只提供选择，用的人决定结果。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Is technology making people lazy? With washing machines, delivery apps and smart tools doing more and more work for us, this question is worth thinking about. In my view, technology does make life easier, but whether it makes us lazy depends on ourselves.","It is true that technology can encourage laziness. Many studies claim that computers distract people, make them lazy thinkers and even lower their work efficiency. When a search engine gives answers in seconds, some students stop thinking for themselves. When cars and elevators are everywhere, people walk less and less. Yet technology can also make us more active and efficient. Online courses push us to learn new skills, fitness apps remind us to exercise, and smart tools save time that we can spend on more meaningful work.","In conclusion, technology itself is neither good nor bad for our habits. It only offers choices; active people use it to grow, while lazy people use it to escape effort."],"id":"tech-r9","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"For this part, you are allowed 30 minutes to write an essay titled “Is technology making people lazy?” The statement given below is for your reference. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.\n题目给出的参考说法：Many studies claim that computers distract people, make them lazy thinkers and even lower their work efficiency.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2021年6月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"科技让人变懒了吗","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2021},{"analysis":[{"en":"Last month, our school carried out a project of collecting used books on campus.","note":"报告开场先交代项目和时间，carry out（开展）是项目报告的准词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"This report introduces the project's aim, organizers, participants and activities.","note":"预告四项 = 题目点名的四项，报告和提案共用这个开场骨架。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The aim of the project was to give old textbooks a second life and help junior students save money.","note":"a second life（第二次生命）把旧书回收的意义说活了；junior students（学弟学妹）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Instead of throwing away books or selling them as waste paper, senior students were encouraged to donate or sell them at low prices.","note":"Instead of… 对比旧做法（当废纸卖）；donate（捐赠）点出项目的公益面。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The project was organized by the student union and the library.","note":"organizers 一句交代，被动语态是报告的常规语态。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"More than two thousand students took part in it during the two weeks.","note":"participants 用数字写规模：two thousand、two weeks——报告靠数字说话。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Collection points were set up in every dormitory building, and volunteers sorted the books by subject and marked their prices.","note":"activities 写流程：set up（设立）收集点、sort by subject（按科目分类）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"A book fair was held on the last weekend, where over five thousand books found new owners.","note":"book fair（书展/书市）是活动高潮；found new owners（找到新主人）拟人化收束。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The project was a great success.","note":"结尾先给总评，报告的收尾习惯。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It saved resources, helped students and made reading more popular on our campus.","note":"三个动词并列总结成果，和开头的 aim 呼应。","tag":"好词"}],"essay":["Last month, our school carried out a project of collecting used books on campus. This report introduces the project's aim, organizers, participants and activities.","The aim of the project was to give old textbooks a second life and help junior students save money. Instead of throwing away books or selling them as waste paper, senior students were encouraged to donate or sell them at low prices. The project was organized by the student union and the library. More than two thousand students took part in it during the two weeks. Collection points were set up in every dormitory building, and volunteers sorted the books by subject and marked their prices. A book fair was held on the last weekend, where over five thousand books found new owners.","The project was a great success. It saved resources, helped students and made reading more popular on our campus."],"id":"cam-r10","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"Directions: Suppose you have just participated in a school project of collecting used books on campus. You are now to write a report about the project, which may include its aim, organizers, participants and activities. You will have 30 minutes to write the report. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2021年12月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"报告：校园旧书回收项目","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2021},{"analysis":[{"en":"To help the freshmen adapt to the new environment and academic studies, our school is planning an orientation program.","note":"提案开场用 To do 点明项目目的，直接套用题目原词 adapt to（适应）——提案第一分。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"This proposal introduces its aim, duration, participants and activities.","note":"一句预告全文结构，四个词正是题目点名要写的四项——阅卷人一眼看到你没漏项。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The aim of the program is to help new students know the campus, understand university study and make new friends, so that they can start their college life smoothly.","note":"aim 展开成三个 to do + so that 目的：熟悉校园、懂学习、交朋友。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The program will last five days, from September 1 to September 5, before the new term begins.","note":"duration 写具体日期，不写「几天」这种空话——提案的数字意识。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"All freshmen are required to take part, and teachers and senior students will work as guides.","note":"participants 一句交代：全体新生参加，老师和学长任向导。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The activities include a campus tour, lectures on how to use the library and choose courses, meetings with teachers, and group games.","note":"include 列四项活动；how to use the library 是新生最实用的内容。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"A welcome party will be held on the last evening.","note":"补一项收尾活动，被动语态 will be held 是活动文的常用说法。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"We believe this program will help freshmen feel at home quickly and get ready for their four years at university.","note":"结尾展望效果：feel at home（有归属感）+ get ready for 收束全篇。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["To help the freshmen adapt to the new environment and academic studies, our school is planning an orientation program. This proposal introduces its aim, duration, participants and activities.","The aim of the program is to help new students know the campus, understand university study and make new friends, so that they can start their college life smoothly. The program will last five days, from September 1 to September 5, before the new term begins. All freshmen are required to take part, and teachers and senior students will work as guides. The activities include a campus tour, lectures on how to use the library and choose courses, meetings with teachers, and group games. A welcome party will be held on the last evening.","We believe this program will help freshmen feel at home quickly and get ready for their four years at university."],"id":"cam-r8","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"Directions: Suppose your school is organizing an orientation program to help the freshmen adapt to the new environment and academic studies. You are now to write a proposal, which may include its aim, duration, participants and activities. You will have 30 minutes to write the proposal. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2021年12月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"提案：新生迎新项目","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2021},{"analysis":[{"en":"To improve students' English speaking ability and give them a stage to show themselves, the university student union is planning to hold an English speech contest.","note":"To do 开场点明办赛目的，和迎新提案同一开场法——提案文共用骨架。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"This proposal introduces the topic, aim, procedure and selection of contestants.","note":"预告四项正是题目点名的四项，一项不漏。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The topic of the contest is “My Dream”.","note":"topic 一句给出，短句干脆——提案不需要在这里抒情。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Its aim is to encourage students to think about their future and express their ideas in English with confidence.","note":"aim 展开：想未来 + 自信表达；with confidence（自信地）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The contest will be held in two rounds.","note":"procedure 先给总框架：two rounds（两轮）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In the first round, each contestant gives a three-minute prepared speech.","note":"three-minute、prepared speech（命题演讲）把赛制写具体。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The top twenty will enter the final, where they will also answer questions from the judges.","note":"the final（决赛）+ judges（评委）；where 从句补决赛的问答环节。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Contestants will be selected through class recommendations and an open sign-up, and students from all grades and majors are welcome.","note":"selection of contestants 用题目原词 contestants；两种选拔渠道 + 全体欢迎，写全了。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Winners will receive certificates and prizes.","note":"补奖励一句：certificates and prizes（证书和奖品），提案更完整。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"We hope this contest will light students' love for English and make our campus life richer.","note":"结尾展望：light（点燃）学生的英语热情收尾。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["To improve students' English speaking ability and give them a stage to show themselves, the university student union is planning to hold an English speech contest. This proposal introduces the topic, aim, procedure and selection of contestants.","The topic of the contest is “My Dream”. Its aim is to encourage students to think about their future and express their ideas in English with confidence. The contest will be held in two rounds. In the first round, each contestant gives a three-minute prepared speech. The top twenty will enter the final, where they will also answer questions from the judges. Contestants will be selected through class recommendations and an open sign-up, and students from all grades and majors are welcome. Winners will receive certificates and prizes.","We hope this contest will light students' love for English and make our campus life richer."],"id":"cam-r9","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"Directions: Suppose your university student union is planning to hold a speech contest. You are now to write a proposal for organizing the contest. The proposal may include the topic, aim, procedure and selection of contestants. You will have 30 minutes to write the proposal. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2021年12月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"提案：举办英语演讲比赛","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2021},{"analysis":[{"en":"This proposal is written to our school library for improving its service.","note":"开场点明提案对象和目的，improving its service 用题目原词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Although our library is a good place to study, there are still some problems that trouble students.","note":"Although 先肯定再提问题——给管理方提意见的得体说法。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I would like to describe the problems and offer possible solutions.","note":"预告结构：problems → solutions，正是题目要求的两部分。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The first problem is that seats are hard to find, especially before exams, because some students occupy seats with their books but do not return for hours.","note":"第一个问题写占座：occupy seats（占座）+ because 给原因——问题要写出现象和成因。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The second problem is that the library closes too early, at ten in the evening, which is not enough for students who study late.","note":"第二个问题写时间：at ten in the evening 给具体钟点，问题才可信。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The third problem is that some popular books have too few copies.","note":"第三个问题写藏书：too few copies（复本太少）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"To solve these problems, I suggest three measures.","note":"转入解决方案段，three measures 和三个问题一一对应——提案最重要的对称结构。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, set a rule that seats left empty for over one hour can be used by others.","note":"对策一对问题一：over one hour 给出可执行的标准，不空喊「禁止占座」。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, keep one reading room open until midnight during the exam weeks.","note":"对策二对问题二：until midnight、exam weeks 都是具体限定，方案显得经过思考。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Third, buy more copies of popular books and develop the digital library so that students can read online.","note":"对策三对问题三，还补了 digital library（数字图书馆）的新思路。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"I hope the library will consider these suggestions.","note":"结尾礼貌收束：consider（考虑）语气得体。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"With small changes, it will serve us even better.","note":"small changes 安抚对方（不用大动干戈）+ serve us better 展望收尾。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["This proposal is written to our school library for improving its service. Although our library is a good place to study, there are still some problems that trouble students. I would like to describe the problems and offer possible solutions.","The first problem is that seats are hard to find, especially before exams, because some students occupy seats with their books but do not return for hours. The second problem is that the library closes too early, at ten in the evening, which is not enough for students who study late. The third problem is that some popular books have too few copies. To solve these problems, I suggest three measures. First, set a rule that seats left empty for over one hour can be used by others. Second, keep one reading room open until midnight during the exam weeks. Third, buy more copies of popular books and develop the digital library so that students can read online.","I hope the library will consider these suggestions. With small changes, it will serve us even better."],"id":"cam-r11","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"Directions: Suppose you are going to write a proposal to your school library for improving its service. You are to write about its current problems and possible solutions to these problems. You will have 30 minutes to write the proposal. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2022年6月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"提案：改进图书馆服务","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2022},{"analysis":[{"en":"This proposal is written to our student union for enriching students' extracurricular activities.","note":"开场点明对象与目的，extracurricular activities 用题目原词——和图书馆提案同一开场。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"At present, many students spend most of their free time on phones in their dormitories.","note":"先写现状问题（宿舍刷手机），提案的必要性就出来了。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Richer activities will make campus life healthier and more interesting.","note":"一句总展望，承上启下。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I suggest organizing three kinds of activities.","note":"总起：three kinds 下面分体育、文化、志愿——题目问的 what 和 why 要一起答。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, sports activities, such as a campus running week and friendly ball games between classes, can help students build strong bodies and make friends.","note":"每类活动都是「例子 + 好处」的写法：such as 举例，can help 写 why——正面落实题目要求。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, cultural activities, such as singing contests, book-sharing meetings and film nights, can enrich our minds and discover hidden talents.","note":"enrich our minds（丰富精神）呼应 enriching；hidden talents（隐藏的才能）说法生动。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Third, volunteer activities, such as helping in the community and protecting the environment, can teach us responsibility while serving others.","note":"while serving others（在服务他人时）把志愿活动的意义点出来。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"These activities should be held regularly, and students should be allowed to choose freely according to their interests.","note":"补一条实施原则：regularly（定期）+ choose freely（自由选择），提案更完整。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I believe that with these activities, our spare time will become a valuable part of college life instead of wasted hours.","note":"valuable part ↔ wasted hours 对比收尾，回扣开头的「宿舍刷手机」。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["This proposal is written to our student union for enriching students' extracurricular activities. At present, many students spend most of their free time on phones in their dormitories. Richer activities will make campus life healthier and more interesting.","I suggest organizing three kinds of activities. First, sports activities, such as a campus running week and friendly ball games between classes, can help students build strong bodies and make friends. Second, cultural activities, such as singing contests, book-sharing meetings and film nights, can enrich our minds and discover hidden talents. Third, volunteer activities, such as helping in the community and protecting the environment, can teach us responsibility while serving others. These activities should be held regularly, and students should be allowed to choose freely according to their interests.","I believe that with these activities, our spare time will become a valuable part of college life instead of wasted hours."],"id":"cam-r12","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"Directions: Suppose you are going to write a proposal to your student union for enriching students' extracurricular activities. You are to write about what activities to organize and why. You will have 30 minutes to write the proposal. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2022年6月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"提案：丰富课外活动","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2022},{"analysis":[{"en":"This proposal is written to our school clinic for improving its service.","note":"开场点明对象与目的，和图书馆提案同一句型——同年三道提案题共用骨架。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The clinic is important to every student, but at present there are some problems that make students unhappy.","note":"先肯定重要性再提问题，提意见的得体顺序。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I would like to describe the problems and offer possible solutions.","note":"预告 problems → solutions 两段式结构。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The first problem is the long waiting time.","note":"三个问题：等太久、关门早、缺药——校医院最真实的三个槽点。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"When many students get sick, they may wait for more than an hour to see a doctor.","note":"more than an hour 用时间量化「久」，see a doctor（看医生）准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The second problem is that the clinic closes too early and is closed on weekends, so students who fall ill at night or on Saturday have to go to hospitals far away.","note":"fall ill（生病）+ so 引出后果：只能跑远路去医院。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The third problem is that some common medicines are often out of stock.","note":"out of stock（缺货、断货）是本题的题眼词组。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"To solve these problems, I suggest three measures.","note":"转入对策段，三条对三问，一一对应。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, add more doctors during busy seasons and let students book a time online.","note":"对策一：忙季加人 + book a time online（网上预约）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, keep the clinic open longer and arrange a doctor on duty at weekends.","note":"对策二：on duty（值班）是医院场景的准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Third, check medicine stocks every week and prepare enough common medicines in advance.","note":"对策三：in advance（提前）备药，对应 out of stock。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"I hope these suggestions will help the clinic serve students better and protect our health on campus.","note":"结尾展望收束，语气礼貌。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["This proposal is written to our school clinic for improving its service. The clinic is important to every student, but at present there are some problems that make students unhappy. I would like to describe the problems and offer possible solutions.","The first problem is the long waiting time. When many students get sick, they may wait for more than an hour to see a doctor. The second problem is that the clinic closes too early and is closed on weekends, so students who fall ill at night or on Saturday have to go to hospitals far away. The third problem is that some common medicines are often out of stock. To solve these problems, I suggest three measures. First, add more doctors during busy seasons and let students book a time online. Second, keep the clinic open longer and arrange a doctor on duty at weekends. Third, check medicine stocks every week and prepare enough common medicines in advance.","I hope these suggestions will help the clinic serve students better and protect our health on campus."],"id":"cam-r13","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"Directions: Suppose you are going to write a proposal to your school clinic for improving its service. You are to write about its current problems and possible solutions to these problems. You will have 30 minutes to write the proposal. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2022年6月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"提案：改进校医院服务","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2022},{"analysis":[{"en":"Last Saturday, our class held a special celebration for Teachers' Day.","note":"报告导语：时间 + 主办者（our class）+ 事件，hold a celebration（举办庆祝）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"This report introduces the activities organized by our class to thank our teachers.","note":"一句点明报告内容和目的（thank our teachers），对应题目要求写给校报。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The celebration began at three in the afternoon in our classroom, which we had decorated with flowers and balloons.","note":"活动叙事从时间地点起笔；decorate with（用……装饰）写出布置细节。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"First, our class monitor gave a short speech, thanking the teachers for their hard work and patience.","note":"class monitor（班长）；thank sb for（感谢某人做了……）是教师节的核心句型。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Then students presented gifts that we had made by hand, including cards with our best wishes and a big cake.","note":"First / Then / After that / At the end 四个时间词串起活动流程——活动报告的骨架；made by hand（手工做的）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"After that, we performed songs and a short play about our daily life with the teachers, which made everyone laugh and also moved our teachers deeply.","note":"perform（表演）+ made everyone laugh / moved…deeply（让大家笑、让老师感动），效果两面都写。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"At the end, each teacher shared a story from his or her own student days and encouraged us to study hard.","note":"结尾环节换老师发言，encourage sb to do 收束活动内容。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The celebration ended in warm applause.","note":"ended in warm applause（在热烈掌声中结束）是活动报道的经典收尾句。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"It was short but meaningful, bringing our class and our teachers much closer.","note":"short but meaningful 总评 + bringing…closer 点出活动拉近师生距离的意义。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Last Saturday, our class held a special celebration for Teachers' Day. This report introduces the activities organized by our class to thank our teachers.","The celebration began at three in the afternoon in our classroom, which we had decorated with flowers and balloons. First, our class monitor gave a short speech, thanking the teachers for their hard work and patience. Then students presented gifts that we had made by hand, including cards with our best wishes and a big cake. After that, we performed songs and a short play about our daily life with the teachers, which made everyone laugh and also moved our teachers deeply. At the end, each teacher shared a story from his or her own student days and encouraged us to study hard.","The celebration ended in warm applause. It was short but meaningful, bringing our class and our teachers much closer."],"id":"cam-r14","kind":"real","month":9,"prompt":"Directions: Suppose your class has just finished celebrating the Teacher's Day. You are now to write a report to the university newspaper on the celebration activities organized by your class. You will have 30 minutes to write the report. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2022年9月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"报告：班级教师节庆祝活动","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2022},{"analysis":[{"en":"Dear Mr. Wang,","note":"邀请信称呼：受邀人是学长，用 Mr. + 姓——邀请信的收信人是具体的人，不能用 Sir or Madam。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"On behalf of our class, I am writing to invite you to share your job experiences with the students of our class.","note":"On behalf of（代表）点明组织者身份，题目原词 on behalf of our class 原样用上；invite sb to do 点明写信目的。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"As one of our most successful former graduates, your experience will surely guide and encourage us greatly.","note":"As… 先夸对方（former graduates 往届毕业生）再讲邀请的意义——邀请信要让对方感到被重视。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The sharing activity will be held at 7 p.m. on Friday, October 14, in Room 301 of the Teaching Building.","note":"时间、地点写到分钟和房间号：will be held + 具体信息——邀请信缺了时间地点就等于没发。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"About sixty students will attend.","note":"补一句规模，让受邀人心里有数。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"We hope you can talk about how you found your first job, what difficulties you met at work and what advice you would give to students who are about to graduate.","note":"三个宾语从句列出希望对方讲的内容：找第一份工作、遇到的困难、给后辈的建议——邀请要讲清「请您讲什么」。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Your talk is expected to last about forty minutes, followed by questions from the students.","note":"时长和环节（talk + questions）交代清，方便对方准备；be expected to（预计）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"We would be honoured if you could accept our invitation.","note":"We would be honoured if…（若您能接受将不胜荣幸）是邀请信的礼貌高点句，背下来。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Please let us know if the time is convenient for you.","note":"留确认口：convenient（方便）——邀请信要等回复。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"We are looking forward to your coming.","note":"期待收尾 + 落款 Yours sincerely + Li Ming，格式完整。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Dear Mr. Wang,","On behalf of our class, I am writing to invite you to share your job experiences with the students of our class. As one of our most successful former graduates, your experience will surely guide and encourage us greatly.","The sharing activity will be held at 7 p.m. on Friday, October 14, in Room 301 of the Teaching Building. About sixty students will attend. We hope you can talk about how you found your first job, what difficulties you met at work and what advice you would give to students who are about to graduate. Your talk is expected to last about forty minutes, followed by questions from the students.","We would be honoured if you could accept our invitation. Please let us know if the time is convenient for you. We are looking forward to your coming.","Yours sincerely,","Li Ming"],"id":"car-r5","kind":"real","month":9,"prompt":"Directions: Suppose your class plans to invite some former graduates to share their job experiences with the students. As the organizer of the activity, you are now to write an invitation letter to the invited speakers on behalf of your class. You will have 30 minutes to write the letter. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2022年9月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"career","themeName":"职业规划","title":"邀请信：请毕业生回校分享求职经验","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2022},{"analysis":[{"en":"Dear Sir or Madam,","note":"写给学校但不知道具体收信人时，称呼用 Dear Sir or Madam——申请信的固定格式。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I am writing to apply to teach kids in remote rural areas during the coming vacation.","note":"第一句点明写信目的：apply to do（申请做某事）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"As a college student who grew up in the countryside myself, I know how much those children need good teachers and new knowledge.","note":"As… 引出自己的乡村背景——申请理由落在亲身经历上，最有说服力。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"There are several things I can do for the kids.","note":"主体段总起句，正面回答题目问的 what you can do。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, I can teach them English and mathematics, the two subjects they find hardest, using games and stories to make learning fun.","note":"同位语点明两门最难的课；using games and stories 写出教学方法，不空喊「我会教」。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, I can open their eyes to the outside world by sharing my college life and encouraging them to dream big.","note":"open their eyes to（让他们开眼界）+ dream big（敢做大梦）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Third, I am patient and good with children, and I can look after their safety and daily needs during the activity.","note":"be good with children（擅长和孩子相处）；look after（照顾）补上安全责任。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"I sincerely hope I can be chosen.","note":"结尾表态：sincerely（真诚地）+ 被动 be chosen。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I will work hard to give the children a meaningful and happy vacation.","note":"许下承诺再收尾，申请信不能只讲愿望。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Thank you for considering my application.","note":"感谢考虑 + 落款 Yours sincerely + Li Ming（不用真名）——书信格式完整。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Dear Sir or Madam,","I am writing to apply to teach kids in remote rural areas during the coming vacation. As a college student who grew up in the countryside myself, I know how much those children need good teachers and new knowledge.","There are several things I can do for the kids. First, I can teach them English and mathematics, the two subjects they find hardest, using games and stories to make learning fun. Second, I can open their eyes to the outside world by sharing my college life and encouraging them to dream big. Third, I am patient and good with children, and I can look after their safety and daily needs during the activity.","I sincerely hope I can be chosen. I will work hard to give the children a meaningful and happy vacation. Thank you for considering my application.","Yours sincerely,","Li Ming"],"id":"edu-r12","kind":"real","month":9,"prompt":"Directions: Suppose your university is selecting some students to teach kids in remote rural areas during the coming vacation. You are now to write an application letter to the university to explain why you want to take part and what you can do for the kids. You will have 30 minutes to write the letter. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2022年9月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"申请信：去偏远乡村支教","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2022},{"analysis":[{"en":"Physical exercise plays an important role in achieving success at college.","note":"第一句把题目原词 role、achieving success 全用上，play a role in 是本题的题眼搭配。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Many students think success only depends on hard study, but in fact a strong body is the base of all achievements.","note":"先破常见误解（只靠苦学），再立自己的观点：身体是 base（根基）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"First, exercise keeps us healthy and energetic.","note":"First / Second / Third 三层作用：身体、意志、社交。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Students who run, swim or play ball regularly get sick less often and can study longer without feeling tired.","note":"run、swim、play ball 三个运动并列；get sick less often（更少生病）把健康写成可感的结果。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, exercise trains our mind.","note":"短句转到第二层：锻炼意志，角度升级。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Sports teach us patience, courage and the spirit of never giving up, which are exactly the qualities needed to overcome difficulties in study.","note":"patience、courage、never giving up 三个品质；exactly 点出它们正是学习需要的。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Third, exercise is a good way to make friends and release pressure.","note":"release pressure（释放压力）是健康话题的核心词组。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"A game with classmates can clear our heads and help us return to our books in a better state.","note":"clear our heads（让头脑清醒）形象；return to our books 回到学习，呼应主题。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In conclusion, exercise is not a waste of study time; it is an investment in success.","note":"not a waste but an investment（不是浪费而是投资），回击「锻炼耽误学习」的说法。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Every college student should find a sport he or she loves and keep doing it.","note":"结尾给行动建议：找到一项喜欢的运动并坚持。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Physical exercise plays an important role in achieving success at college. Many students think success only depends on hard study, but in fact a strong body is the base of all achievements.","First, exercise keeps us healthy and energetic. Students who run, swim or play ball regularly get sick less often and can study longer without feeling tired. Second, exercise trains our mind. Sports teach us patience, courage and the spirit of never giving up, which are exactly the qualities needed to overcome difficulties in study. Third, exercise is a good way to make friends and release pressure. A game with classmates can clear our heads and help us return to our books in a better state.","In conclusion, exercise is not a waste of study time; it is an investment in success. Every college student should find a sport he or she loves and keep doing it."],"id":"hea-r2","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"In this task, you are to write an essay on the role of physical exercise in achieving success at college. You will have 30 minutes for the task. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2022年12月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"health","themeName":"健康","title":"体育锻炼对大学成功的作用","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2022},{"analysis":[{"en":"Developing a healthy lifestyle is of great importance for college students.","note":"动名词作主语 + of great importance，正面回应题目的 importance。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"After leaving home, many students eat irregularly, stay up late and seldom exercise, and their health quietly gets worse.","note":"三个坏习惯并列：eat irregularly（饮食不规律）、stay up late（熬夜）、seldom exercise，全是准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"It is time to take our lifestyle seriously.","note":"It is time to…（是时候……了）短句警醒，过渡到讲好处。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A healthy lifestyle brings at least three benefits.","note":"at least three benefits 预告结构：下面 First / Second / Third 一一对应。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, it gives us energy.","note":"第一个好处最短最直接：给精力。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Regular sleep and balanced meals keep our minds clear, so we can study more efficiently.","note":"regular sleep、balanced meals（均衡饮食）是健康题的标配词组；efficiently 回扣学习。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, it protects us from illness.","note":"第二个好处转到少生病，protect sb from（保护某人免于）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Small habits, such as drinking enough water and walking every day, build a strong body over time.","note":"such as 举两个最小的习惯；over time（久而久之）点出积累。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Third, a healthy lifestyle improves our mood.","note":"第三个好处升到情绪：身体 → 精力 → 心情，层层递进。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Students who exercise and rest well are usually more confident and less anxious, and they get along better with others.","note":"confident / anxious 对比 + get along better（相处更好），把心情的好处写满。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, health is the wealth we carry for life.","note":"health is the wealth（健康是财富）比喻收尾，金句好记。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"College students should start with small steps — sleep early, eat well and move more — and turn them into habits for a lifetime.","note":"破折号里三个最简动作（早睡、吃好、多动）；turn…into habits、for a lifetime 收束。","tag":"好词"}],"essay":["Developing a healthy lifestyle is of great importance for college students. After leaving home, many students eat irregularly, stay up late and seldom exercise, and their health quietly gets worse. It is time to take our lifestyle seriously.","A healthy lifestyle brings at least three benefits. First, it gives us energy. Regular sleep and balanced meals keep our minds clear, so we can study more efficiently. Second, it protects us from illness. Small habits, such as drinking enough water and walking every day, build a strong body over time. Third, a healthy lifestyle improves our mood. Students who exercise and rest well are usually more confident and less anxious, and they get along better with others.","In short, health is the wealth we carry for life. College students should start with small steps — sleep early, eat well and move more — and turn them into habits for a lifetime."],"id":"hea-r3","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"In this task, you are to write an essay on the importance of developing a healthy lifestyle among college students. You will have 30 minutes for the task. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2022年12月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"health","themeName":"健康","title":"大学生养成健康生活方式的重要性","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2022},{"analysis":[{"en":"Developing social skills is necessary for college students.","note":"第一句把题目原词 necessity 换成 necessary 直接表态。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"College is not only a place to gain knowledge; it is also a small society where we learn to work, live and grow with others.","note":"a small society（小社会）是大学话题的经典定位；三个动词并列写「和别人一起」。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Social skills matter in study first.","note":"主体段分两层：先校内学习，再毕业后，最后补生活——matter 反复作段首词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Group projects, class discussions and club activities all require students to communicate clearly, listen patiently and cooperate with different people.","note":"三个校园场景 + 三个社交动作并列，把 social skills 写具体。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Those who cannot express themselves often suffer even when they are hardworking.","note":"express themselves（表达自己）；even when 让步：再努力，不会表达也吃亏。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Social skills matter even more after graduation.","note":"even more 递进转入第二层：毕业后更重要。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Employers value teamwork and communication as much as professional knowledge, because almost every job is done with other people.","note":"value…as much as…（和……一样看重）+ because 给理由，论证完整。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Besides, good social skills make college life warmer: students who can build friendships enjoy more support and less loneliness.","note":"Besides 补第三层（生活）；more support / less loneliness 对比收束。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, social skills are not a talent for a few outgoing people; they can be learned and practised.","note":"结尾先破误解：不是少数外向者的天赋（outgoing 外向的），是人人可学的技能。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Every student should step out and grow them, starting today.","note":"step out（走出去）+ starting today 行动号召收尾。","tag":"好词"}],"essay":["Developing social skills is necessary for college students. College is not only a place to gain knowledge; it is also a small society where we learn to work, live and grow with others.","Social skills matter in study first. Group projects, class discussions and club activities all require students to communicate clearly, listen patiently and cooperate with different people. Those who cannot express themselves often suffer even when they are hardworking. Social skills matter even more after graduation. Employers value teamwork and communication as much as professional knowledge, because almost every job is done with other people. Besides, good social skills make college life warmer: students who can build friendships enjoy more support and less loneliness.","In short, social skills are not a talent for a few outgoing people; they can be learned and practised. Every student should step out and grow them, starting today."],"id":"soc-r9","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"In this task, you are to write an essay on the necessity of developing social skills for college students. You will have 30 minutes for the task. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2022年12月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"大学生培养社交能力的必要性","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2022},{"analysis":[{"en":"Last Wednesday, a famous scholar gave a lecture at our university on the future of artificial intelligence.","note":"导语交代时间、人物、主题，give a lecture（做讲座）+ 题目原词 famous scholar。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"This report summarizes the most important points of the lecture for our campus newspaper readers.","note":"点明报告任务：summarize（总结要点）——题目要求概括，就不能流水账复述全程。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The scholar began by pointing out that artificial intelligence is developing faster than most people expected, and it has already entered our study, work and daily life.","note":"began by pointing out（首先指出）是转述观点的准句式；要点一：发展超预期。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, he warned that AI is a tool, not a master.","note":"warned（提醒、警告）+ tool / master 对比：要点二最有分量的一句，短而有力。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"It can help us deal with information, but it cannot replace human creativity, feelings and judgement.","note":"展开要点二：can / cannot 对照；creativity、judgement（创造力、判断力）点名机器替代不了的东西。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"He also advised students not to fear AI, but to learn to work with it: whatever major we study, we should build the abilities that machines do not have, such as asking good questions and thinking independently.","note":"要点三是给学生的建议：advise sb not to…but to…；whatever major（无论什么专业）+ such as 两个机器没有的能力。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Finally, he expressed the hope that young people will use new technology responsibly.","note":"Finally 收最后一个要点：express the hope（表达希望）+ responsibly（负责任地）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The lecture lasted two hours and was warmly welcomed by the students.","note":"结尾补讲座的时长和反响，报道要素完整。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It helped us see both the chances and the limits of AI more clearly.","note":"chances / limits 两面总结：机会与限度都看清了——报道的总评收尾。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Last Wednesday, a famous scholar gave a lecture at our university on the future of artificial intelligence. This report summarizes the most important points of the lecture for our campus newspaper readers.","The scholar began by pointing out that artificial intelligence is developing faster than most people expected, and it has already entered our study, work and daily life. However, he warned that AI is a tool, not a master. It can help us deal with information, but it cannot replace human creativity, feelings and judgement. He also advised students not to fear AI, but to learn to work with it: whatever major we study, we should build the abilities that machines do not have, such as asking good questions and thinking independently. Finally, he expressed the hope that young people will use new technology responsibly.","The lecture lasted two hours and was warmly welcomed by the students. It helped us see both the chances and the limits of AI more clearly."],"id":"cam-r15","kind":"real","month":3,"prompt":"Directions: Suppose you have attended a lecture delivered by a famous scholar. Write a report to the campus newspaper, summarizing its most important points. You will have 30 minutes for this task and should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2023年3月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"讲座报道：著名学者的 AI 讲座","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2023},{"analysis":[{"en":"Last week, I took part in a career planning seminar held at our university.","note":"小结（account）开场先交代时间、事件：take part in + seminar（研讨会、讲座）用题目原词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Several guests from different companies shared their experiences, and I learned a lot from the seminar.","note":"一句预告全文两部分：讲了什么 + 我学到了什么——正对应题目的 account + summarize。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"This is an account of what happened and what I gained.","note":"再明说一句结构，阅卷人立刻知道你两问都答了。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"At the seminar, the guests first introduced the job situations in their industries and the abilities that companies value most, such as communication skills and a strong sense of responsibility.","note":"first / then 串讲座流程；a strong sense of responsibility（强烈的责任感）是企业最看重的品质，准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Then they answered students' questions about choosing a first job, preparing resumes and facing interviews.","note":"三个学生最关心的问题并列：resumes（简历）、interviews（面试）都是求职准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The most useful advice for me was this: a career is not decided in one day, so we should start planning early — know ourselves, know the market, and improve step by step.","note":"转入「我学到了什么」：冒号引出最有用的一条建议；know ourselves, know the market 对仗好记。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I also learned that a good resume should show real experience, and that internships during college are the best way to explore what job suits us.","note":"also 补第二条收获：internships（实习）+ explore what job suits us（摸清什么工作适合自己）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The seminar lasted two hours, but its influence on me will last much longer.","note":"last 两义双关：讲座持续两小时，影响持续更久——小结类文章的漂亮收尾。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"From now on, I will plan my career seriously instead of waiting until graduation.","note":"以行动承诺收尾：From now on（从现在起），呼应 start planning early。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Last week, I took part in a career planning seminar held at our university. Several guests from different companies shared their experiences, and I learned a lot from the seminar. This is an account of what happened and what I gained.","At the seminar, the guests first introduced the job situations in their industries and the abilities that companies value most, such as communication skills and a strong sense of responsibility. Then they answered students' questions about choosing a first job, preparing resumes and facing interviews. The most useful advice for me was this: a career is not decided in one day, so we should start planning early — know ourselves, know the market, and improve step by step. I also learned that a good resume should show real experience, and that internships during college are the best way to explore what job suits us.","The seminar lasted two hours, but its influence on me will last much longer. From now on, I will plan my career seriously instead of waiting until graduation."],"id":"car-r6","kind":"real","month":3,"prompt":"Directions: Suppose you have taken part in a career planning seminar. Write an account of the seminar and summarize what you have learned from it. You will have 30 minutes for this task and should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2023年3月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"career","themeName":"职业规划","title":"职业规划讲座小结","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2023},{"analysis":[{"en":"Hello, fellow members of our book club.","note":"论坛帖开场先向读书会成员打招呼，fellow members（各位同好）——场合对了，格式分就有了。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Today I would like to recommend a book that moved me deeply: The Little Prince, written by the French writer Antoine de Saint-Exupéry.","note":"第一段完成题目第一问「介绍这本书」：书名 + 作者 + 一句总评（moved me deeply 深深打动我）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It looks like a children's book, but it is truly a book for adults.","note":"looks like…but… 一句制造反差，是这本书最好的介绍语。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The book tells the story of a little prince who travels from planet to planet and finally comes to Earth.","note":"tell the story of…（讲述……的故事）概括情节；from planet to planet 写旅行线。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Through his eyes, we see how strange the adult world is: people chase numbers, power and business, but forget love, friendship and responsibility.","note":"Through his eyes（透过他的眼睛）；chase（追逐）vs forget 两组三词对比，点出书的主题。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The language of the book is simple and beautiful, and many lines are worth reading again and again.","note":"再夸语言：simple and beautiful；be worth reading（值得读）用上题目原词 worth。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"One of them says that what is essential is invisible to the eye — a sentence I have never forgotten since I first read it.","note":"引一句书中最有名的话作证据：what is essential is invisible to the eye（重要的东西用眼睛看不见）——荐书帖引原句最加分。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"This book is worth reading because it reminds us of the child we once were.","note":"正面回答题目第二问 why it is worth reading：remind us of（让我们想起）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I strongly recommend it to every member, and I look forward to discussing it with you.","note":"结尾发出讨论邀请，符合论坛帖的互动场合。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Hello, fellow members of our book club. Today I would like to recommend a book that moved me deeply: The Little Prince, written by the French writer Antoine de Saint-Exupéry. It looks like a children's book, but it is truly a book for adults.","The book tells the story of a little prince who travels from planet to planet and finally comes to Earth. Through his eyes, we see how strange the adult world is: people chase numbers, power and business, but forget love, friendship and responsibility. The language of the book is simple and beautiful, and many lines are worth reading again and again. One of them says that what is essential is invisible to the eye — a sentence I have never forgotten since I first read it.","This book is worth reading because it reminds us of the child we once were. I strongly recommend it to every member, and I look forward to discussing it with you."],"id":"cul-r7","kind":"real","month":3,"prompt":"Directions: Suppose you have read a book recently and intend to recommend it to other members of your book club via an online forum. Briefly introduce the book and explain why it is worth reading. You will have 30 minutes for this task and should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2023年3月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"读书会荐书：《小王子》","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2023},{"analysis":[{"en":"In response to the university's survey on online classes, I would like to share my opinions.","note":"In response to…（回应……）点明这是调查回复，开门见山。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Online classes have clear advantages, but they also have disadvantages that should not be ignored.","note":"第一段就把题目要的 advantages 和 disadvantages 两个词都点到，结构预告。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The biggest advantage is flexibility.","note":"flexibility（灵活性）一个词概括网课最大优点。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Students can learn anytime and anywhere, and they can watch the recordings again when a point is not clear.","note":"anytime and anywhere 对举；recordings（录播）是网课的准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Online classes also save the time of travelling between classrooms.","note":"also 补一个小优点：省通勤时间，具体可感。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, the disadvantages are just as clear.","note":"just as（同样）转入缺点段，和优点段分量对称。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Without a teacher watching, some students are easily distracted by phones and games.","note":"Without… 状语写前提；be distracted by（被……分心）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Besides, staring at a screen for hours is tiring for the eyes, and students have fewer chances to discuss with teachers and classmates face to face.","note":"stare at a screen（盯着屏幕）动名词作主语；face to face 点出网课缺的东西。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"To improve online classes, I suggest shorter lessons with more questions and discussions, so that students stay active.","note":"最后一段正面回答题目第三问 improvements：建议 + so that 目的。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Teachers could also give small quizzes during class to check understanding.","note":"quizzes（小测）建议具体可执行，不是空喊「加强管理」。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"With such improvements, online classes will become a truly helpful way of learning.","note":"With such improvements… 收尾展望，回应开头。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["In response to the university's survey on online classes, I would like to share my opinions. Online classes have clear advantages, but they also have disadvantages that should not be ignored.","The biggest advantage is flexibility. Students can learn anytime and anywhere, and they can watch the recordings again when a point is not clear. Online classes also save the time of travelling between classrooms. However, the disadvantages are just as clear. Without a teacher watching, some students are easily distracted by phones and games. Besides, staring at a screen for hours is tiring for the eyes, and students have fewer chances to discuss with teachers and classmates face to face.","To improve online classes, I suggest shorter lessons with more questions and discussions, so that students stay active. Teachers could also give small quizzes during class to check understanding. With such improvements, online classes will become a truly helpful way of learning."],"id":"edu-r13","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"Suppose your university is conducting a survey to collect students' opinions of online classes. You are to write a response to the survey about their advantages and disadvantages, and what improvements can be made. You will have 30 minutes for the task. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2023年6月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"网课的利弊与改进（调查回复）","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2023},{"analysis":[{"en":"The student union is organizing an online discussion on interpersonal relationships.","note":"第一句复述题目背景（学生会组织线上讨论），点明写作场合。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"As a college student, I believe that maintaining a warm and friendly relationship with classmates is both important and learnable.","note":"表态用题目原词 warm and friendly；learnable（可以学会的）预告下文要讲方法。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"There are several ways to build such a relationship.","note":"总起句对应题目第一问 ways；下面 First / Second / Third。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, be sincere and kind.","note":"方法一是态度：sincere and kind（真诚友善），祈使句简洁。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A true smile, a helping hand with notes or homework, and remembering a classmate's name all make people feel respected.","note":"三个最小的具体动作举例：微笑、帮忙、记名字——关系题写细节最加分。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, learn to listen and communicate.","note":"方法二转到沟通。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"When disagreements appear, talk calmly instead of arguing or giving the silent treatment.","note":"the silent treatment（冷处理、冷战）地道；talk calmly（ calmly 平静地）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Third, respect differences.","note":"方法三最短：尊重差异。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Classmates come from different places with different habits; understanding them instead of judging them keeps friendships alive.","note":"understanding / judging 对比；keep friendships alive（让友谊长青）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Such a relationship brings great benefits: study becomes easier with partners to discuss with, difficulties feel lighter with friends to share them, and college life becomes a warm memory instead of a lonely journey.","note":"一段末尾集中回答题目第二问 benefits：三个 with 短语并列，warm memory ↔ lonely journey 对比收束本段。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, warm relationships are built by small acts of kindness every day.","note":"结尾回扣方法：small acts of kindness（小小的善举）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Let us start with a smile and a greeting, and make our class a second family.","note":"Let us… 号召收尾；second family（第二个家）呼应 warm。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["The student union is organizing an online discussion on interpersonal relationships. As a college student, I believe that maintaining a warm and friendly relationship with classmates is both important and learnable.","There are several ways to build such a relationship. First, be sincere and kind. A true smile, a helping hand with notes or homework, and remembering a classmate's name all make people feel respected. Second, learn to listen and communicate. When disagreements appear, talk calmly instead of arguing or giving the silent treatment. Third, respect differences. Classmates come from different places with different habits; understanding them instead of judging them keeps friendships alive. Such a relationship brings great benefits: study becomes easier with partners to discuss with, difficulties feel lighter with friends to share them, and college life becomes a warm memory instead of a lonely journey.","In short, warm relationships are built by small acts of kindness every day. Let us start with a smile and a greeting, and make our class a second family."],"id":"soc-r10","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"Suppose the student union of your university is organizing an online discussion on interpersonal relationships. You are to write an essay on ways to maintain a warm and friendly relationship with your classmates and on the benefits of such a relationship. You will have 30 minutes for the task. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2023年6月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"与同学保持温暖友好的关系（线上讨论）","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2023},{"analysis":[{"en":"Our student union is organizing an online discussion on college students doing community service.","note":"复述题目背景开场，和同年人际关系题同一写法。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my view, community service benefits both the community and the students themselves, and every student can find a way to serve.","note":"表态预告结构：both…（对社区和对学生两边都有好处）正是下文的展开顺序。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The benefits are clear.","note":"短句领起好处段，正面回答题目第一问 benefits。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"For the community, student volunteers bring energy and knowledge: they help elderly people, teach children and keep public places clean.","note":"For the community / For students 对称分边写；冒号后三个动作列志愿服务。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"For students, service is a living classroom.","note":"a living classroom（活课堂）比喻：服务本身就是一堂课。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"It teaches responsibility, patience and teamwork, and helps us understand society beyond textbooks.","note":"三个品质并列；beyond textbooks（课本之外）点出服务的教育意义。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"As for me, I can provide several services.","note":"As for me（至于我）转到题目第二问：我能提供什么服务。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I can teach English and computer skills to children in the community on weekends, help old people learn to use smartphones, and join environmental activities such as sorting rubbish and planting trees.","note":"三个 I can 并列把服务写具体到科目和人群；sorting rubbish、planting trees 都是现成素材。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, community service turns young students into responsible citizens.","note":"turn…into…（把……变成……）收尾升华：从学生到 responsible citizens（负责任的公民）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I will start this weekend, and I hope more classmates will join.","note":"以自己的行动承诺收尾，比空喊口号可信。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Our student union is organizing an online discussion on college students doing community service. In my view, community service benefits both the community and the students themselves, and every student can find a way to serve.","The benefits are clear. For the community, student volunteers bring energy and knowledge: they help elderly people, teach children and keep public places clean. For students, service is a living classroom. It teaches responsibility, patience and teamwork, and helps us understand society beyond textbooks. As for me, I can provide several services. I can teach English and computer skills to children in the community on weekends, help old people learn to use smartphones, and join environmental activities such as sorting rubbish and planting trees.","In conclusion, community service turns young students into responsible citizens. I will start this weekend, and I hope more classmates will join."],"id":"soc-r11","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"Suppose the student union of your university is organizing an online discussion on college students doing community service. You are to write an essay on its benefits and the service you can provide to the community. You will have 30 minutes for the task. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2023年6月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"大学生做社区服务（线上讨论）","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2023},{"analysis":[{"en":"For the coming edition of our university newspaper, I would like to write about the campus event that has impressed me most: the school sports meeting held last month.","note":"投稿开场交代场合，冒号直接给出选定的活动——impressed 用题目原词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It was only two days long, but it left me with memories I will never forget.","note":"only two days 与 never forget 对比：时间短、印象深。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"What impressed me most was not the results, but the spirit behind them.","note":"What 主语从句 + not…but… 点出本段角度：打动我的是精神不是成绩。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In the 3,000-metre race, a runner from our class fell behind and was almost the last one, yet the whole class ran to the fence, shouting his name until he reached the finish line.","note":"一个具体场景写满全段：fall behind（落后）、shouting his name、finish line——细节是记叙文的命。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"He did not win a medal, but he finished the race, and we were prouder of him than of any champion.","note":"prouder…than of any champion（比为任何冠军都更自豪），情感高潮句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"That day I understood that a sports meeting is not only about being faster or stronger; it is about never giving up and never running alone.","note":"从一件事悟出道理：never giving up、never running alone（从不独自奔跑）双 never 收束本段。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"This event impressed me because it showed the best side of our class: courage, friendship and unity.","note":"结尾收三个词：courage、friendship、unity（勇气、友谊、团结）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"I will remember it for a long time.","note":"短句收尾，回扣 impressed。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["For the coming edition of our university newspaper, I would like to write about the campus event that has impressed me most: the school sports meeting held last month. It was only two days long, but it left me with memories I will never forget.","What impressed me most was not the results, but the spirit behind them. In the 3,000-metre race, a runner from our class fell behind and was almost the last one, yet the whole class ran to the fence, shouting his name until he reached the finish line. He did not win a medal, but he finished the race, and we were prouder of him than of any champion. That day I understood that a sports meeting is not only about being faster or stronger; it is about never giving up and never running alone.","This event impressed me because it showed the best side of our class: courage, friendship and unity. I will remember it for a long time."],"id":"cam-r16","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"Suppose the university newspaper is inviting submissions from the students for its coming edition on a campus event that has impressed them most. You are now to write an essay for submission. You will have 30 minutes to write the essay. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2023年12月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"印象最深的校园活动：校运会（校报投稿）","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2023},{"analysis":[{"en":"Asked what in my university impresses me most, many would expect me to name a famous building or a great teacher.","note":"Asked… 分词开头直接带入题目问题；先写别人以为的答案，为转折蓄势。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"But my answer is our library at night.","note":"短句揭晓答案：不选建筑本身，选「夜晚的图书馆」——切口小而新。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It is not the library itself that moves me most; it is the people in it.","note":"强调句 It is not…that… 再点深一层：打动我的是人不是楼。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Every evening, the library is full of students reading, writing and preparing for their dreams.","note":"三个动名词并列写晚自习图景；preparing for their dreams 一句升华。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Some are freshmen practising English words, some are seniors working on their theses, and some are students like me who simply enjoy the quiet.","note":"Some…some…some… 三类人并列：新生、毕业生、和我；theses（毕业论文）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Nobody talks loudly, yet the air is full of energy.","note":"安静与能量并存的反差句：the air is full of energy（空气里满是劲头）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"When I feel tired or want to give up, I look around at these hardworking faces, and strength quietly comes back to me.","note":"写图书馆对自己的作用：strength comes back（力量回来了），个人感受让文章有温度。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The library at night shows me what a university truly is: a place where young people grow together toward the future.","note":"冒号给出对大学的定义收束本段：grow together（一起成长）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"That is why the night library impresses me most.","note":"That is why… 回扣题目原词 impresses。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It is a building of books, but more than that, it is a home of dreams.","note":"a building of books / a home of dreams 对仗收尾，投稿文的好结尾。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Asked what in my university impresses me most, many would expect me to name a famous building or a great teacher. But my answer is our library at night. It is not the library itself that moves me most; it is the people in it.","Every evening, the library is full of students reading, writing and preparing for their dreams. Some are freshmen practising English words, some are seniors working on their theses, and some are students like me who simply enjoy the quiet. Nobody talks loudly, yet the air is full of energy. When I feel tired or want to give up, I look around at these hardworking faces, and strength quietly comes back to me. The library at night shows me what a university truly is: a place where young people grow together toward the future.","That is why the night library impresses me most. It is a building of books, but more than that, it is a home of dreams."],"id":"cam-r17","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"Suppose the university newspaper is inviting submissions from the students for its coming edition on what in their university impresses them most. You are now to write an essay for submission. You will have 30 minutes to write the essay. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2023年12月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"大学里最打动我的：夜晚的图书馆（校报投稿）","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2023},{"analysis":[{"en":"For the coming edition of our university newspaper, I would like to write about the recent development in my hometown.","note":"投稿文开场交代场合，recent development 用题目原词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In the past few years, this small town has changed so much that I almost could not recognize it last winter.","note":"so…that… + could not recognize（认不出来了）用个人感受写变化之大。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The most visible change is transportation.","note":"主体段先抓最显眼的变化（visible 看得见的）：交通。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A new high-speed railway station has been built, and the trip to the provincial capital now takes only forty minutes instead of three hours.","note":"forty minutes / three hours 数字对比，变化立刻可感；provincial capital（省会）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Roads have been widened, and shared bikes can be seen everywhere.","note":"被动语态写建设成果（have been widened 已被拓宽），报道感强。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Life has also become more convenient.","note":"also 转到第二个方面：生活便利。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A new hospital and a big library have opened, old streets have been repaired with lights and trees, and people can pay for almost everything with their phones.","note":"三个并列分句列变化：医院图书馆、老街改造、手机支付——投稿写细节最重要。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Behind these changes, farmers sell their fruit online to the whole country, and young people who once left for big cities are returning to start small businesses.","note":"Behind these changes 再挖一层：人的变化（农民网上卖果、青年返乡创业），比只写建筑深刻。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I am proud of my hometown's development.","note":"结尾表情感：be proud of（为……自豪）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It is becoming modern without losing its warmth, and I believe its best days are still ahead.","note":"modern without losing its warmth（变现代而不失温情）+ best days are still ahead（好日子还在后头）收尾。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["For the coming edition of our university newspaper, I would like to write about the recent development in my hometown. In the past few years, this small town has changed so much that I almost could not recognize it last winter.","The most visible change is transportation. A new high-speed railway station has been built, and the trip to the provincial capital now takes only forty minutes instead of three hours. Roads have been widened, and shared bikes can be seen everywhere. Life has also become more convenient. A new hospital and a big library have opened, old streets have been repaired with lights and trees, and people can pay for almost everything with their phones. Behind these changes, farmers sell their fruit online to the whole country, and young people who once left for big cities are returning to start small businesses.","I am proud of my hometown's development. It is becoming modern without losing its warmth, and I believe its best days are still ahead."],"id":"soc-r12","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"Suppose the university newspaper is inviting submissions from the students for its coming edition on the recent development in their hometown. You are now to write an essay for submission. You will have 30 minutes to write the essay. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2023年12月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"家乡的新发展（校报投稿）","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2023},{"analysis":[{"en":"Our university is seeking students' opinions on whether university libraries should be open to the public.","note":"复述征求意见的背景开场，whether 从句带出问题——同年三道「是否开放」题共用开场。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my view, they should be open, but in a planned and limited way.","note":"表态带限定：赞成，但要 planned and limited（有计划、有限度）——有条件的支持比单纯赞成更成熟。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Opening university libraries to the public has clear benefits.","note":"主体段先讲好处，动名词短语作主语。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Books and reading rooms belong to society in a sense, and many citizens, especially those who love reading but live far from public libraries, can benefit from them.","note":"belong to society（属于社会）+ in a sense（在某种意义上）留分寸；benefit from（从……受益）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"It also helps universities serve the local community and build a learning society.","note":"also 补一个社会层面的好处：a learning society（学习型社会）是政策热词，用上加分。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, we must also see the problems.","note":"However 转入问题面，利弊对称。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"University libraries are built first for students and teachers.","note":"短句立原则：first for（首先是为……）——后面所有让步的根基。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"If too many visitors come, seats and books will become even harder to get, and the quiet study environment may be damaged.","note":"If 从句推演具体后果：座位、书、安静环境三样受损。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Therefore, I suggest opening the libraries at set times, such as weekends and holidays, with visitors booking in advance and using limited areas.","note":"给出折中方案：set times（固定时段）、book in advance（提前预约）、limited areas（限定区域）——观点题有方案才完整。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, sharing is a good idea, but it should not disturb the students the libraries were built for.","note":"结尾重申原则：sharing 好，但不能 disturb 本主。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A limited opening can satisfy both sides.","note":"satisfy both sides（两边都满意）一句收尾，呼应 limited。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Our university is seeking students' opinions on whether university libraries should be open to the public. In my view, they should be open, but in a planned and limited way.","Opening university libraries to the public has clear benefits. Books and reading rooms belong to society in a sense, and many citizens, especially those who love reading but live far from public libraries, can benefit from them. It also helps universities serve the local community and build a learning society. However, we must also see the problems. University libraries are built first for students and teachers. If too many visitors come, seats and books will become even harder to get, and the quiet study environment may be damaged. Therefore, I suggest opening the libraries at set times, such as weekends and holidays, with visitors booking in advance and using limited areas.","In conclusion, sharing is a good idea, but it should not disturb the students the libraries were built for. A limited opening can satisfy both sides."],"id":"cam-r18","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"Suppose your university is seeking students' opinions on whether university libraries should be open to the public. You are now to write an essay to express your view. You will have 30 minutes for the task. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2024年6月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"大学图书馆该向公众开放吗","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2024},{"analysis":[{"en":"Our university is seeking students' opinions on whether university sports facilities should be open to the public.","note":"复述背景开场，和图书馆题同一句型，只换设施名。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I support the idea, as long as students' needs are protected first.","note":"support + as long as（只要）条件：学生优先——表态带前提。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Sports facilities in universities are often empty during holidays and weekday mornings, while many citizens around the campus have no good place to exercise.","note":"while 对比供需两端：一边闲置、一边没地方——开放的理由一句说清。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Opening the facilities can make full use of them and help local people stay healthy, which also builds a friendly relationship between the university and the community.","note":"make full use of（充分利用）是本题题眼；再升一层到校社关系。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Of course, opening brings problems too.","note":"Of course 让步转入问题，和图书馆题的 However 换个说法避免重复。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"More visitors mean more wear on the equipment, higher costs and possible safety risks.","note":"三个问题并列：wear（损耗）、costs、safety risks（安全风险），名词化表达显正式。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Besides, students must always come first: if the playground is crowded with visitors, students will have nowhere to play.","note":"come first（排第一位）重申原则；冒号后给具体后果。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, I suggest opening the facilities at fixed times with online booking, and charging a small fee for maintenance.","note":"方案三件套：固定时段、网上预约、收维护费（maintenance 维护）——比图书馆题的方案多了收费一条，因设施不同而变。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In this way, both the public and the students can benefit.","note":"In this way… 收尾：双赢结论。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Our university is seeking students' opinions on whether university sports facilities should be open to the public. I support the idea, as long as students' needs are protected first.","Sports facilities in universities are often empty during holidays and weekday mornings, while many citizens around the campus have no good place to exercise. Opening the facilities can make full use of them and help local people stay healthy, which also builds a friendly relationship between the university and the community. Of course, opening brings problems too. More visitors mean more wear on the equipment, higher costs and possible safety risks. Besides, students must always come first: if the playground is crowded with visitors, students will have nowhere to play.","In short, I suggest opening the facilities at fixed times with online booking, and charging a small fee for maintenance. In this way, both the public and the students can benefit."],"id":"cam-r19","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"Suppose your university is seeking students' opinions on whether university sports facilities should be open to the public. You are now to write an essay to express your view. You will have 30 minutes for the task. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2024年6月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"大学体育设施该向公众开放吗","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2024},{"analysis":[{"en":"Our university is seeking students' opinions on whether university canteens should be open to the public.","note":"复述背景开场，同年第三次使用——同一套卷的姐妹题就该这样复用句型。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Unlike libraries and sports facilities, canteens are directly connected with students' daily meals, so I hold a more careful view: they should not be fully open.","note":"Unlike… 先和另外两道题划清界限（食堂关乎一日三餐），再亮出更谨慎的立场——三道题立场各不同，阅卷人看得出你审题了。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"There are reasons for my view.","note":"短句预告理由段。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"University canteens enjoy government support and serve students at low prices.","note":"先讲食堂的特殊性：government support（政府补贴）+ low prices——反对全开的根基。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"If they are opened to the public, large numbers of visitors will come for cheap and tasty food, and students may have to wait in long lines or even find no seats at busy hours.","note":"If 从句推演后果：排长队、没座位；at busy hours（高峰时段）具体。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Food safety is another worry: more people from outside make management harder.","note":"another worry 补食品安全：food safety 是食堂话题的必备词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, a complete ban is not necessary either.","note":"However 再让步：全关也没必要——立场是「有限开放」不是「一刀切」。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Parents visiting their children and guests of the university should be welcome to eat with students.","note":"举出该欢迎的两类人（家长、来宾），让步有对象不空泛。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"My suggestion is limited opening: visitors can use one special canteen or eat at set times with a guest card.","note":"方案：专用食堂 / 固定时段 / guest card（访客卡），和图书馆题的方案同中有异。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, canteens should serve students first.","note":"结尾重申原则：serve students first。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A small, well-managed opening is acceptable, but a full opening would do more harm than good.","note":"do more harm than good（弊大于利）收尾，成语式表达加分。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Our university is seeking students' opinions on whether university canteens should be open to the public. Unlike libraries and sports facilities, canteens are directly connected with students' daily meals, so I hold a more careful view: they should not be fully open.","There are reasons for my view. University canteens enjoy government support and serve students at low prices. If they are opened to the public, large numbers of visitors will come for cheap and tasty food, and students may have to wait in long lines or even find no seats at busy hours. Food safety is another worry: more people from outside make management harder. However, a complete ban is not necessary either. Parents visiting their children and guests of the university should be welcome to eat with students. My suggestion is limited opening: visitors can use one special canteen or eat at set times with a guest card.","In conclusion, canteens should serve students first. A small, well-managed opening is acceptable, but a full opening would do more harm than good."],"id":"cam-r20","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"Suppose your university is seeking students' opinions on whether university canteens should be open to the public. You are now to write an essay to express your view. You will have 30 minutes for the task. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2024年6月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"大学食堂该向公众开放吗","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2024},{"analysis":[{"en":"Our university newspaper is inviting students to write about how to enrich our knowledge of traditional Chinese culture.","note":"复述投稿主题开场，enrich our knowledge 用题目原词组。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"As young Chinese, we should know our own culture well, yet many of us know far less about it than we think.","note":"yet 转出问题：far less than we think（比我们以为的少得多）——先指出差距，建议才有必要。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Here are some ways that work.","note":"短句预告方法段，that work（行得通的）显出实在。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, read the classics.","note":"三个方法用祈使句领起：读经典、访古迹、亲体验——投稿文的建议要干脆。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Books such as The Analects and classical poems are the roots of our culture, and reading even a little of them each week will deepen our understanding.","note":"The Analects（《论语》）具体书名；roots（根）比喻；even a little 降低门槛，建议更可执行。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, visit museums and historical places.","note":"第二个方法从书本走向实地。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Standing before real objects and old buildings, we can feel history in a way that pictures in textbooks cannot give.","note":"Standing before… 分词开头；real objects 与 pictures 对比，写出实地感。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Third, take part in cultural activities: learn calligraphy, join a traditional festival celebration, or watch Peking opera.","note":"calligraphy（书法）、Peking opera 具体文化名词并列——文化题靠具体取胜。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Culture becomes ours when we experience it with our own hands and hearts.","note":"with our own hands and hearts（亲手亲身）点出体验的意义。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Traditional culture is not something old and distant; it is the root of who we are.","note":"结尾破除距离感：not old and distant，而是 the root of who we are（我们身份的根）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Let us start learning it seriously, and pass it on with pride.","note":"pass it on（传承下去）+ with pride 收尾，号召有力。","tag":"好词"}],"essay":["Our university newspaper is inviting students to write about how to enrich our knowledge of traditional Chinese culture. As young Chinese, we should know our own culture well, yet many of us know far less about it than we think. Here are some ways that work.","First, read the classics. Books such as The Analects and classical poems are the roots of our culture, and reading even a little of them each week will deepen our understanding. Second, visit museums and historical places. Standing before real objects and old buildings, we can feel history in a way that pictures in textbooks cannot give. Third, take part in cultural activities: learn calligraphy, join a traditional festival celebration, or watch Peking opera. Culture becomes ours when we experience it with our own hands and hearts.","Traditional culture is not something old and distant; it is the root of who we are. Let us start learning it seriously, and pass it on with pride."],"id":"cul-r8","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"Suppose the university newspaper is inviting submissions from the students for its coming edition on how to enrich students' knowledge of traditional Chinese culture. You are now to write an essay for submission. You will have 30 minutes to write the essay. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2024年12月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"丰富传统文化知识（校报投稿）","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2024},{"analysis":[{"en":"Our university newspaper is inviting students to write about how we can contribute to a green campus.","note":"第一句复述投稿背景，contribute to（为……作贡献）用上题目原词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"As students who live and study here, we can do a lot, often in small ways that cost nothing.","note":"先立场：能做的很多，而且 cost nothing（不花钱）——打消「环保很麻烦」的顾虑。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"First, we can save resources in daily life.","note":"First / Second / Third 三个行动分层：省资源、添绿色、传理念。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Turning off lights when leaving a room, using both sides of paper and taking shorter showers all reduce waste.","note":"三个动名词并列全是具体小事：随手关灯、双面用纸、缩短洗澡——环境题要写细节。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, we can make the campus greener in a real sense: join tree-planting activities, protect the grass and trees we already have, and sort our rubbish so that more of it can be recycled.","note":"in a real sense（真正意义上）区分口号与行动；sort rubbish（垃圾分类）、be recycled 准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Third, we can spread the idea.","note":"第三层从自己做到影响别人，行动升级。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"When we ride bikes instead of taking cars, refuse plastic bags and remind our roommates to save water, green habits slowly become the habit of the whole campus.","note":"When 从句列三个带头动作；green habits → the habit of the whole campus，个人习惯变集体习惯。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A green campus is not built by slogans but by daily actions.","note":"not by slogans but by daily actions（不靠口号靠行动），结尾点题句，背下来。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"If every student does a small part, our campus will become cleaner, healthier and more beautiful.","note":"does a small part（出一份小力）+ 三个比较级展望收尾。","tag":"好词"}],"essay":["Our university newspaper is inviting students to write about how we can contribute to a green campus. As students who live and study here, we can do a lot, often in small ways that cost nothing.","First, we can save resources in daily life. Turning off lights when leaving a room, using both sides of paper and taking shorter showers all reduce waste. Second, we can make the campus greener in a real sense: join tree-planting activities, protect the grass and trees we already have, and sort our rubbish so that more of it can be recycled. Third, we can spread the idea. When we ride bikes instead of taking cars, refuse plastic bags and remind our roommates to save water, green habits slowly become the habit of the whole campus.","A green campus is not built by slogans but by daily actions. If every student does a small part, our campus will become cleaner, healthier and more beautiful."],"id":"env-r1","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"Suppose the university newspaper is inviting submissions from the students for its coming edition on how the students can contribute to a green campus. You are now to write an essay for submission. You will have 30 minutes to write the essay. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2024年12月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"environment","themeName":"环境","title":"为绿色校园作贡献（校报投稿）","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2024},{"analysis":[{"en":"In response to the business school's survey, I would like to share my views on the express delivery service industry in China.","note":"In response to… 点明调查回复的场合，题目原词 express delivery service industry 全带上。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"This young industry has grown with amazing speed and has quietly changed the way we live.","note":"amazing speed 总评发展；quietly（悄悄地）一个词写出影响之深。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The development of express delivery is easy to see.","note":"主体段先讲 development（题目第一问），后讲 impact——顺序跟着题目走。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Ten years ago, a package might take a week to cross the country; today, orders placed in the morning often arrive the next day, and fresh food can be delivered within hours.","note":"a week → the next day → within hours 三级时间递进，把「快」写到极致——今昔对比的加强版。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Behind this speed are huge networks of warehouses, trucks, planes and millions of couriers, supported by smart technology that tracks every package.","note":"倒装句 Behind this speed are…；warehouses（仓库）、couriers（快递员）都是行业准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The impact on our lives is deep.","note":"短句转入题目第二问 impact，分段清楚。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Online shopping has become part of daily life, farmers and small businesses can sell their products to the whole country, and people in small towns enjoy the same goods as those in big cities.","note":"三个影响并列：购物日常化、小生意卖全国、小城镇同享商品——最后一层最有高度。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, express delivery is more than a service; it is a bridge connecting producers and consumers across China.","note":"bridge 比喻收尾：连接 producers（生产者）和 consumers（消费者）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"It will keep making our lives faster and richer.","note":"keep making（持续让）+ faster and richer 展望收尾。","tag":"好词"}],"essay":["In response to the business school's survey, I would like to share my views on the express delivery service industry in China. This young industry has grown with amazing speed and has quietly changed the way we live.","The development of express delivery is easy to see. Ten years ago, a package might take a week to cross the country; today, orders placed in the morning often arrive the next day, and fresh food can be delivered within hours. Behind this speed are huge networks of warehouses, trucks, planes and millions of couriers, supported by smart technology that tracks every package. The impact on our lives is deep. Online shopping has become part of daily life, farmers and small businesses can sell their products to the whole country, and people in small towns enjoy the same goods as those in big cities.","In my view, express delivery is more than a service; it is a bridge connecting producers and consumers across China. It will keep making our lives faster and richer."],"id":"soc-r13","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"Suppose the business school of your university is conducting a survey to collect students' opinions on the express delivery service industry in China. You are to write a response about its recent development and its impact on people's lives. You will have 30 minutes to write the essay. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2024年12月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"中国快递业的发展与影响（调查回复）","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2024},{"analysis":[{"en":"Our university is organizing a forum on the development of students' cross-cultural communication abilities.","note":"复述论坛背景开场，cross-cultural（跨文化的）是本题题眼词，全篇要反复用准。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my view, this ability is becoming more and more important, and universities should help students develop it on purpose.","note":"表态分两半：能力越来越重要 + 学校应有意识地培养（on purpose 有意地）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Cross-cultural communication means talking and working with people from different cultures without misunderstandings.","note":"先下定义再论证：means…（指的是）是论坛发言显条理的写法。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It is important because our future work will surely connect us with the world: foreign companies, international projects and online partners from other countries.","note":"冒号后三个未来工作场景并列，把重要性落到就业上。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"To develop this ability, students first need language skills, especially spoken English.","note":"转入「怎么培养」：先语言，first 领起。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"More importantly, we need an open mind.","note":"More importantly 递进：比语言更重要的是 an open mind（开放的心态）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Learning about other cultures' customs, values and ways of thinking helps us respect differences instead of judging them.","note":"customs、values（风俗、价值观）是文化话题的核心名词；respect / judge 对比。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Universities can help by offering culture courses, inviting foreign teachers and students, and encouraging exchange programmes.","note":"三个 by doing 并列写学校的做法；exchange programmes（交换项目）准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, cross-cultural communication ability is a key that opens the world.","note":"a key that opens the world（打开世界的钥匙）比喻收尾。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Students who develop it early will walk further on the road ahead.","note":"walk further（走得更远）展望式结尾，呼应论坛主题。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Our university is organizing a forum on the development of students' cross-cultural communication abilities. In my view, this ability is becoming more and more important, and universities should help students develop it on purpose.","Cross-cultural communication means talking and working with people from different cultures without misunderstandings. It is important because our future work will surely connect us with the world: foreign companies, international projects and online partners from other countries. To develop this ability, students first need language skills, especially spoken English. More importantly, we need an open mind. Learning about other cultures' customs, values and ways of thinking helps us respect differences instead of judging them. Universities can help by offering culture courses, inviting foreign teachers and students, and encouraging exchange programmes.","In conclusion, cross-cultural communication ability is a key that opens the world. Students who develop it early will walk further on the road ahead."],"id":"cul-r9","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"Suppose your university is organizing a forum on the development of students' cross-cultural communication abilities. You are now to write an essay to express your view. You will have 30 minutes to write the essay. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2025年6月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"培养跨文化沟通能力（论坛发言）","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2025},{"analysis":[{"en":"Recently, our university has been seeking students' opinions on whether College Chinese should be made a compulsory course.","note":"第一句复述题目背景（学校在征求意见），whether 从句把问题原样带出。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my view, it should.","note":"短句表态干脆：it should（应该设）——观点题先亮明立场。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Chinese is not only our mother tongue; it is also the basis of all other learning.","note":"mother tongue（母语）+ basis（基础），分号连接两个定位。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"First, good Chinese ability helps students in every subject.","note":"First / Second 两个理由分层：先实用，再文化。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Reports, papers and even science answers all need clear and correct expression, yet many college students write with mistakes and poor logic because they stopped learning Chinese after high school.","note":"三个写作场景并列；yet 转出问题（错字、逻辑差），because 给原因，论证完整。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Second, College Chinese carries our culture.","note":"carry our culture（承载我们的文化），carry 用得比 have 高级。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Through classical poems and fine essays, students can understand Chinese history and values more deeply, which no foreign language course can replace.","note":"classical poems（古典诗词）具体化文化内容；which…can replace 反衬不可替代。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Some students worry that the course will add to their burden, but one course a week is a small price for a lifelong skill.","note":"先让步对方顾虑（add to their burden 增加负担），再用 a small price 反驳——观点题加分手法。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In conclusion, making College Chinese a compulsory course is necessary and worthwhile.","note":"动名词短语作主语回扣题目原词 compulsory course，necessary 回应题目的 necessity。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It will benefit students in both study and life.","note":"benefit sb（使某人受益）收尾简洁。","tag":"好词"}],"essay":["Recently, our university has been seeking students' opinions on whether College Chinese should be made a compulsory course. In my view, it should. Chinese is not only our mother tongue; it is also the basis of all other learning.","First, good Chinese ability helps students in every subject. Reports, papers and even science answers all need clear and correct expression, yet many college students write with mistakes and poor logic because they stopped learning Chinese after high school. Second, College Chinese carries our culture. Through classical poems and fine essays, students can understand Chinese history and values more deeply, which no foreign language course can replace. Some students worry that the course will add to their burden, but one course a week is a small price for a lifelong skill.","In conclusion, making College Chinese a compulsory course is necessary and worthwhile. It will benefit students in both study and life."],"id":"edu-r14","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"Suppose your university is seeking students' opinions on the necessity of making College Chinese a compulsory course. You are now to write an essay to express your view. You will have 30 minutes to write the essay. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2025年6月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"大学语文应设为必修课吗","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2025},{"analysis":[{"en":"Our university is conducting a survey on the appropriate use of AI technology in assisting learning.","note":"第一句复述题目背景，appropriate、assisting learning 两个题面词都带上。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my view, AI can be a powerful helper for students, but only when it is used appropriately.","note":"表态带条件：powerful helper（强有力的帮手）+ only when…——立场有分寸。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Used well, AI helps learning in many ways.","note":"Used well 分词短句领起好处段，和结尾的 appropriate 呼应。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It answers questions at any hour, explains difficult points in simple words and gives students practice that fits their own level.","note":"三个动词并列列 AI 的好处；at any hour（任何时间）、fits their own level（合个人水平）写得具体。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"For a shy student, asking AI is easier than asking in class, so more questions get answered.","note":"换一个角度举例：对害羞的学生，问 AI 更敢开口——好处写出了新意。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"However, AI can also harm learning if students depend on it too much.","note":"However 转入坏处，depend on it too much 点出病根。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Some copy AI's answers into their homework without thinking, and slowly lose the ability to solve problems on their own.","note":"copy…without thinking 把「抄答案」写具体；on their own（靠自己）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"AI can also make mistakes, so its answers must be checked, not blindly trusted.","note":"also 补第二个坏处；blindly trusted（盲目相信）和 check 对比。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, the key word is “appropriate”.","note":"结尾把题目原词 appropriate 拎出来当钥匙，回扣感强。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Students should let AI explain, question and check, but always do the core thinking themselves.","note":"explain、question、check 三个动词划清 AI 该干的活；core thinking（核心思考）必须自己做。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Our university is conducting a survey on the appropriate use of AI technology in assisting learning. In my view, AI can be a powerful helper for students, but only when it is used appropriately.","Used well, AI helps learning in many ways. It answers questions at any hour, explains difficult points in simple words and gives students practice that fits their own level. For a shy student, asking AI is easier than asking in class, so more questions get answered. However, AI can also harm learning if students depend on it too much. Some copy AI's answers into their homework without thinking, and slowly lose the ability to solve problems on their own. AI can also make mistakes, so its answers must be checked, not blindly trusted.","In conclusion, the key word is “appropriate”. Students should let AI explain, question and check, but always do the core thinking themselves."],"id":"tech-r10","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"Suppose your university is conducting a survey to collect students' opinions on the appropriate use of AI technology in assisting learning. You are now to write an essay to express your view. You will have 30 minutes to write the essay. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2025年6月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"恰当使用 AI 辅助学习（调查回复）","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2025},{"analysis":[{"en":"The student union is collecting opinions on improving its work for the coming year.","note":"复述背景开场：学生会在征集意见——回应文的场合先交代清。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"As an ordinary student, I would like to suggest that it focus on one goal: better enriching student life.","note":"As an ordinary student（作为一名普通学生）亮明身份；focus on one goal 把建议收成一个中心：enrich student life 用题目原词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"To enrich student life, the union can work in three directions.","note":"总起预告三条建议：办活动、先倾听、做小事。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, organize activities that students truly need, not only big shows.","note":"第一条先立标准：truly need（真正需要）↔ big shows（大场面），批评形式主义。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Study-sharing meetings before exams, sports games between dormitories and small interest clubs will attract more students than formal ceremonies.","note":"三个具体活动例子并列；attract more students than（比……更能吸引学生）比较收束。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, listen before acting.","note":"第二条用短句口号式表达：先听再做——好记又有态度。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The union should collect opinions through online surveys regularly and tell students what has been done with their suggestions, so that we feel our voices matter.","note":"展开第二条：regularly（定期）征集 + 反馈结果；our voices matter（我们的声音算数）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Third, serve daily life in small ways: a lost-and-found platform, umbrella sharing on rainy days and a guide for new students are small services that everyone will remember.","note":"第三条最具体：lost-and-found（失物招领）、雨伞共享、新生指南——小事最见服务心。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In short, a good student union is not measured by how many activities it holds, but by how much richer it makes students' days.","note":"not measured by…but by…（不看……而看……）给好学生会下定义，结尾立意。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I hope our union will keep moving in this direction.","note":"展望式收尾，语气积极得体。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["The student union is collecting opinions on improving its work for the coming year. As an ordinary student, I would like to suggest that it focus on one goal: better enriching student life.","To enrich student life, the union can work in three directions. First, organize activities that students truly need, not only big shows. Study-sharing meetings before exams, sports games between dormitories and small interest clubs will attract more students than formal ceremonies. Second, listen before acting. The union should collect opinions through online surveys regularly and tell students what has been done with their suggestions, so that we feel our voices matter. Third, serve daily life in small ways: a lost-and-found platform, umbrella sharing on rainy days and a guide for new students are small services that everyone will remember.","In short, a good student union is not measured by how many activities it holds, but by how much richer it makes students' days. I hope our union will keep moving in this direction."],"id":"cam-r21","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"Suppose the student union of your university is collecting opinions on improving its work for the coming year. You are now to write a response by suggesting how it can better enrich student life. You will have 30 minutes to write the essay. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2025年12月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"学生会如何改进工作（意见回复）","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2025},{"analysis":[{"en":"Our university is organizing a forum on how students can make the best use of on-campus resources for academic development.","note":"复述论坛主题开场，make the best use of（充分利用）是本题题眼词组，全篇反复用。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my view, our campus is richer than most students realize; the problem is that many of us use only a small part of it.","note":"先立论：资源不缺，缺的是用——分号后半句点出问题所在。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The library is the first resource we should use well.","note":"三类资源分层：图书馆、老师、人——每层一句总起。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Beyond borrowing books, it offers databases, study rooms and lectures that many students never try.","note":"Beyond borrowing books（不止借书）；databases（数据库）点出多数人没用过的资源。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Teachers are the second resource.","note":"短句换层：老师也是资源——视角新颖。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Office hours and emails are open to us, yet many students are too shy to ask questions until the exam week.","note":"office hours（答疑时间）是大学准词；too shy to（害羞得不敢）+ until the exam week 写出拖延的真实。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The third resource is people: senior students, classmates and academic clubs can share experience and materials that save us much time.","note":"第三层是人脉资源；share experience and materials（分享经验和资料）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"To make the best use of these resources, we should explore the campus actively in the first term, make a simple plan each term, and turn using resources into a habit.","note":"三层讲完后集中给方法：早探索、做计划、成习惯——回扣题眼词组收束本段。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In conclusion, resources do not help those who ignore them.","note":"结尾短句立论：ignore them（不用它们）资源再多也白搭。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Students who learn to use the campus fully will gain far more from the same four years.","note":"the same four years（同样的四年）对比收尾：差距不在学校，在用法。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Our university is organizing a forum on how students can make the best use of on-campus resources for academic development. In my view, our campus is richer than most students realize; the problem is that many of us use only a small part of it.","The library is the first resource we should use well. Beyond borrowing books, it offers databases, study rooms and lectures that many students never try. Teachers are the second resource. Office hours and emails are open to us, yet many students are too shy to ask questions until the exam week. The third resource is people: senior students, classmates and academic clubs can share experience and materials that save us much time. To make the best use of these resources, we should explore the campus actively in the first term, make a simple plan each term, and turn using resources into a habit.","In conclusion, resources do not help those who ignore them. Students who learn to use the campus fully will gain far more from the same four years."],"id":"cam-r22","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"Suppose your university is organizing a forum on how students can make the best use of on-campus resources for academic development. You are now to write an essay to express your view. You will have 30 minutes to write the essay. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2025年12月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"充分利用校内资源（论坛发言）","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2025},{"analysis":[{"en":"It is proposed that all university students should be required to learn academic writing.","note":"第一句原样复述题目的提议——回应提议类作文的标准开场。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I support this proposal, because academic writing is a basic skill that every student needs, whatever major they are in.","note":"support 表态 + because 给总理由；whatever major（无论什么专业）回应题目里的 all。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, students have to write a lot at university: course papers, lab reports and finally a graduation thesis.","note":"冒号列出三类写作：course papers、lab reports、graduation thesis（毕业论文），全是准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Without training, many of them write in a disorganized way, mixing opinions with facts and forgetting to give sources.","note":"disorganized（条理混乱）；mix opinions with facts、give sources（注明出处）点出没受训练的典型毛病。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"A course in academic writing teaches them how to build an argument, use evidence and respect the work of others.","note":"build an argument（构建论证）、evidence（证据）——学术写作的三个核心动作。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, this skill remains useful after graduation.","note":"第二个理由从校内延伸到毕业后，视野打开。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Clear reports and proposals are needed in almost every job, and people who write well are more likely to be trusted with important tasks.","note":"be trusted with（被托付）写出写得好带来的职场回报。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, requiring academic writing is not an extra burden but a necessary preparation.","note":"not…but… 回应可能的反对声（怕增加负担），收尾先破后立。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Universities should offer the course with training that fits different majors.","note":"最后一句给落地建议：按专业区别训练，不一刀切。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["It is proposed that all university students should be required to learn academic writing. I support this proposal, because academic writing is a basic skill that every student needs, whatever major they are in.","First, students have to write a lot at university: course papers, lab reports and finally a graduation thesis. Without training, many of them write in a disorganized way, mixing opinions with facts and forgetting to give sources. A course in academic writing teaches them how to build an argument, use evidence and respect the work of others. Second, this skill remains useful after graduation. Clear reports and proposals are needed in almost every job, and people who write well are more likely to be trusted with important tasks.","In short, requiring academic writing is not an extra burden but a necessary preparation. Universities should offer the course with training that fits different majors."],"id":"edu-r15","kind":"real","month":12,"prompt":"Suppose it is proposed that all university students should be required to learn academic writing. You are now to write a response by stating what you think of the proposal. You will have 30 minutes to write the essay. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2025年12月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"所有学生都该学学术写作吗","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2025},{"analysis":[{"en":"I am writing to put forward a proposal to the university on how to make students' campus life easier.","note":"第一句点明文体和目的：put forward a proposal（提出提案）用题目原词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Students spend most of their time on campus, and small inconveniences, repeated every day, become big troubles.","note":"给提案找理由：small inconveniences（小不便）天天重复就成 big troubles——提案的必要性。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Here are my suggestions.","note":"短句预告建议段。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, build one online platform for daily services.","note":"三条建议用祈使句领起：一个平台、改善宿舍、信息透明——提案的建议要干脆可执行。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"At present, students must use different apps and offices to book a sports field, repair a dormitory light, borrow equipment or check a lost item.","note":"四个办事场景并列写「跑断腿」的现状：订场、报修、借器材、找失物。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"If all these services were in one place, much time would be saved.","note":"虚拟语气 If…were… 描绘整合后的效果，提案的说服手法。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Second, improve life in the dormitories: add more washing machines and hot-water hours, and make the repair service faster.","note":"第二条落到宿舍：washing machines、hot-water hours（热水时段）全是学生最有感的细节。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Third, make information clearer.","note":"第三条最短，先给总要求再展开。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A single campus map and calendar showing canteen menus, library seats and activity notices would help every student, especially freshmen, every day.","note":"一张地图日历整合三类信息（菜单、座位、通知）；especially freshmen 点出受益最大的人群。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"None of these changes is expensive, but together they would remove many small stones from students' daily road.","note":"先打消成本顾虑（None…is expensive），再用 small stones（小石子）比喻收尾：搬走日常路上的小石子。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I hope the university will consider them.","note":"礼貌收束，提案的标准结尾。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["I am writing to put forward a proposal to the university on how to make students' campus life easier. Students spend most of their time on campus, and small inconveniences, repeated every day, become big troubles. Here are my suggestions.","First, build one online platform for daily services. At present, students must use different apps and offices to book a sports field, repair a dormitory light, borrow equipment or check a lost item. If all these services were in one place, much time would be saved. Second, improve life in the dormitories: add more washing machines and hot-water hours, and make the repair service faster. Third, make information clearer. A single campus map and calendar showing canteen menus, library seats and activity notices would help every student, especially freshmen, every day.","None of these changes is expensive, but together they would remove many small stones from students' daily road. I hope the university will consider them."],"id":"cam-r23","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"Suppose you are invited to put forward a proposal to the university on how to make students' campus life easier. You are now to write an essay to make your proposal. You will have 30 minutes to write the essay. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第2套","source":"真题 · 2026年6月 · 第2套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"提案：让校园生活更便利","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2026},{"analysis":[{"en":"It is proposed that university students should be required to take part in at least one research project.","note":"复述提议开场；take part in 是 participate 的同义说法，换词避免照抄。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my opinion, this proposal is both necessary and practical, and I support it.","note":"表态句直接用上题目给的两个评价维度：necessary + practical——题目给什么词就用什么词搭框架。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The proposal is necessary because research trains abilities that classes alone cannot.","note":"主体段第一部分只讲 necessity，和表态句的顺序一一对应。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In a project, students learn to ask questions, search for information, design steps and solve real problems, instead of only memorizing knowledge for exams.","note":"四个动词并列写科研训练的动作；instead of 和死记硬背对比。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"These abilities are exactly what future employers value.","note":"exactly what…（正是……）把话题接到就业，论证落地。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The proposal is also practical.","note":"短句转入第二个维度 practical，段落内部再分层。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Universities already have teachers, labs and libraries, and many projects can be small and low-cost, such as surveys and data analysis.","note":"讲可行性要给证据：现有资源 + 低成本例子（surveys、data analysis)。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"With teachers' guidance, even first-year students can finish a simple project in one term.","note":"even first-year students（连大一学生都能）——用最弱的情况证明可行。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In conclusion, requiring one research project is a wise step.","note":"结尾重申支持，wise step（明智之举）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It will help students turn what they learn in class into real ability.","note":"turn…into…（把……变成……）收尾：把课堂知识变成真本事。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["It is proposed that university students should be required to take part in at least one research project. In my opinion, this proposal is both necessary and practical, and I support it.","The proposal is necessary because research trains abilities that classes alone cannot. In a project, students learn to ask questions, search for information, design steps and solve real problems, instead of only memorizing knowledge for exams. These abilities are exactly what future employers value. The proposal is also practical. Universities already have teachers, labs and libraries, and many projects can be small and low-cost, such as surveys and data analysis. With teachers' guidance, even first-year students can finish a simple project in one term.","In conclusion, requiring one research project is a wise step. It will help students turn what they learn in class into real ability."],"id":"edu-r16","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"Suppose it is proposed that university students should be required to participate in at least one research project. You are now to write a response by stating what you think of the proposal in terms of its necessity and practicality. You will have 30 minutes to write the response. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第3套","source":"真题 · 2026年6月 · 第3套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"学生必须参加科研项目吗","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2026},{"analysis":[{"en":"Robots are no longer only in factories and films.","note":"no longer only（不再只在）开场：机器人正走出工厂和电影，入题快。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In the near future, they may become a common sight on our campus, helping students and teachers in many ways.","note":"a common sight（常见景象）+ in the near future，把话题落到校园。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"I would like to share my ideas about their future applications here.","note":"投稿文的口吻：share my ideas…here 点明这是校报投稿，future applications 用题目原词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, robots can serve in the library.","note":"First / Second / Third 三个应用场景分层：图书馆、安全清洁、学习本身。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"They can guide students to the right shelves, carry heavy books and keep the library open at night when human staff are off work.","note":"三个动作写图书馆机器人的活；off work（下班）点出夜间值守的优势。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, robots can help with campus safety and cleaning.","note":"第二个场景换到安全与清洁，help with（帮忙处理）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Patrol robots can watch the campus around the clock, while cleaning robots keep classrooms and roads tidy.","note":"patrol（巡逻）、around the clock（全天候）都是准词；while 并列两类机器人。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Third, robots can support learning itself.","note":"第三个场景升到学习本身，itself 强调「不只是干杂活」。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In labs, robot assistants can prepare materials and remind students of safety rules; in language classes, robot partners can practise conversation with shy students at any time.","note":"分号并列实验室和语言课两个场景；remind sb of（提醒）用法准。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Of course, robots should assist people, not replace them.","note":"结尾先立界限：assist / replace——机器人题的万能落点。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"If we use them wisely, our campus will become smarter, safer and more convenient for everyone.","note":"三个比较级并列收尾展望：更智能、更安全、更方便。","tag":"好词"}],"essay":["Robots are no longer only in factories and films. In the near future, they may become a common sight on our campus, helping students and teachers in many ways. I would like to share my ideas about their future applications here.","First, robots can serve in the library. They can guide students to the right shelves, carry heavy books and keep the library open at night when human staff are off work. Second, robots can help with campus safety and cleaning. Patrol robots can watch the campus around the clock, while cleaning robots keep classrooms and roads tidy. Third, robots can support learning itself. In labs, robot assistants can prepare materials and remind students of safety rules; in language classes, robot partners can practise conversation with shy students at any time.","Of course, robots should assist people, not replace them. If we use them wisely, our campus will become smarter, safer and more convenient for everyone."],"id":"tech-r11","kind":"real","month":6,"prompt":"Suppose the university newspaper is inviting submissions from the students for its coming edition on future applications of robots on campus. You are now to write an essay for submission. You will have 30 minutes to write the essay. You should write at least 120 words but no more than 180 words.","set":"第1套","source":"真题 · 2026年6月 · 第1套","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"机器人在校园的未来应用（校报投稿）","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词","year":2026}];
